window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD && window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD("0007", [{"word":"cause","ipa_uk":"/kɔːz/","ipa_us":"/kɔːz/","definition_zh":"原因；起因；事业；理由；造成，引起","definition_en":"the reason or source of an effect, or to make something happen","core_image":"推倒第一张多米诺骨牌的那一下——后面所有的动作都由它带出来","scene":"消防员蹲在烧焦的墙边，对住户说：The cause of the fire was a faulty wire.","sceneCN":"这里 cause 是「起因、根源」（第 2 个义项：造成结果的那个源头）；句意：这场火灾的起因是一根故障电线。图中可辨识物件：烧焦的墙、消防员、配电箱。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"原因；起因；理由；事业"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"造成；引起；使发生"},{"tag":"conj.","zh":"（口语）因为（'cause，because 的缩略）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"the cause of","zh":"……的原因"},{"phrase":"cause damage","zh":"造成损害"},{"phrase":"cause somebody to do something","zh":"使某人做某事"},{"phrase":"a good cause","zh":"一项正当的事业"},{"phrase":"have cause to do","zh":"有理由做……"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单","form":"causes"},{"label":"过去式","form":"caused"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"caused"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"causing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"causal","pos":"adj.","zh":"因果的；原因的"},{"word":"causation","pos":"n.","zh":"因果作用；起因"},{"word":"causative","pos":"adj.","zh":"使役的；原因的"},{"word":"causeless","pos":"adj.","zh":"无原因的"},{"word":"because","pos":"conj.","zh":"因为（由 by + cause 凝固而成）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Ground for a decision: the reason behind it","titleCN":"缘由：做出决定背后的理由","definition":"the reason or motive that explains why someone acts or decides","definitionCN":"解释某人为何行动或作出决定的理由、动机","example":"There is no cause for alarm; the test results are normal.","exampleCN":"没有理由惊慌，检查结果是正常的。","why":"The earliest English sense was 'reason or motive for a decision, grounds for action'. The word began as the ground a person stands on when asked why, not yet as a physical force.","whyCN":"英语中最早的义项是“作出决定的理由、行动的根据”。它最初指被问“为什么”时一个人站得住的那块“地面”，还不是物理上的力。"},{"no":"02","title":"Source of an effect: what makes the result happen","titleCN":"根源：让结果发生的那个源头","definition":"the thing, event, or person that produces a particular result","definitionCN":"产生某种结果的事物、事件或人","example":"Investigators are still looking for the cause of the explosion.","exampleCN":"调查人员仍在寻找爆炸的起因。","why":"From the mid-14c. the word was used for 'cause of an effect; source, origin'. The reason you can name became the thing out in the world that produces the result.","whyCN":"从 14 世纪中期起，这个词被用来指“结果的起因、来源”。原本只是你口头能说出的“理由”，这时变成了世界当中真正产生结果的那个东西。"},{"no":"03","title":"Cause as a verb: bring an effect into being","titleCN":"造成：把结果带出来","definition":"to make something happen, especially something bad","definitionCN":"使某事发生，尤指不好的事","example":"Heavy rain caused flooding across the valley.","exampleCN":"大雨造成整个山谷洪水泛滥。","why":"The verb is recorded from the late 14c. with the sense 'produce an effect'. Once a cause is identified as a source, it is a short step to saying that the source acts: it causes.","whyCN":"动词义记录于 14 世纪后期，意为“产生结果”。一旦“原因”被认作源头，再说这个源头在起作用、在“造成”结果，就只差一步。"},{"no":"04","title":"The side you take: a cause to defend","titleCN":"事业：你选择站队去捍卫的事","definition":"a principle, aim, or movement that people support and fight for","definitionCN":"人们支持并为之奋斗的原则、目标或运动","example":"She has devoted her life to the cause of equal education.","exampleCN":"她毕生投入于教育平等的事业。","why":"Latin causa also meant 'lawsuit, judicial process'. From c. 1300 English used cause for 'a side taken in controversy', so the legal case turned into the public cause one defends.","whyCN":"拉丁语 causa 也有“诉讼、司法程序”之意。英语从约 1300 年起用 cause 指“争论中所站的一边”，于是法庭上的“案子”变成公共生活中要捍卫的“事业”。"},{"no":"05","title":"Justification: a reason good enough to act","titleCN":"正当理由：足以支撑行动的根据","definition":"a reason that justifies an action or a complaint","definitionCN":"为某一行动或抱怨提供正当性的理由","example":"You have no cause to complain about the service.","exampleCN":"你没有理由抱怨这项服务。","why":"Late 14c. records 'proper or adequate reason, justification for an action'. A cause in court had to be sufficient; outside court the word keeps that sense of a reason strong enough to stand on.","whyCN":"14 世纪后期记录了“适当或充分的理由、行动的正当依据”。法庭上的诉因必须站得住；法庭之外，这个词仍保留“足以立身的理由”这一层。"},{"no":"06","title":"Medical cause: the agent behind an illness","titleCN":"病因：疾病背后的致病因素","definition":"the disease, organism, or condition that produces a medical symptom","definitionCN":"引起医学症状的疾病、病原体或状况","example":"Doctors still do not know the cause of her headaches.","exampleCN":"医生仍不知道她头痛的病因。","why":"Medicine narrowed the general 'source of an effect' to the agent that produces symptoms. The cause is what a doctor looks for before treating the effect.","whyCN":"医学把泛指的“结果来源”缩小为产生症状的那个因素。医生在治“果”之前，先要找的就是这个“因”。"},{"no":"07","title":"Legal cause: a case or a ground for action","titleCN":"诉因：案件或提起诉讼的根据","definition":"in law, a case or the legally recognized ground on which an action is brought","definitionCN":"法律上指案件，或提起诉讼所依据的法定理由","example":"The lawyer argued that the plaintiff had no cause of action.","exampleCN":"律师辩称原告没有诉因。","why":"Causa in Latin covered 'judicial process, lawsuit', and law kept that old sense. Everyday English moved to 'reason', but the courtroom preserved cause as the case itself.","whyCN":"拉丁语 causa 包含“司法程序、诉讼”的意思，法律保留了这一古义。日常英语转向“理由”，法庭却把 cause 保存为“案件本身”。"},{"no":"08","title":"Cause in logic: one term in a causal chain","titleCN":"逻辑上的因：因果链条中的前项","definition":"the event or condition that is followed necessarily by an effect, in the pair cause and effect","definitionCN":"在“因与果”这一对概念中，必然引出结果的事件或条件","example":"Every effect must have a cause, the philosopher insisted.","exampleCN":"这位哲学家坚持认为，每个结果都必有一个原因。","why":"Philosophy took the everyday word and made it a technical term: cause and effect name the two ends of one chain. The cause is the earlier link that hands its force to the next.","whyCN":"哲学把这个日常词变成了术语：“因”与“果”命名同一条链的两端。因是较早的一环，把自己的力交给下一环。"},{"no":"09","title":"'Cause: because, clipped to one syllable","titleCN":"口语连词：'cause，because 的缩略","definition":"in informal speech, a shortened form of because, meaning for the reason that","definitionCN":"口语中 because 的缩略形式，表示“因为”","example":"I stayed home 'cause the roads were icy.","exampleCN":"我待在家里，因为路面上结了冰。","why":"Because began as the phrase by cause, literally 'for the reason that'. Speech clipped the first syllable, leaving 'cause, which still carries the old idea of a reason.","whyCN":"because 原本是短语 by cause，字面意思就是“由于这个原因”。口语把前面的音节剪掉，只剩下 'cause，里面仍装着“理由”这个古老的意思。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Cause comes from Latin causa, a word whose own origin is unknown. It entered English through Old French around 1200 and spread from 'reason' to 'source', 'lawsuit', and 'the side one defends'.","cn":"cause 来自拉丁语 causa，而 causa 本身的来源不明。它约 1200 年经古法语进入英语，从“理由”扩展到“来源”“诉讼”和“所捍卫的一方”。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (before 1C BC)","en":"Causa meant 'a cause, a reason; interest; judicial process, lawsuit'. Etymologists record its deeper origin as unknown, so the earliest step is source uncertain and no root should be invented for it.","cn":"causa 意为“原因、理由；利益；司法程序、诉讼”。词源学家记载其更深来源不明，因此最深层只能标为“来源不确定”，不应为它编造词根。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (12c.)","en":"Old French cause meant 'cause, reason; lawsuit, case in law' and passed the legal and everyday senses together into English.","cn":"古法语 cause 意为“原因、理由；诉讼、法律案件”，把法律义和日常义一并传入英语。"},{"era":"c. 1200 ENGLISH","en":"The first English records give 'reason or motive for a decision, grounds for action'. By c. 1300 the word also meant 'a side taken in controversy'.","cn":"英语最早的记录是“作出决定的理由、行动的根据”。到约 1300 年，这个词也指“争论中所站的一边”。"},{"era":"MID-14c ENGLISH","en":"From mid-14c. cause meant 'cause of an effect; source, origin'; late 14c. added 'reason for something taking place' and the verb 'produce an effect'.","cn":"从 14 世纪中期起，cause 指“结果的起因、来源”；14 世纪后期又添“事情发生的理由”以及动词“产生结果”。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Because came from the phrase by cause, and its clipped form 'cause is written by the mid-15c. Modern English keeps cause for reasons, sources, causes we support, and legal grounds.","cn":"because 来自短语 by cause，其缩略形式 'cause 在 15 世纪中期已见于书面。现代英语用 cause 表示理由、来源、所支持的事业和法律根据。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"course","ipa":"/kɔːs/","tag":"near sound","definition":"a direction, a route, or a set of lessons. It differs from cause by one letter and ends in /s/, not /z/.","definitionCN":"路线；课程。与 cause 只差一个字母，结尾读 /s/，不是 /z/。"},{"word":"coarse","ipa":"/kɔːs/","tag":"same sound as course","definition":"rough in texture or rude in manner. It is a homophone of course and is often confused with cause in writing.","definitionCN":"粗糙的；粗鲁的。与 course 同音，书写时常与 cause 混淆。"},{"word":"clause","ipa":"/klɔːz/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"a part of a sentence or a section of a legal document. It shares the -ause ending but begins with cl-.","definitionCN":"从句；条款。同样以 -ause 结尾，但开头是 cl-。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"reason","ipa":"/ˈriːzn/","tag":"motive","definition":"the explanation or justification for an action. It matches cause in the 'ground for a decision' sense.","definitionCN":"理由；原因。对应 cause 表“行动根据”的义项。"},{"word":"motive","ipa":"/ˈməʊtɪv/","tag":"inner drive","definition":"the inner need or desire that pushes a person to act. It is more personal than cause.","definitionCN":"动机。指推动人行动的内在需要或欲望，比 cause 更偏个人。"},{"word":"source","ipa":"/sɔːs/","tag":"origin","definition":"the place or thing from which something comes. It matches the 'source of an effect' sense.","definitionCN":"来源；源头。对应 cause 表“结果来源”的义项。"},{"word":"origin","ipa":"/ˈɒrɪdʒɪn/","tag":"beginning","definition":"the point where something begins or is produced. It stresses the starting point rather than the producing force.","definitionCN":"起源。强调起点，而不是产生结果的力量。"},{"word":"trigger","ipa":"/ˈtrɪɡə(r)/","tag":"immediate cause","definition":"the small event that sets a larger process going. It is the last push rather than the whole cause.","definitionCN":"触发因素。指引发更大过程的小事件，是最后那一推，而不是完整的原因。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: the Latin causa family, the legal sense that survives in cause of action, and the phrase by cause behind because.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 causa 词族、仍活在 cause of action 里的法律义，以及 because 背后的短语 by cause。"},"normal":[{"en":"because = by + cause: the word literally says 'by the reason that'. The cause is the reason standing behind the clause.","cn":"because = by + cause：字面就是“由于那个理由”。cause 就是从句背后站着的那个理由。"},{"en":"accuse comes from ad causa, 'to bring a charge against'. A charge names a cause in court.","cn":"accuse 来自 ad causa“就某案由提出指控”。指控就是把法庭上的一个案由点出来。"},{"en":"cause of action is a legal phrase: the ground that lets a case proceed. It shows the old lawsuit sense still alive.","cn":"cause of action 是个法律短语：让案件得以进行的根据。它说明古老的诉讼义仍活着。"},{"en":"a good cause is a side you take, not a thing you make. The word kept the c. 1300 sense of a side in controversy.","cn":"a good cause 是你站的一边，不是弄出来的东西。这个词保留了约 1300 年“争论中的一方”的义项。"},{"en":"cause and effect is one chain with two ends: the cause hands its force to the effect.","cn":"cause and effect 是一条链的两端：因把自己的力交给果。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Cause is the answer to a why-question: point at the ground, then at the thing standing on it.","cn":"cause 是对“为什么”的回答：先指向那块地面，再指向站在上面的东西。"},{"en":"The word moves from the reason in the mind to the source in the world, then to the act of producing, and finally to the side people defend.","cn":"这个词从心里的理由，走到世界中的源头，再走到产生结果的动作，最后走到人们捍卫的一方。"},{"en":"So reason, source, make, cause, and lawsuit are one notion seen from five positions in the same chain.","cn":"所以“理由、源头、造成、事业、诉讼”是同一个概念在同一条链上五个不同位置的样子。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The cause of the crash is still under investigation.","cn":"撞车事故的原因仍在调查中。"},{"en":"Poor sanitation can cause serious disease.","cn":"卫生条件差会引发严重疾病。"},{"en":"She donated the prize money to a local cause.","cn":"她把奖金捐给了一项本地公益事业。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“靠子”——万事都靠一个“由头”起头，这个由头就是 cause 原因、造成","word":"cause"},"root":"源自拉丁语 causa“原因、理由、诉讼”，该词本身来源不明；经古法语 cause 于约 1200 年进入英语，核心是“可指认的由头”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of cause, from the reason in a decision to the side people defend. Each step moves the same 'ground' outward: mind, world, action, law, logic, speech.","cn":"cause 的九个义项，从决定背后的理由一直到人们捍卫的事业。每一步都让同一块“根据”往外挪：心里、世界、行动、法庭、逻辑、口语。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a first push that hands its force down a chain.","cn":"核心意象：第一推，把自己的力沿链条传下去。"},"chain":["ASK WHY","NAME A GROUND","FIND THE SOURCE","PRODUCE THE EFFECT","TAKE A SIDE","LINK CAUSE TO EFFECT"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S5","en":"A REASON ONE CAN STAND ON: a motive for a decision and a justification strong enough to defend.","cn":"站得住的理由：决定的动机，与足以辩护的正当根据。"},{"senses":"S2 · S6","en":"A SOURCE IN THE WORLD: the origin of an effect, narrowed in medicine to the agent of a disease.","cn":"世界中的源头：结果的来源，在医学里缩小为致病因素。"},{"senses":"S3 · S8","en":"THE CHAIN IN ACTION: the verb produces an effect, and logic names the two ends cause and effect.","cn":"链条在运作：动词义产生结果，逻辑义则命名因与果两端。"},{"senses":"S4 · S7","en":"THE LEGAL SIDE: a side taken in controversy grows out of the lawsuit, and law keeps cause as the case itself.","cn":"法律的一面：争论中站的一边由诉讼义长出来，法律则把 cause 保留为案件本身。"},{"senses":"S9","en":"THE CLIPPED FORM: because began as by cause, and speech cut it down to 'cause.","cn":"被剪短的形式：because 原本是 by cause，口语把它削成了 'cause。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Cause is a Latin loan whose family is built on the bare stem caus-: -al, -ation, -ative, -less, and the prefixed forms accuse, excuse and recuse.","cn":"cause 是拉丁借词，其词族建立在光秃的词干 caus- 上：-al、-ation、-ative、-less，以及带前缀的 accuse、excuse、recuse。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin causa 'cause, reason, lawsuit' is the base of causalis, causatio and causari; the same noun sits inside accusare and excusare, where it means the charge in a case.","cn":"拉丁语 causa“原因、理由、诉讼”是 causalis、causatio、causari 的基础；同一个名词也藏在 accusare 和 excusare 里，那里指案件中的指控。"},"items":[{"word":"cause","structure":"Latin causa (cause, reason)","meaning":"the reason or source of an effect","meaningCN":"原因；起因（直接来自拉丁语 causa）","example":"The cause of the delay was a broken signal.","exampleCN":"延误的原因是信号灯坏了。"},{"word":"causal","structure":"caus- (cause) + -al (adjective)","meaning":"relating to cause and effect","meaningCN":"因果的（-al 构成形容词）","example":"The study looks for a causal link between the two events.","exampleCN":"这项研究寻找两个事件之间的因果联系。"},{"word":"causation","structure":"caus- + -ation (noun of action)","meaning":"the act or relation of causing","meaningCN":"因果作用；起因（-ation 构成动作名词）","example":"Correlation alone does not prove causation.","exampleCN":"仅有相关性并不能证明因果关系。"},{"word":"causative","structure":"caus- + -ative (adjective)","meaning":"expressing or producing a cause","meaningCN":"使役的；原因的（-ative 构成形容词）","example":"English has causative verbs such as 'make' and 'have'.","exampleCN":"英语有 make、have 这类使役动词。"},{"word":"causeless","structure":"cause + -less (without)","meaning":"having no cause","meaningCN":"无原因的（-less 表没有）","example":"The panic seemed causeless.","exampleCN":"那阵恐慌似乎没有来由。"},{"word":"because","structure":"by + cause (fused phrase)","meaning":"for the reason that","meaningCN":"因为（by + cause 凝固而成）","example":"We stopped because the road was closed.","exampleCN":"我们停下来，因为道路封了。"},{"word":"accuse","structure":"ac- (ad-, to) + causa (charge)","meaning":"to bring a charge against","meaningCN":"指控（ad- 朝向 + causa 案由）","example":"They accused him of cheating.","exampleCN":"他们指控他作弊。"},{"word":"excuse","structure":"ex- (out of) + causa (charge)","meaning":"to release from a charge","meaningCN":"原谅；免除（ex- 出 + causa 指控）","example":"Please excuse my late reply.","exampleCN":"请原谅我回复晚了。"},{"word":"recuse","structure":"re- (back) + causa (legal case)","meaning":"to withdraw from a case because of prejudice","meaningCN":"（因利益冲突）回避（re- 回 + causa 案件）","example":"The judge recused herself from the trial.","exampleCN":"那位法官回避了这场审判。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"causa","structure":"causa (noun)","meaning":"cause, reason, lawsuit","meaningCN":"原因；理由；诉讼"},{"word":"causalis","structure":"causa + -alis","meaning":"relating to a cause","meaningCN":"因果的"},{"word":"causari","structure":"causa + -ari (verb)","meaning":"to plead, to debate a question","meaningCN":"辩护；争论"}]}},{"word":"cease","ipa_uk":"/siːs/","ipa_us":"/siːs/","definition_zh":"停止；终止；不再","definition_en":"to stop happening or to stop doing something","core_image":"转动的轮子被按下停止键，一圈圈慢下来，最后停住","scene":"雨停在午夜，屋里的母亲轻声说：The rain finally ceased around midnight.","sceneCN":"这里 cease 是「（自然现象）停止」（第 1 个义项：风雨、声音等自行停下来）；句意：雨在午夜前后终于停了。图中可辨识物件：窗上的雨痕、台灯、挂钟。","pos":[{"tag":"vi.","zh":"停止；终止；不再发生"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"停止（某项活动或运营）"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（古/书面）停止（多用于 without cease）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"cease to exist","zh":"不复存在"},{"phrase":"cease fire","zh":"停火"},{"phrase":"cease production","zh":"停止生产"},{"phrase":"cease and desist","zh":"停止并不得再犯"},{"phrase":"without cease","zh":"不停地"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单","form":"ceases"},{"label":"过去式","form":"ceased"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"ceased"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"ceasing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"ceaseless","pos":"adj.","zh":"不停的；无休止的"},{"word":"ceaselessly","pos":"adv.","zh":"不停地"},{"word":"unceasing","pos":"adj.","zh":"不断的；持续的"},{"word":"cessation","pos":"n.","zh":"停止；中止"},{"word":"ceasefire","pos":"n.","zh":"停火"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Come to an end: the rain stops","titleCN":"自行停止：雨停下来","definition":"to stop happening or come to an end, used of natural events, sounds, or actions","definitionCN":"（自然现象、声音或动作）停止发生，告一段落","example":"The noise from the street ceased after midnight.","exampleCN":"街上的噪音午夜之后停了。","why":"Latin cessare was a frequentative of cedere 'go away, withdraw, yield'. When an activity withdraws, it leaves the scene, and what we see is that it has ceased.","whyCN":"拉丁语 cessare 是 cedere“离开、退出、让出”的反复形式。一个活动“退场”了，我们看到的便是它“停止了”。"},{"no":"02","title":"Put a stop to: end an activity or operation","titleCN":"使停止：结束一项活动或运营","definition":"to stop an activity, business, or process, especially permanently","definitionCN":"停止某项活动、业务或流程，尤指永久停止","example":"The factory ceased operations after the accident.","exampleCN":"事故之后，这家工厂停止了运营。","why":"The transitive sense 'put a stop to' is recorded in the late 14c. and is now rarer. Here the subject does not withdraw itself; it makes the activity withdraw.","whyCN":"及物的“使停止”义记录于 14 世纪后期，现在较少用。这里退出舞台的不是主语本身，而是主语让那个活动退场。"},{"no":"03","title":"Cease to be: stop existing or stop doing","titleCN":"不再：不复存在或不再做","definition":"followed by a to-infinitive, to stop doing something or stop being in a state","definitionCN":"后接不定式，表示停止做某事或不再处于某种状态","example":"Many small shops ceased to exist during the recession.","exampleCN":"经济衰退期间，许多小店铺不复存在。","why":"When the verb takes an infinitive, the withdrawal lands on a state of being: the shop does not slow down, it stops being at all.","whyCN":"当动词接不定式时，“退出”落在一种存在状态上：店铺不是慢下来，而是彻底不再“在”。"},{"no":"04","title":"Cease doing: give up a practice","titleCN":"停止某种做法：放弃一种惯例","definition":"followed by a gerund, to stop doing something regularly","definitionCN":"后接动名词，表示停止某种经常性的做法","example":"The company ceased using plastic bags last year.","exampleCN":"这家公司去年停止使用塑料袋。","why":"A gerund names an ongoing practice. The withdrawal is aimed at a habit rather than at a single act, so the change is a policy, not a pause.","whyCN":"动名词命名一种持续的做法。“退出”针对的是习惯，而不是单个动作，所以这改变是一项政策，而不是一次暂停。"},{"no":"05","title":"Cease fire: a military command to stop shooting","titleCN":"停火：停止射击的军令","definition":"in warfare, to stop firing weapons, usually by order or by agreement","definitionCN":"作战中停止射击，通常出于命令或协议","example":"Both sides agreed to cease fire at dawn.","exampleCN":"双方同意在黎明停火。","why":"The command cease fire is attested from 1847. In battle the general verb narrowed to one action, because stopping the shooting is what stopping means there.","whyCN":"cease fire 这一军令记录于 1847 年。战场上，泛指的“停”缩小为一个具体动作，因为在那种场合，“停”就是停火。"},{"no":"06","title":"Cease and desist: a legal order to stop for good","titleCN":"停止并不得再犯：法律上的永久停止令","definition":"in law, to stop an activity and not resume it, usually under a formal order","definitionCN":"法律上指停止某项活动且不得恢复，通常依据正式命令","example":"The court ordered the firm to cease and desist from the practice.","exampleCN":"法院命令该公司停止这种做法并不得再犯。","why":"Legal English pairs two near-synonyms for emphasis. Cease supplies the formal 'stop', desist adds 'refuse to continue', and together they close the door on repetition.","whyCN":"法律英语用两个近义词并列来加强语气。cease 提供正式的“停止”，desist 添上“拒绝继续”，两者合起来把重复的大门关上。"},{"no":"07","title":"Without cease: without stopping, a surviving noun","titleCN":"不停地：残留至今的古名词","definition":"in the phrase without cease, continuously and without a pause","definitionCN":"用于短语 without cease，表示连续不断、没有停顿","example":"The wind blew without cease for three days.","exampleCN":"风不停地刮了三天。","why":"The noun cease, 'a stopping', is recorded around 1300 and is now archaic. It survives mainly in without cease, where the old noun still names a pause that never comes.","whyCN":"名词 cease 意为“一次停止”，记录于约 1300 年，现已古旧。它主要活在 without cease 里，那个古老的名词仍指一次始终没来的停顿。"},{"no":"08","title":"Cease from: withdraw from an activity","titleCN":"停止（做）：从活动中退出","definition":"in formal or archaic style, to stop doing something, used with from","definitionCN":"在正式或古旧文体中与 from 连用，表示停止做某事","example":"The monks ceased from work at the sound of the bell.","exampleCN":"钟声一响，修士们就停止劳作。","why":"Cedere meant 'withdraw from'. The preposition from keeps the literal picture: the person steps back out of the activity rather than switching it off.","whyCN":"cedere 本义是“从……退出”。介词 from 保留了字面画面：人是从活动中退出来，而不是把活动关掉。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Cease comes from Latin cessare, a frequentative verb built on cedere 'to go away, withdraw, yield'. The modern word keeps the picture of stepping back until motion stops.","cn":"cease 来自拉丁语 cessare，这是由 cedere“离开、退出、让出”构成的反复动词。现代词仍保留“一直后退直到不动”的画面。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Cessare meant 'cease, go slow, give over, leave off, be idle'. It was a frequentative of cedere (past participle cessus) 'go away, withdraw, yield'.","cn":"cessare 意为“停止、慢下来、放弃、中断、闲着”，是 cedere（过去分词 cessus）“离开、退出、让出”的反复形式。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Cedere is traced to PIE *ked- 'to go, yield'. The root is a reconstruction with no written record, so this deepest layer is source uncertain.","cn":"cedere 被追溯到原始印欧语 *ked-“走、让出”。该词根是重构形式，没有书面记录，故这一最深层为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (12c.)","en":"Cesser meant 'come to an end, stop, cease; give up, desist' and supplied the form English borrowed.","cn":"cesser 意为“结束、停止、中止；放弃、停止”，提供了英语借入的词形。"},{"era":"c. 1300 ENGLISH","en":"English cesen meant 'stop moving, acting, or speaking; come to an end'. The transitive 'put a stop to' follows in the late 14c. and is now rare; the noun cease is also c. 1300 and archaic.","cn":"英语 cesen 意为“停止移动、行动或说话；结束”。及物的“使停止”接着出现在 14 世纪后期，现已少用；名词 cease 同样记录于约 1300 年，已属古旧。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The military command cease fire is attested from 1847, and the noun ceasefire from 1916. Ceaseless and cessation keep the same stem alive in ordinary English.","cn":"军令 cease fire 记录于 1847 年，名词 ceasefire 记录于 1916 年。ceaseless 与 cessation 让同一个词干在普通英语里继续活着。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"seize","ipa":"/siːz/","tag":"near sound","definition":"to take hold of something suddenly, or to take control by force. It ends in /z/, while cease ends in /s/.","definitionCN":"抓住；夺取。结尾读 /z/，而 cease 结尾读 /s/。"},{"word":"crease","ipa":"/kriːs/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"a line or fold made by folding or pressing; to make such a line. It adds cr- before -ease.","definitionCN":"折痕；压出折痕。在 -ease 前多了 cr-。"},{"word":"ease","ipa":"/iːz/","tag":"near sound","definition":"lack of difficulty, or to make something less painful. It is a short word with no initial consonant.","definitionCN":"容易；减轻。是个短词，开头没有辅音。"},{"word":"seas","ipa":"/siːz/","tag":"near sound","definition":"the plural of sea. It is a homophone of seize and close to cease in sound.","definitionCN":"sea 的复数。与 seize 同音，读音接近 cease。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"stop","ipa":"/stɒp/","tag":"general word","definition":"to end movement or action. It is the plain everyday equivalent of cease.","definitionCN":"停止。是 cease 最日常的说法。"},{"word":"halt","ipa":"/hɔːlt/","tag":"formal stop","definition":"to stop moving or stop an activity, often by order. It is more abrupt than cease.","definitionCN":"停止；叫停。常带命令意味，比 cease 更突然。"},{"word":"end","ipa":"/end/","tag":"come to an end","definition":"to finish or reach the last part. It stresses completion rather than withdrawal.","definitionCN":"结束。强调完成，而不是退出。"},{"word":"terminate","ipa":"/ˈtɜːmɪneɪt/","tag":"formal end","definition":"to bring something to a formal end, especially a contract or a process.","definitionCN":"终止。尤指正式结束合同或程序。"},{"word":"discontinue","ipa":"/ˌdɪskənˈtɪnjuː/","tag":"give up regularly","definition":"to stop doing or producing something on a regular basis.","definitionCN":"停止；停产。指停止经常性做的事或生产。"},{"word":"desist","ipa":"/dɪˈzɪst/","tag":"legal partner","definition":"to stop doing something, especially after being told to. It pairs with cease in cease and desist.","definitionCN":"停止（尤指被要求后）。在 cease and desist 中与 cease 并列。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: the Latin cedere family, the legal doublet cease and desist, and compounds such as ceasefire.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 cedere 词族、法律双词 cease and desist，以及 ceasefire 这类复合词。"},"normal":[{"en":"cease and desist is a legal doublet: cease is the Latin 'stop', desist adds 'refuse to continue'.","cn":"cease and desist 是法律上的双词结构：cease 是拉丁语的“停”，desist 添上“拒绝继续”。"},{"en":"ceasefire = cease + fire: the command literally tells soldiers to stop firing.","cn":"ceasefire = cease + fire：这条命令字面上就是让士兵停止开火。"},{"en":"cessation is the noun from the same Latin stem cess-; a cessation of fighting is a stop.","cn":"cessation 是同一拉丁词干 cess- 构成的名词；a cessation of fighting 就是停止战斗。"},{"en":"cede, cession and concession come from cedere 'yield'; cease is its frequentative, 'keep yielding until motion ends'.","cn":"cede、cession、concession 都来自 cedere“让出”；cease 是它的反复形式，意为“一直让，直到不动”。"},{"en":"without cease keeps the archaic noun: a pause that never arrives.","cn":"without cease 保留了古旧的名词：一次始终不来的停顿。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Cease is motion withdrawing: the activity steps back off the stage, and what remains is stillness.","cn":"cease 是运动在退出：活动从舞台上退下，剩下的是静止。"},{"en":"The same verb covers rain, factories, gunfire and habits; the object changes, the withdrawal does not.","cn":"同一个动词覆盖雨、工厂、炮火和习惯；对象变了，退出这个动作没变。"},{"en":"Its grammar repeats the picture: to cease is to leave a state, cease from is to step out of an activity, without cease is a gap that never opens.","cn":"它的语法也在重复这幅画：cease 是离开一种状态，cease from 是从活动中退出，without cease 是一个始终没有打开的缺口。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The baby finally ceased crying and fell asleep.","cn":"婴儿终于不再哭，睡着了。"},{"en":"The airline ceased all flights to the island.","cn":"这家航空公司停止了所有飞往该岛的航班。"},{"en":"They worked without cease until the roof was finished.","cn":"他们不停地干活，直到屋顶完工。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“息事”——把事“息”掉、让它停下来 → cease 停止、终止","word":"cease"},"root":"源自拉丁语 cessare“停止、慢下来”，是 cedere“离开、退让”（过去分词 cessus）的反复形式；核心是“退出动作，直到静止”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of cease, all built on withdrawal: an activity leaves the scene, and the result is silence, stillness, or an end. Grammar and compounds extend the same picture.","cn":"cease 的八个义项都建立在“退出”上：一个活动离开现场，结果是安静、静止或终结。语法搭配与复合词延续了同一画面。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: motion withdraws from the scene until it stops.","cn":"核心意象：运动从现场退出，直到停住。"},"chain":["MOVE","WITHDRAW","GO SLOW","LEAVE OFF","COME TO AN END","STAY STOPPED"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1","en":"AN ACTIVITY LEAVES BY ITSELF: rain, noise and wind simply withdraw from the scene.","cn":"活动自行离场：雨、噪音、风只是从现场退走。"},{"senses":"S2","en":"SOMEONE MAKES IT LEAVE: a factory or an airline is ordered to withdraw its operations.","cn":"有人让它离场：工厂或航空公司被要求撤回运营。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"THE TARGET OF THE STOP: an infinitive ends a state of being, a gerund gives up a standing practice.","cn":"停止的对象：不定式终结一种存在状态，动名词放弃一种长期做法。"},{"senses":"S5 · S6","en":"TWO FORMAL SCENES: the battlefield narrows stop to gunfire, the courtroom doubles it into cease and desist.","cn":"两个正式场景：战场把“停”缩小为炮火，法庭把它叠成 cease and desist。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"THE OLD NOUN AND THE OLD PREPOSITION: without cease keeps a pause that never comes, while cease from keeps the literal step out.","cn":"古老的名词与古老的介词：without cease 保留一次不来的停顿，cease from 保留字面上的退出。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Cease carries the Latin stem cess- into English: -less, -ation and the negative prefixes un- and in- build the family, while compounds such as ceasefire keep the verb visible.","cn":"cease 把拉丁词干 cess- 带进英语：-less、-ation 以及否定前缀 un-、in- 构成词族，ceasefire 这类复合词则让动词本身仍然可见。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin cedere 'go, yield' produced cessare 'stop' and cessatio 'a stopping'; the same root appears in concede, proceed and exceed, where the sense of going or yielding remains.","cn":"拉丁语 cedere“走、让出”产生了 cessare“停止”和 cessatio“一次停止”；同一词根还出现在 concede、proceed、exceed 里，那里仍保留“走”或“让出”的意思。"},"items":[{"word":"cease","structure":"Latin cessare (stop), frequentative of cedere","meaning":"to stop happening or doing","meaningCN":"停止；终止（来自拉丁语 cessare）","example":"The music ceased at midnight.","exampleCN":"音乐在午夜停了。"},{"word":"ceaseless","structure":"cease + -less (without)","meaning":"without stopping","meaningCN":"不停的（-less 表没有）","example":"The ceaseless rain flooded the fields.","exampleCN":"不停的雨淹了田地。"},{"word":"ceaselessly","structure":"ceaseless + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a way that never stops","meaningCN":"不停地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"She worked ceaselessly for the charity.","exampleCN":"她为这家慈善机构不停地工作。"},{"word":"unceasing","structure":"un- (not) + ceasing (present participle)","meaning":"never stopping","meaningCN":"不断的（un- 表否定）","example":"His unceasing efforts finally paid off.","exampleCN":"他不断的努力终于有了回报。"},{"word":"cessation","structure":"cess- (stop) + -ation (noun of action)","meaning":"a stopping or a pause","meaningCN":"停止；中止（-ation 构成动作名词）","example":"Both sides welcomed a cessation of hostilities.","exampleCN":"双方都欢迎停止敌对行动。"},{"word":"incessant","structure":"in- (not) + cess- (stop) + -ant (adjective)","meaning":"continuing without a pause","meaningCN":"持续不断的（in- 否定 + -ant 形容词）","example":"Her incessant questions tired the guide.","exampleCN":"她没完没了的问题让导游很累。"},{"word":"concession","structure":"con- (fully) + cess- (yield) + -ion (noun)","meaning":"something yielded; an act of granting","meaningCN":"让步；特许（con- + cess 让出 + -ion）","example":"The union won a major concession.","exampleCN":"工会赢得了一项重大让步。"},{"word":"proceed","structure":"pro- (forward) + cedere (go)","meaning":"to go forward; to continue","meaningCN":"继续进行；前进（pro- 向前 + cedere 走）","example":"The meeting proceeded as planned.","exampleCN":"会议按计划继续进行。"},{"word":"exceed","structure":"ex- (beyond) + cedere (go)","meaning":"to go beyond a limit","meaningCN":"超过（ex- 超出 + cedere 走）","example":"Costs must not exceed the budget.","exampleCN":"成本不得超过预算。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"cessare","structure":"frequentative of cedere","meaning":"to stop, go slow, be idle","meaningCN":"停止；慢下来；闲着"},{"word":"cedere","structure":"cedere (verb)","meaning":"to go, withdraw, yield","meaningCN":"走；退出；让出"},{"word":"cessatio","structure":"cessare + -tio","meaning":"a stopping, cessation","meaningCN":"停止；中止"}]}},{"word":"challenge","ipa_uk":"/ˈtʃælɪndʒ/","ipa_us":"/ˈtʃælɪndʒ/","definition_zh":"挑战；质疑；向……挑战；难题；指控","definition_en":"to question, invite to compete, or accuse; also a difficult task or a call to compete","core_image":"一只手套被扔到地上：你敢不敢接招","scene":"面试官把一份复杂的案例推到桌上说：This task will challenge everything you know.","sceneCN":"这里 challenge 是「考验、使受挑战」（第 8 个义项：任务激发并检验能力）；句意：这项任务会挑战你所知道的一切。图中可辨识物件：桌面、案例文件、笔、面试官。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"挑战；难题；质疑；邀请比赛"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"向……挑战；质疑；考验；指控"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"（challenged）有……障碍的（委婉语）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"face a challenge","zh":"面对挑战"},{"phrase":"challenge somebody to do something","zh":"挑战某人做某事"},{"phrase":"challenge a decision","zh":"质疑一项决定"},{"phrase":"a legal challenge","zh":"法律上的异议"},{"phrase":"rise to the challenge","zh":"迎难而上"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单","form":"challenges"},{"label":"过去式","form":"challenged"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"challenged"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"challenging"},{"label":"复数","form":"challenges"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"challenger","pos":"n.","zh":"挑战者"},{"word":"challenging","pos":"adj.","zh":"有挑战性的；考验人的"},{"word":"challenged","pos":"adj.","zh":"受到挑战的；（委婉）有障碍的"},{"word":"unchallenged","pos":"adj.","zh":"未受质疑的；无人挑战的"},{"word":"challengeable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可质疑的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A difficult task: something that tests you","titleCN":"艰巨任务：考验你的难题","definition":"a task or situation that tests someone's abilities and is therefore difficult","definitionCN":"考验某人能力、因而显得困难的任务或处境","example":"Learning to write academic English is a real challenge.","exampleCN":"学会写学术英语是一项真正的挑战。","why":"The 'difficult task' sense is recorded only by 1954, the youngest step. A task becomes a challenge when it calls you out, as a duel calls a fighter out.","whyCN":"“艰巨任务”这一义到 1954 年才有记录，是最年轻的一步。任务之所以成为 challenge，是因为它像决斗点名一样把你“叫出来”。"},{"no":"02","title":"Question: doubt whether something is true or right","titleCN":"质疑：怀疑某事是否真实或正当","definition":"to express doubt about whether something is true, valid, or acceptable","definitionCN":"对某事物是否真实、有效或可接受表示怀疑","example":"Several scientists challenged the study's conclusions.","exampleCN":"几位科学家质疑这项研究的结论。","why":"From the late 13c. the verb meant 'object to, take exception to'. The old accusation turns into a demand for proof: you throw the charge back at the claim.","whyCN":"从 13 世纪后期起，动词意为“反对、对……提出异议”。古老的指控变成索要证据：你把指控反掷回那个说法。"},{"no":"03","title":"Invite to compete: throw down the glove","titleCN":"邀战：把手套扔到地上","definition":"to invite someone to compete or fight, especially in a contest","definitionCN":"邀请某人比赛或较量，尤指在竞赛中","example":"He challenged the champion to a rematch.","exampleCN":"他向冠军挑战，要求再赛一场。","why":"Late 14c. records 'call to fight'. The core picture is a glove thrown down: a formal invitation that the other side must answer.","whyCN":"14 世纪后期记录了“叫阵、邀战”。核心画面是一只扔下的手套：一份对方必须回应的正式邀请。"},{"no":"04","title":"A call to compete: the invitation itself","titleCN":"挑战邀请：那只被扔出的手套","definition":"an invitation to take part in a contest or to prove oneself","definitionCN":"邀请某人参加比赛或证明自己的举动或话语","example":"She accepted his challenge to run a marathon.","exampleCN":"她接受了他跑马拉松的挑战。","why":"The noun keeps the duel: the challenge is the thrown glove as an object, not the fight that follows. Early 14c. already used it for 'a call to fight'.","whyCN":"名词保留了决斗：challenge 是扔出去的那只手套本身，而不是随后的打斗。14 世纪初它就已指“叫阵”。"},{"no":"05","title":"Accuse: lay a charge against someone","titleCN":"指控：把罪责加在某人身上","definition":"in older or formal use, to accuse someone of a fault or crime","definitionCN":"在较古老或正式的用法中，指控某人犯错或犯罪","example":"In medieval courts a man could be challenged with treason.","exampleCN":"在中世纪法庭上，一个人可能被指控叛国。","why":"The verb began c. 1200 as 'to rebuke', from Latin calumniari 'to accuse falsely'. The oldest layer is a charge laid on a person, before any idea of a contest.","whyCN":"动词约 1200 年出现时意为“斥责”，来自拉丁语 calumniari“诬告”。最古老的一层是把罪责加在某人身上，还没有任何比赛的意思。"},{"no":"06","title":"Challenge at the gate: demand identification","titleCN":"喝问身份：哨兵拦下并盘问","definition":"of a sentry or guard, to call out to someone and demand that they identify themselves","definitionCN":"（哨兵或警卫）喝住某人，要求其说明身份","example":"The guard challenged every car that approached the gate.","exampleCN":"警卫对每一辆靠近大门的车都喝问身份。","why":"A sentry's challenge is an accusation in miniature: you are stopped and must answer who you are. The duel's 'call out' became a security check.","whyCN":"哨兵的 challenge 是缩小版的指控：你被拦下，必须回答自己是谁。决斗中的“叫出来”变成了安全检查。"},{"no":"07","title":"Challenge a juror: object in court","titleCN":"申请回避：在法庭上提出异议","definition":"in law, to object formally to a juror, a witness, or a ruling","definitionCN":"法律上对陪审员、证人或某项裁定提出的正式异议","example":"The defence challenged two jurors before the trial began.","exampleCN":"审判开始前，辩方申请两名陪审员回避。","why":"Mid-15c. law used challenge for 'an objection'. The courtroom is the modern home of the old accusatory sense: a charge against the validity of a procedure.","whyCN":"15 世纪中期的法律用 challenge 指“异议”。法庭是古老指控义的现代归宿：对程序有效性提出指控。"},{"no":"08","title":"Test and push: make someone use their full ability","titleCN":"考验：把人逼到能力的边上","definition":"to test someone's ability or courage, often in a way that makes them grow","definitionCN":"考验某人的能力或勇气，常使其因此成长","example":"The course challenges students to think for themselves.","exampleCN":"这门课促使学生独立思考。","why":"A contest tests strength; remove the opponent and what remains is the test itself. The verb then means to stretch someone's capacity rather than to fight them.","whyCN":"比赛检验实力；把对手拿掉，剩下的就是检验本身。于是动词转而表示拉伸某人的能力，而不是与他打斗。"},{"no":"09","title":"A formal objection: a challenge to a rule","titleCN":"正式反对：对规则或决定的异议","definition":"a public or legal objection to a decision, law, or authority","definitionCN":"对某项决定、法律或权威的公开或法律异议","example":"The new housing rule faces a legal challenge from residents.","exampleCN":"这项新住房规定面临居民的法律异议。","why":"The noun's legal sense 'an objection' dates from the mid-15c. A challenge to a law is a charge brought against it, and the law must answer.","whyCN":"名词的法律义“异议”可追溯到 15 世纪中期。对一条法律的 challenge 就是把它传唤到庭，它必须作出回答。"},{"no":"10","title":"Challenged: a softened word for disability","titleCN":"委婉语：challenged 指“有障碍的”","definition":"used in the phrase physically challenged, a euphemism for having a disability","definitionCN":"用于 physically challenged 这一短语，是“身有残障”的委婉说法","example":"The centre runs sports programmes for the physically challenged.","exampleCN":"该中心为身体有障碍的人提供体育项目。","why":"From 1985 challenged became a euphemism for 'disabled'. The logic is kind: a disability is recast as a challenge to be met, not a defect.","whyCN":"从 1985 年起，challenged 成为 disabled 的委婉说法。其逻辑是善意的：把残障重新表述为有待应对的挑战，而不是缺陷。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Challenge goes back through Old French to Latin calumnia 'false accusation'. English kept the charge, then turned it into an objection, a call to fight, and finally a difficult task.","cn":"challenge 经古法语上溯到拉丁语 calumnia“诬告”。英语保留了“指控”，再把它变成异议、叫阵，最后变成艰巨任务。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Calumnia meant 'trickery, subterfuge, misrepresentation, malicious charge', from calvi 'to trick, deceive'. The deeper origin of calvi is uncertain, and sources only suggest distant links to call, so the earliest layer is source uncertain.","cn":"calumnia 意为“诡计、托词、歪曲、恶意指控”，来自 calvi“欺骗”。calvi 的更深来源不明，资料只提出与 call 可能有远亲关系，因此最深层为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"VULGAR LATIN","en":"The verb *calumniare 'to accuse falsely' is recorded as a reconstructed Vulgar Latin form, marked with a star. Being a reconstruction without direct written record, it is also source uncertain.","cn":"动词 *calumniare“诬告”被记录为带星号的俗拉丁语重构形式。既然是重构、没有直接书面记录，它也属“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (c. 1200)","en":"Chalongier meant 'complain, protest; haggle, quibble'. English took it c. 1200 as 'to rebuke', then late 13c. as 'to object to'.","cn":"chalongier 意为“抱怨、抗议；讨价还价、狡辩”。英语约 1200 年借入为“斥责”，13 世纪后期转为“反对”。"},{"era":"LATE 13c–14c ENGLISH","en":"By c. 1300 the verb also meant 'to accuse' and 'to call to account'; late 14c. added 'to call to fight'. The noun, early 14c., first meant 'accusation, fault'.","cn":"到约 1300 年，动词也指“指控”和“要求某人作出解释”；14 世纪后期又添“叫阵、邀战”。名词在 14 世纪初先指“指控、过失”。"},{"era":"17c ENGLISH","en":"The accusatory connotations faded in the 17c. Law kept 'an objection' from the mid-15c., and 'a calling to fight' also dates from the mid-15c.","cn":"指控色彩在 17 世纪淡去。法律保留了 15 世纪中期以来的“异议”义，“叫阵”同样始于 15 世纪中期。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The sense 'difficult task' appears in 1954, and challenged as a euphemism for 'disabled' in 1985. The modern word is mostly about tests, not charges.","cn":"“艰巨任务”义出现于 1954 年，challenged 作为“残障”的委婉语出现于 1985 年。现代这个词多半关乎考验，而不是指控。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and sound, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和读音挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"change","ipa":"/tʃeɪndʒ/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"to make or become different. It shares the opening sound but has no l and no sense of testing.","definitionCN":"改变。开头读音相近，但没有 l，也没有“考验”之意。"},{"word":"challenger","ipa":"/ˈtʃælɪndʒə(r)/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"a person who challenges another person to a contest. It is the agent noun built directly on challenge.","definitionCN":"挑战者。它是直接由 challenge 构成的施事名词。"},{"word":"challenged","ipa":"/ˈtʃælɪndʒd/","tag":"derived adjective","definition":"having been challenged; also a euphemism for having a disability.","definitionCN":"受到挑战的；也用作“有残障”的委婉语。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"dare","ipa":"/deə(r)/","tag":"provoke","definition":"to invite someone to do something risky, testing their courage.","definitionCN":"激将；挑战某人做有风险的事，以检验其勇气。"},{"word":"confront","ipa":"/kənˈfrʌnt/","tag":"face directly","definition":"to face someone or something directly, especially in a hostile way.","definitionCN":"直面；对抗，尤指带敌意地面对。"},{"word":"dispute","ipa":"/dɪˈspjuːt/","tag":"argue against","definition":"to argue that something is wrong or not valid.","definitionCN":"争辩；认为某事错误或无效。"},{"word":"question","ipa":"/ˈkwestʃən/","tag":"doubt","definition":"to express doubt about something.","definitionCN":"质疑；对某事表示怀疑。"},{"word":"test","ipa":"/test/","tag":"try ability","definition":"to measure or try someone's ability.","definitionCN":"测验；检验某人的能力。"},{"word":"defy","ipa":"/dɪˈfaɪ/","tag":"resist","definition":"to refuse to obey, or to be too strong to be explained.","definitionCN":"违抗；使无法解释。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: challenge and calumny are doublets from Latin calumnia, and the duel, the courtroom objection and the exam question share one gesture.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：challenge 与 calumny 是来自拉丁语 calumnia 的同源双式词，决斗、法庭异议和考试提问共享同一个动作。"},"normal":[{"en":"challenge and calumny are doublets: both come from Latin calumnia 'false accusation'. The duel grew out of the accusation.","cn":"challenge 与 calumny 是同源双式词：都来自拉丁语 calumnia“诬告”。决斗是从指控里长出来的。"},{"en":"a challenge is literally a call: the old verb meant 'to call to account' and 'to call to fight'.","cn":"challenge 字面上是一次“点名呼叫”：古动词既指“要求某人作出解释”，也指“叫阵”。"},{"en":"challenger is the person who throws the glove; unchallenged means nobody threw one.","cn":"challenger 是扔手套的人；unchallenged 就是没人朝他扔过手套。"},{"en":"a legal challenge asks a rule to answer for itself, just as a duel asks a fighter to answer.","cn":"法律上的 challenge 是要求一条规则为自己作答，正如决斗要求一名斗士应战。"},{"en":"physically challenged reframes a disability as a challenge, a task to meet rather than a defect.","cn":"physically challenged 把残障重新说成一项挑战，是要应对的任务，而不是缺陷。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Challenge is an accusation that has been turned into a question; the demand for proof is the modern form of the old charge.","cn":"challenge 是一个被转成问句的指控；索要证据就是古老罪责的现代形态。"},{"en":"The same call moves outward: accuse a person, question a claim, summon a fighter, test a student, and finally name the hard task itself.","cn":"同一次“点名”往外走：指控一个人、质疑一个说法、叫阵一名斗士、考验一个学生，最后命名艰巨任务本身。"},{"en":"So the glove, the courtroom objection and the exam question are one gesture: you are called out and must answer.","cn":"所以手套、法庭异议和考试题是同一个动作：你被叫出来，必须回应。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The job offers a serious challenge to anyone who takes it.","cn":"这份工作对任何接手的人都是一场严峻挑战。"},{"en":"Nobody dared to challenge his version of the story.","cn":"没人敢质疑他对这件事的说法。"},{"en":"The teacher challenged us to solve the problem in ten minutes.","cn":"老师挑战我们十分钟内解出这道题。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“拆轮子”——把轮子拆开再装回去，是个大挑战 → challenge 挑战","word":"challenge"},"root":"源自拉丁语 calumnia“诬告、诡计”，经古法语 chalongier 进入英语；核心是“把指控叫到对方头上”，后转为“叫阵、质疑、考验”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Ten senses of challenge, from a false accusation to a difficult task. The accusation became an objection, the objection became a call to fight, and the duel became a test.","cn":"challenge 的十个义项，从诬告走到艰巨任务。指控变成异议，异议变成叫阵，决斗又变成考验。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a glove thrown down — you are called out and must answer.","cn":"核心意象：一只扔下的手套——你被点名，必须回应。"},"chain":["ACCUSE","REBUKE","OBJECT","CALL TO ACCOUNT","CALL TO FIGHT","TEST AND TASK"],"branches":[{"senses":"S5","en":"THE OLDEST LAYER: a charge laid on a person, from the Latin verb 'to accuse falsely'.","cn":"最古老的一层：把罪责加到某人身上，来自拉丁语“诬告”动词。"},{"senses":"S2 · S9","en":"THE CHARGE TURNS INTO AN OBJECTION: a claim or a law must answer for itself.","cn":"指控转为异议：一个说法或一条法律必须为自己作答。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"THE DUEL: a glove thrown down, and the invitation kept as an object.","cn":"决斗：一只扔下的手套，以及被当作物件保留的邀请。"},{"senses":"S6 · S7","en":"THE FORMAL CHALLENGE: a sentry demands a name, a court demands a valid procedure.","cn":"正式场合的挑战：哨兵索取姓名，法庭要求程序有效。"},{"senses":"S1 · S8 · S10","en":"THE TEST WITHOUT AN OPPONENT: abilities are stretched, the task becomes the challenge, and disability is softened into one.","cn":"没有对手的考验：能力被拉伸，任务本身成为挑战，残障也被委婉地说成一种挑战。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Challenge comes from Latin calumnia through Old French. Its English family adds -er, -ing, -ed, -able and un-, while the doublet calumny keeps the original 'false accusation'.","cn":"challenge 经古法语来自拉丁语 calumnia。它的英语词族加上 -er、-ing、-ed、-able 和 un-，而同源双式词 calumny 保留了原本的“诬告”义。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin calumnia 'trickery, false charge' and calumniari 'to accuse falsely' are the base; calumny, calumniate and calumnious preserve the old sense that English challenge has largely left behind.","cn":"拉丁语 calumnia“诡计、诬告”和 calumniari“诬告”是基础；calumny、calumniate、calumnious 保留了英语 challenge 大多已丢掉的古义。"},"items":[{"word":"challenge","structure":"Latin calumnia via Old French chalongier","meaning":"to question, accuse, or invite to compete","meaningCN":"质疑；指控；邀战（经古法语借入）","example":"She challenged the official figures.","exampleCN":"她质疑官方数字。"},{"word":"challenger","structure":"challenge + -er (agent noun)","meaning":"one who challenges","meaningCN":"挑战者（-er 表示施事者）","example":"The challenger lost the final round.","exampleCN":"挑战者输掉了最后一轮。"},{"word":"challenging","structure":"challenge + -ing (adjective)","meaning":"difficult in an interesting way","meaningCN":"有挑战性的（-ing 构成形容词）","example":"It was a challenging but rewarding job.","exampleCN":"这份工作有挑战性，也很有收获。"},{"word":"challenged","structure":"challenge + -ed (past participle)","meaning":"having been challenged","meaningCN":"受到挑战的（-ed 构成过去分词）","example":"His authority was openly challenged.","exampleCN":"他的权威受到公开挑战。"},{"word":"unchallenged","structure":"un- (not) + challenged","meaning":"not questioned or opposed","meaningCN":"未受质疑的（un- 表否定）","example":"The report went unchallenged.","exampleCN":"那份报告未受质疑。"},{"word":"challengeable","structure":"challenge + -able (able to be)","meaning":"open to being questioned","meaningCN":"可质疑的（-able 表能够被……）","example":"The ruling is legally challengeable.","exampleCN":"这项裁决在法律上可被质疑。"},{"word":"calumny","structure":"Latin calumnia (false charge)","meaning":"a false accusation; slander","meaningCN":"诬告；诽谤（直接来自拉丁语）","example":"The article was dismissed as calumny.","exampleCN":"那篇文章被斥为诽谤。"},{"word":"calumniate","structure":"calumni- + -ate (verb)","meaning":"to slander; to make false charges","meaningCN":"诬蔑；诽谤（-ate 构成动词）","example":"He was accused of calumniating his rival.","exampleCN":"他被指诽谤对手。"},{"word":"calumnious","structure":"calumni- + -ous (adjective)","meaning":"slanderous","meaningCN":"诽谤性的（-ous 构成形容词）","example":"The paper printed calumnious claims.","exampleCN":"这家报纸刊登了诽谤性言论。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"calumnia","structure":"calumnia (noun)","meaning":"trickery; a false charge","meaningCN":"诡计；诬告"},{"word":"calumniari","structure":"calumnia + -ari (verb)","meaning":"to accuse falsely","meaningCN":"诬告；诽谤"},{"word":"calumniosus","structure":"calumnia + -osus","meaning":"full of false charges; slanderous","meaningCN":"充满诬告的；诽谤的"}]}},{"word":"characteristic","ipa_uk":"/ˌkærəktəˈrɪstɪk/","ipa_us":"/ˌkerəktəˈrɪstɪk/","definition_zh":"特征；特点；特有的；典型的","definition_en":"a distinctive quality that identifies something, or typical of a person or thing","core_image":"石头上刻下的一个记号：看一眼就知道这是谁的东西","scene":"品酒师举着杯子说：A smoky aroma is characteristic of this region's red wines.","sceneCN":"这里 characteristic 是「特有的、典型的」（第 2 个义项：be characteristic of 表示某类事物的标志性特点）；句意：烟熏香气是这个产区红酒的典型特征。图中可辨识物件：酒杯、酒标、产区地图。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"特征；特点；特性"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"特有的；典型的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"be characteristic of","zh":"是……的典型特征"},{"phrase":"a defining characteristic","zh":"决定性特征"},{"phrase":"physical characteristics","zh":"身体特征"},{"phrase":"with characteristic humor","zh":"以他一贯的幽默"},{"phrase":"the characteristics of a species","zh":"一个物种的性状"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more characteristic"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most characteristic"},{"label":"复数","form":"characteristics"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"character","pos":"n.","zh":"性格；角色；字符"},{"word":"characterize","pos":"v.","zh":"描绘；以……为特征"},{"word":"characterization","pos":"n.","zh":"刻画；描述"},{"word":"characteristically","pos":"adv.","zh":"典型地；一贯地"},{"word":"uncharacteristic","pos":"adj.","zh":"反常的；非典型的"},{"word":"characterless","pos":"adj.","zh":"无特色的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A distinctive feature: the mark that identifies a thing","titleCN":"特征：能认出事物的那个记号","definition":"a quality or feature that is typical of a person, place, or thing and helps identify it","definitionCN":"某人、某地或某物典型而可供辨认的品质或特点","example":"Patience is one of the characteristics of a good teacher.","exampleCN":"耐心是好老师的一个特征。","why":"Greek kharaktēr first meant an engraved mark, then 'a defining quality'. A feature is the mark by which you recognise what kind of thing you have.","whyCN":"希腊语 kharaktēr 最初指刻下的记号，后指“界定性的品质”。特征就是你借以认出这是哪类事物的那个记号。"},{"no":"02","title":"Typical of: the mark of a whole class","titleCN":"特有的：整个类别的标志","definition":"typical of a particular person, group, or kind of thing","definitionCN":"某一特定的人、群体或一类事物所特有的","example":"Such patience is characteristic of experienced nurses.","exampleCN":"这种耐心是经验丰富的护士特有的。","why":"The adjective keeps the mark but shifts the viewpoint: instead of naming the mark, it says the mark belongs to the class. The 1660s adjective was built on character + -istic.","whyCN":"形容词保留了“记号”，但换了视角：它不说记号是什么，而说这个记号属于哪一类。1660 年代的形容词由 character + -istic 构成。"},{"no":"03","title":"With characteristic X: in someone's usual style","titleCN":"以一贯的……：某人惯常的作风","definition":"used before a noun to mean 'in the way that person usually does things'","definitionCN":"置于名词前，表示“以某人一贯的方式”","example":"She accepted the criticism with characteristic calm.","exampleCN":"她以一贯的平静接受了批评。","why":"Here characteristic does not classify a group but stamps a single person's habit. The mark is now a signature: this is so like her.","whyCN":"这里 characteristic 不是在给一类事物归类，而是在给一个人的习惯盖印。记号变成了签名：这太像她了。"},{"no":"04","title":"Biological character: a trait used to tell species apart","titleCN":"生物性状：区分物种的特征","definition":"in biology, a structural or functional feature used to identify and compare organisms","definitionCN":"生物学中用于识别和比较生物体的结构或功能特征","example":"Wing colour is a useful characteristic for identifying the species.","exampleCN":"翅色是识别该物种的一个有用性状。","why":"Science needs stable marks to separate one species from another. The everyday 'distinctive feature' becomes a technical trait that can be measured and compared.","whyCN":"科学需要稳定的记号来区分物种。日常的“显著特征”于是变成可测量、可比较的技术性“性状”。"},{"no":"05","title":"Mathematical characteristic: the integer part of a logarithm","titleCN":"数学首数：对数的整数部分","definition":"in mathematics, the whole-number part of a logarithm, or a property named in characteristic equations","definitionCN":"数学中对数的整数部分，或特征方程中所称的性质","example":"The characteristic of log 250 is 2, because the value lies between 100 and 1,000.","exampleCN":"log 250 的首数是 2，因为这个值介于 100 与 1000 之间。","why":"Mathematics borrowed the word for a number that marks a value's place. The characteristic is the fixed part that tells you which order of magnitude you are in — a mark, not a quality.","whyCN":"数学借这个词来指标出数值位置的那个数。首数是告诉你处在哪个数量级的固定部分——它是指号，不是品质。"},{"no":"06","title":"Characteristics: the set of features that make up a place","titleCN":"多项特色：一个地方的整体标志","definition":"the combination of features that gives a place, product, or group its distinct character","definitionCN":"使某地、某产品或某群体具有独特面貌的特征组合","example":"The guide describes the characteristics of the region's food.","exampleCN":"这本指南介绍了该地区食物的特色。","why":"When the marks are collected, they stop being separate traits and become a profile. The plural names the whole pattern by which a place is recognised.","whyCN":"当这些记号被收集起来，它们就不再是孤立的特征，而成为一幅画像。复数指的是一个地方被人认出的整体图案。"},{"no":"07","title":"Character traits: the parts that make up a person","titleCN":"性格特点：构成一个人品格的要素","definition":"a quality that forms part of a person's character, especially a moral one","definitionCN":"构成一个人性格的一部分，尤指道德方面的品质","example":"Generosity was one of her most marked characteristics.","exampleCN":"慷慨是她最显著的性格特点之一。","why":"Character in English came to mean 'the sum of qualities that define a person' (1640s). A characteristic is one of those qualities singled out from the sum.","whyCN":"英语里的 character 在 17 世纪 40 年代起指“界定一个人的全部品质”。characteristic 就是从这总体里单挑出来的一项品质。"},{"no":"08","title":"Characteristically: in a way typical of someone","titleCN":"典型地：以某人一贯的方式","definition":"in a manner that is typical of a particular person or thing, used as the adverb characteristically","definitionCN":"以某人或某物典型的风格，用副词 characteristically 表示","example":"He was, characteristically, the last to arrive.","exampleCN":"他一贯如此，总是最后一个到。","why":"The adverb carries the 'signature' sense of sense 3 and applies it to an action: the way of doing something is itself the identifying mark.","whyCN":"副词承接第 3 义的“签名”含义，并把它用到动作上：做事的方式本身就是那个辨识记号。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Characteristic is character plus -istic, and character goes back to Greek kharaktēr 'engraved mark'. The word moved from a physical stamp to an invisible defining quality, then to a technical feature.","cn":"characteristic 是 character 加 -istic，而 character 可上溯到希腊语 kharaktēr“刻下的记号”。这个词从实物印记走到无形的界定品质，再走到技术性特征。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK","en":"Kharaktēr meant 'engraved mark', also 'instrument for marking', from kharassein 'to engrave', from kharax 'pointed stake'. The etymology of kharax is uncertain and Beekes calls it 'most probably Pre-Greek', so the deepest step is source uncertain.","cn":"kharaktēr 意为“刻下的记号”，也指“用来刻印的工具”，来自 kharassein“刻”，再来自 kharax“尖桩”。kharax 的词源不明，Beekes 认为它“极可能属于前希腊语”，所以最深层为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"HELLENISTIC GREEK","en":"Kharaktēr was extended by metaphor to 'a defining quality, individual feature'. The physical mark became the invisible thing that marks a person or thing as what it is.","cn":"kharaktēr 经隐喻扩展为“界定性的品质、个别特征”。有形的记号变成了无形的、把某人某物标定为自身的那个东西。"},{"era":"LATIN AND MIDDLE ENGLISH","en":"Latin character kept both 'brand, mark' and 'distinctive quality'. English had carecter by mid-14c. for 'a symbol marked or branded on the body', and by late 15c. for 'an alphabetic letter'.","cn":"拉丁语 character 同时保留“烙印、记号”和“独特品质”。英语在 14 世纪中期已有 carecter，指“烙在身上或画上的符号”，到 15 世纪后期又指“字母”。"},{"era":"1640s ENGLISH","en":"Character came to mean 'the sum of qualities that define a person or thing and distinguish it from another'. The abstract sense was ready for an adjective to be built on it.","cn":"character 取得“界定一个人或事物、并使之区别于他者的全部品质”之义。抽象含义已经为派生形容词准备好了基础。"},{"era":"1660s ENGLISH","en":"Characteristic appears in the 1660s as both adjective and noun, from character + -istic on the model of Greek kharaktēristikos. The earlier adjective was characteristical (1620s).","cn":"characteristic 在 17 世纪 60 年代同时以形容词和名词出现，由 character + -istic 仿希腊语 kharaktēristikos 构成。更早的形容词形式是 1620 年代的 characteristical。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Science made characteristic a measurable property, as in characteristic curve. Uncharacteristic is recorded from 1753, and characteristically from the 1640s.","cn":"科学把 characteristic 变成可测量的性质，如 characteristic curve（特性曲线）。uncharacteristic 记录于 1753 年，characteristically 则始于 17 世纪 40 年代。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"character","ipa":"/ˈkærəktə(r)/","tag":"base noun","definition":"the qualities that define a person, or a letter or symbol. It is the noun characteristic is built on.","definitionCN":"性格；角色；字符。它是 characteristic 所由构成的名词。"},{"word":"characterize","ipa":"/ˈkærəktəraɪz/","tag":"derived verb","definition":"to describe the qualities of something, or to be typical of it.","definitionCN":"描绘……的特点；以……为特征。"},{"word":"characterless","ipa":"/ˈkærəktələs/","tag":"derived adjective","definition":"without distinctive qualities.","definitionCN":"无特色的；没有特点的。"},{"word":"characteristically","ipa":"/ˌkærəktəˈrɪstɪkli/","tag":"derived adverb","definition":"in a way typical of someone or something.","definitionCN":"典型地；一贯地。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"feature","ipa":"/ˈfiːtʃə(r)/","tag":"part of a whole","definition":"an important part or quality of something.","definitionCN":"特点；组成部分。"},{"word":"trait","ipa":"/treɪt/","tag":"personal quality","definition":"a particular quality in someone's character.","definitionCN":"（人的）性格特点。"},{"word":"quality","ipa":"/ˈkwɒləti/","tag":"general word","definition":"a characteristic of a person or thing, often a good one.","definitionCN":"品质；特性，常指好的品质。"},{"word":"attribute","ipa":"/ˈætrɪbjuːt/","tag":"assigned quality","definition":"a quality or feature regarded as part of something.","definitionCN":"属性；被视作某物一部分的品质。"},{"word":"property","ipa":"/ˈprɒpəti/","tag":"natural quality","definition":"a quality that belongs naturally to something.","definitionCN":"性质；固有属性。"},{"word":"peculiarity","ipa":"/pɪˌkjuːliˈærəti/","tag":"odd feature","definition":"a strange or distinctive feature.","definitionCN":"古怪之处；独特特征。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: the Greek mark kharaktēr, the character family, and the scientific use of a characteristic curve.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：希腊语记号 kharaktēr、character 词族，以及 characteristic curve 的科学用法。"},"normal":[{"en":"character and characteristic share the Greek mark: kharaktēr is an engraved stamp, and a character in a play is stamped with certain qualities.","cn":"character 与 characteristic 共享那个希腊记号：kharaktēr 是刻下的印章，戏剧里的角色则被印上某些品质。"},{"en":"characteristically is the adverb of the signature: what a person does 'in character'.","cn":"characteristically 是“签名”的副词：一个人“合乎本性”地做事。"},{"en":"uncharacteristic = un- + characteristic: the mark is missing, so the behaviour surprises us.","cn":"uncharacteristic = un- + characteristic：记号不见了，所以那行为让我们吃惊。"},{"en":"a characteristic curve in science is a line that marks how a device behaves — the same 'mark' idea made measurable.","cn":"科学里的 characteristic curve 是标出器件行为的曲线——同一个“记号”概念变得可测量。"},{"en":"characterize means to stamp something with its marks, either by describing it or by being typical of it.","cn":"characterize 是给某物盖上它的记号，或者通过描述，或者通过本身具有代表性。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"A characteristic is a mark read in two directions: outward it identifies a class, inward it reveals a person.","cn":"characteristic 是一个可以双向读的记号：向外辨认一个类别，向内揭示一个人。"},{"en":"The history moves from a physical engraved sign to an invisible defining quality, then to a measurable property in science.","cn":"历史从有形的刻痕走到无形的界定品质，再走到科学中可测量的性质。"},{"en":"So recognisability is the core: every sense answers the question 'by what mark do I know this?'","cn":"所以可辨认性是核心：每个义项都在回答“我凭什么记号认出这个？”"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Curiosity is a characteristic shared by most scientists.","cn":"好奇心是大多数科学家共有的一个特征。"},{"en":"It is characteristic of him to help without being asked.","cn":"不等人开口就帮忙，是他一贯的作风。"},{"en":"The two species differ in several physical characteristics.","cn":"这两个物种在若干身体特征上有所不同。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“卡拉克特”——卡片上刻着特有的记号，一眼就能认出 → characteristic 特征、特有的","word":"characteristic"},"root":"源自希腊语 kharaktēr“刻下的记号”，经拉丁语 character 进入英语；核心是“用来辨认的印记”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of characteristic, all built on a mark: the mark identifies a thing, a class, a person's habit, a species, a number, or a place.","cn":"characteristic 的八个义项都建立在“记号”上：记号可以辨认一个事物、一个类别、一个人的习惯、一个物种、一个数，或一个地方。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: an engraved mark that tells you what something is.","cn":"核心意象：一个刻下的记号，告诉你这是什么。"},"chain":["ENGRAVE A MARK","IMPRINT ON A THING","DEFINING QUALITY","TYPICAL OF A CLASS","SIGNATURE OF A PERSON","MEASURABLE PROPERTY"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S7","en":"THE MARK ON A THING OR PERSON: one trait identifies the kind, and one trait stands out inside a character.","cn":"事物或人身上的记号：一项特征辨认类别，一项特征在性格内部凸显出来。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"THE MARK POINTS OUTWARD OR INWARD: typical of a whole class, or the signature of one person's habit.","cn":"记号或向外或向内：既是整个类别的典型，也是一个人习惯的签名。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"THE MARK MADE TECHNICAL: a species trait in biology, and the integer part that fixes a logarithm's place.","cn":"记号变得技术化：生物学里的物种性状，以及固定对数量级的整数部分。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"THE MARKS COLLECTED: the plural turns separate traits into the profile of a place.","cn":"记号被收集：复数把分散的特征变成一个地方的整体画像。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"THE MARK IN ACTION: the adverb applies the signature to the way something is done.","cn":"记号落在动作上：副词把“签名”用到做事的方式上。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Characteristic is character plus -istic, and the whole family circles the Greek mark kharaktēr: character, characterize, characterization, characteristically, uncharacteristic.","cn":"characteristic 是 character 加 -istic，整个词族都围着希腊语记号 kharaktēr 转：character、characterize、characterization、characteristically、uncharacteristic。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Greek kharaktēr 'engraved mark' passed into Latin as character and into English as character; the suffix -istic comes from Greek -istikos, so characteristic literally means 'of the mark'.","cn":"希腊语 kharaktēr“刻下的记号”经拉丁语 character 进入英语的 character；后缀 -istic 来自希腊语 -istikos，所以 characteristic 字面上就是“属于记号的”。"},"items":[{"word":"characteristic","structure":"character + -istic (Greek -istikos)","meaning":"typical; a distinctive trait","meaningCN":"特有的；特征（-istic 构成形容词兼名词）","example":"Patience is his most characteristic quality.","exampleCN":"耐心是他最典型的品质。"},{"word":"character","structure":"Greek kharaktēr (engraved mark)","meaning":"the qualities of a person; a symbol","meaningCN":"性格；角色；字符（来自希腊语“刻痕”）","example":"The novel has a strong central character.","exampleCN":"这部小说有一个强有力的中心人物。"},{"word":"characterize","structure":"character + -ize (verb)","meaning":"to describe or be typical of","meaningCN":"描绘特点；以……为特征（-ize 构成动词）","example":"Long dry summers characterize the region.","exampleCN":"漫长干燥的夏季是这个地区的特点。"},{"word":"characterization","structure":"characterize + -ation (noun)","meaning":"the act of describing qualities","meaningCN":"刻画；描述（-ation 构成名词）","example":"The film's characterization of the hero is subtle.","exampleCN":"影片对主人公的刻画很细腻。"},{"word":"characteristically","structure":"characteristic + -ally (adverb)","meaning":"in a typical way","meaningCN":"典型地；一贯地（-ally 构成副词）","example":"She was characteristically early.","exampleCN":"她一如既往地到得早。"},{"word":"uncharacteristic","structure":"un- (not) + characteristic","meaning":"not typical","meaningCN":"反常的；非典型的（un- 表否定）","example":"His anger was quite uncharacteristic.","exampleCN":"他发火很反常。"},{"word":"characterless","structure":"character + -less (without)","meaning":"without distinctive qualities","meaningCN":"无特色的（-less 表没有）","example":"The street was ugly and characterless.","exampleCN":"那条街又丑又没特色。"},{"word":"realistic","structure":"real + -istic (suffix example)","meaning":"seeming true to life","meaningCN":"逼真的；现实的（-istic 后缀例词）","example":"The painting is remarkably realistic.","exampleCN":"这幅画非常逼真。"},{"word":"artistic","structure":"art + -istic (suffix example)","meaning":"relating to art","meaningCN":"艺术的（-istic 后缀例词）","example":"The room shows her artistic taste.","exampleCN":"这个房间显示了她的艺术品味。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"kharaktēr","structure":"Greek kharaktēr (noun)","meaning":"engraved mark; instrument for marking","meaningCN":"刻下的记号；刻印工具"},{"word":"kharassein","structure":"Greek verb","meaning":"to engrave","meaningCN":"刻；雕"},{"word":"kharaktēristikos","structure":"kharaktēr + -istikos","meaning":"of or indicating character","meaningCN":"属于或标示特征的"}]}},{"word":"circumstance","ipa_uk":"/ˈsɜːkəmstəns/","ipa_us":"/ˈsɜːrkəmstæns/","definition_zh":"情况；环境；境况；细节；排场","definition_en":"a condition or fact that surrounds and affects an event; also the surrounding situation of a person's life","core_image":"一圈人围着你站，他们不说什么，却决定了你此刻能怎么走","scene":"律师翻看案卷说：Under these circumstances, we should postpone the hearing.","sceneCN":"这里 circumstance 是「情况、情形」（第 1 个义项：围绕并影响事件的条件，常用复数）；句意：在这种情况下，我们应该推迟听证。图中可辨识物件：案卷、会议桌、日历、律师。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"情况；环境；境况；细节；（复数）境遇"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"under the circumstances","zh":"在这种情况下"},{"phrase":"under no circumstances","zh":"决不；无论如何都不"},{"phrase":"in reduced circumstances","zh":"生活拮据"},{"phrase":"extenuating circumstances","zh":"可减轻处罚的情节"},{"phrase":"a victim of circumstance","zh":"环境的受害者"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"circumstances"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"circumstantial","pos":"adj.","zh":"依情况而定的；间接的"},{"word":"circumstantially","pos":"adv.","zh":"间接地；依情况地"},{"word":"circumstantiate","pos":"v.","zh":"用细节证实；详细说明"},{"word":"circumstances","pos":"n.","zh":"境况；经济状况"},{"word":"happenstance","pos":"n.","zh":"偶然事件；机缘"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Conditions around an event: the situation as it stands","titleCN":"情况：围绕事件的处境","definition":"the conditions and facts that surround an event and affect how it is judged","definitionCN":"围绕某一事件并影响其判断的条件与事实","example":"Under these circumstances, postponing the match was the only sensible choice.","exampleCN":"在这种情况下，推迟比赛是唯一明智的选择。","why":"Latin circumstare meant 'stand around'. The facts that stand around an event are exactly what circumstance names: they are not the event itself, but they press on it.","whyCN":"拉丁语 circumstare 意为“站在周围”。围绕一个事件站着的那些事实，正是 circumstance 所指：它们不是事件本身，却在挤压事件。"},{"no":"02","title":"A particular fact: one detail in the case","titleCN":"具体事实：案件中的一个细节","definition":"a single fact or detail that is part of a situation","definitionCN":"构成某一情境的单个事实或细节","example":"The police recorded every circumstance of the accident.","exampleCN":"警方记录了这起事故的每一个细节。","why":"C. 1300 used the word for 'a particular detail'. One of the facts standing around an event can be picked out and counted on its own.","whyCN":"约 1300 年，这个词就指“某一具体细节”。围着事件站着的诸多事实中，可以单独挑出一个来计数。"},{"no":"03","title":"Surroundings: the conditions of life around a person","titleCN":"环境：一个人生活周围的条件","definition":"the conditions in which someone lives or works, especially their environment","definitionCN":"某人生活或工作所处的条件，尤指环境","example":"Children growing up in poor circumstances need more support.","exampleCN":"在贫困环境中长大的孩子需要更多支持。","why":"From mid-14c. circumstance meant 'a person's surroundings, environment'. The literal circle around a place became the social and material world around a life.","whyCN":"从 14 世纪中期起，circumstance 指“一个人的周边环境”。围绕一个地点的字面圆圈，变成了围绕一条生命的社会与物质世界。"},{"no":"04","title":"Means: the state of one's finances","titleCN":"境况：一个人的经济状况","definition":"in the plural, a person's material welfare or financial position","definitionCN":"复数形式指一个人的物质福利或经济状况","example":"After the war the family lived in reduced circumstances.","exampleCN":"战后这家人生活拮据。","why":"Circumstances in the plural came to mean 'condition of life, material welfare' by 1704. What surrounds a life includes the money and comfort it can reach.","whyCN":"复数 circumstances 在 1704 年取得“生活状况、物质福利”之义。环绕一条生命的东西，也包括它能触及的金钱与舒适。"},{"no":"05","title":"Non-essential detail: the part that does not matter","titleCN":"次要细节：不影响本质的部分","definition":"a detail that does not affect the essential nature of something","definitionCN":"不影响某事物本质的细节","example":"The essential point was buried under a mass of circumstances.","exampleCN":"要点被一大堆次要细节埋住了。","why":"From the 1590s circumstance could mean 'that which is non-essential'. A fact that only stands around the core can be stripped away without changing the core.","whyCN":"自 16 世纪 90 年代起，circumstance 可指“非本质之物”。只在外围站着的事实可以被剥掉，而核心不变。"},{"no":"06","title":"Pomp and circumstance: ceremony and show","titleCN":"排场与仪式：典礼的铺张","definition":"in the fixed phrase pomp and circumstance, ceremonial display and formal show","definitionCN":"用于固定短语 pomp and circumstance，指典礼的排场与仪式感","example":"The graduation was full of pomp and circumstance.","exampleCN":"毕业典礼充满了排场与仪式感。","why":"A late 14c. sense 'formality about an important event, ceremonious accompaniment' survived in Shakespeare's phrase pomp and circumstance. Ceremony is the decorative circle drawn around an event.","whyCN":"14 世纪后期有“重大事件的礼仪、仪式性伴随物”一义，活在莎士比亚的短语 pomp and circumstance 里。仪式就是给事件画上的那圈装饰。"},{"no":"07","title":"Under no circumstances: in no possible case","titleCN":"决不：没有任何一种情况可以","definition":"in the phrase under no circumstances, used to mean never, whatever the situation","definitionCN":"用于短语 under no circumstances，表示无论何种情况都绝不","example":"Under no circumstances should you share this password.","exampleCN":"在任何情况下你都不应分享这个密码。","why":"A circumstance is a possible surrounding condition. Saying 'under no circumstances' closes every one of those conditions: there is no situation in which the act is allowed.","whyCN":"circumstance 是一种可能的环境条件。“under no circumstances”把所有这些条件逐一关上：没有任何处境允许这个行为。"},{"no":"08","title":"Extenuating circumstances: facts that lessen blame","titleCN":"减责情节：可减轻罪责的事实","definition":"in law, the facts of a case that may reduce the seriousness of an offence","definitionCN":"法律上可能减轻罪行严重程度的情节","example":"The judge took the extenuating circumstances into account.","exampleCN":"法官考虑了可减轻处罚的情节。","why":"A case is judged together with what stood around it. The circumstances are the surrounding facts that make the same act more or less blameworthy.","whyCN":"判案要连同案件周围的东西一起看。这些 circumstance 就是围绕的事实，它们让同一个行为变得更该责或更不该责。"},{"no":"09","title":"Victim of circumstance: what you did not choose","titleCN":"环境的受害者：并非自选的条件","definition":"in the phrase a victim of circumstance, a person harmed by conditions they did not control","definitionCN":"用于短语 a victim of circumstance，指被自己无法控制的条件所害的人","example":"He insists he is a victim of circumstance, not a criminal.","exampleCN":"他坚持自己是环境的受害者，而不是罪犯。","why":"Conditions that stand around you were not chosen by you. When those conditions do the harm, circumstance shades into chance, and the person is acted upon rather than acting.","whyCN":"围在你身边的条件并非你所选。当这些条件造成伤害时，circumstance 就带上“机缘”的色彩，人成了被作用的一方，而不是行动者。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Circumstance joins circum 'around' to stare 'stand': the things that stand around an event. Latin circumstantia was a loan-translation of Greek peristasis, and English borrowed the word around 1200.","cn":"circumstance 把 circum“周围”和 stare“站”合在一起：站在一个事件周围的东西。拉丁语 circumstantia 是对希腊语 peristasis 的仿译，英语约 1200 年借入。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Circumstare meant 'stand around, surround, encompass, occupy', from circum 'around' plus stare 'to stand'. The image is a ring of things posted around a point.","cn":"circumstare 意为“站在周围、环绕、包围、占据”，由 circum“周围”加 stare“站”构成。画面是一圈东西被布置在一个点的四周。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Stare is traced to PIE *sta- 'to stand, make or be firm'. The root is a reconstruction without direct written record, so this deepest layer is source uncertain.","cn":"stare 被追溯到原始印欧语 *sta-“站立、使牢固”。该词根是重构形式，没有直接书面记录，故这一最深层为“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"LATIN (circumstantia)","en":"Circumstantia meant 'surrounding condition', the neuter plural of circumstans, present participle of circumstare. The Latin word is a loan-translation of Greek peristasis.","cn":"circumstantia 意为“周围的条件”，是 circumstare 的现在分词 circumstans 的中性复数。这个拉丁词是对希腊语 peristasis 的仿译。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (13c.)","en":"Circonstance meant 'circumstance, situation', and literally 'outskirts'. The literal spatial sense and the abstract sense travelled together.","cn":"circonstance 意为“情况、处境”，字面上还指“外围、郊区”。字面的空间义和抽象义一起传了过来。"},{"era":"c. 1200 ENGLISH","en":"The first English sense was 'a fact related to another fact and modifying it without affecting its essential nature', first used of sins. By c. 1300 it also meant 'a particular detail'; mid-14c. added 'a person's surroundings'.","cn":"英语最早的意思是“与另一事实相关、在不改变其本质的前提下修饰它的事实”，最初用于罪。到约 1300 年也指“某一具体细节”；14 世纪中期又添“一个人的周边环境”。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The 1590s added 'that which is non-essential', and 1704 gave circumstances the sense 'condition of life, material welfare'. Pomp and circumstance comes from Shakespeare, and circumstantial evidence is recorded from 1691.","cn":"16 世纪 90 年代添“非本质之物”，1704 年复数 circumstances 取得“生活状况、物质福利”义。pomp and circumstance 出自莎士比亚，circumstantial evidence 记录于 1691 年。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling and the shared circum- element, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写和共同的 circum- 成分挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"circumstances","ipa":"/ˈsɜːkəmstənsɪz/","tag":"plural form","definition":"the plural of circumstance, often meaning the conditions of life.","definitionCN":"circumstance 的复数，常指生活境况。"},{"word":"circumstantial","ipa":"/ˌsɜːkəmˈstænʃl/","tag":"derived adjective","definition":"based on surrounding facts rather than direct proof; also detailed.","definitionCN":"基于旁证的；间接的；也有“详细”之意。"},{"word":"circumference","ipa":"/səˈkʌmfərəns/","tag":"shared circum-","definition":"the distance around a circle. It shares circum- 'around' but uses ferre 'carry'.","definitionCN":"圆周；周长。同样有 circum-“周围”，但词根是 ferre“携带”。"},{"word":"circumstantiate","ipa":"/ˌsɜːkəmˈstænʃieɪt/","tag":"derived verb","definition":"to support a statement with details.","definitionCN":"用细节证实；详细说明。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"situation","ipa":"/ˌsɪtʃuˈeɪʃn/","tag":"state of affairs","definition":"the set of conditions at a particular time.","definitionCN":"某一时刻的整体情况。"},{"word":"condition","ipa":"/kənˈdɪʃn/","tag":"factor","definition":"the state something is in, or a factor that affects it.","definitionCN":"状态；影响因素。"},{"word":"context","ipa":"/ˈkɒntekst/","tag":"surrounding frame","definition":"the situation around something that helps explain it.","definitionCN":"语境；帮助理解某事的周围情境。"},{"word":"setting","ipa":"/ˈsetɪŋ/","tag":"place and time","definition":"the place and circumstances in which something happens.","definitionCN":"背景；某事发生的地点与情境。"},{"word":"surroundings","ipa":"/səˈraʊndɪŋz/","tag":"physical environment","definition":"everything around a person or place.","definitionCN":"周围环境；四周的事物。"},{"word":"environment","ipa":"/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt/","tag":"natural or social conditions","definition":"the natural or social conditions around someone.","definitionCN":"自然环境；社会环境。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: circum- 'around' plus stare 'stand', the plural sense of finances from 1704, and the legal phrase extenuating circumstances.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：circum-“周围”加 stare“站”、1704 年来的复数“财力”义，以及法律短语 extenuating circumstances。"},"normal":[{"en":"circumstance = circum- 'around' + stare 'stand': the facts literally stand around the event.","cn":"circumstance = circum-“周围”+ stare“站”：事实就字面地站在事件四周。"},{"en":"circumstances in the plural means money by 1704: what stands around a life includes its comfort.","cn":"复数 circumstances 在 1704 年已指钱财：围在一条生命周围的东西，也包括它的舒适。"},{"en":"circumstantial evidence is built from facts standing around a case, not from a direct witness.","cn":"circumstantial evidence 由围在案件四周的事实拼成，而不是来自直接目击者。"},{"en":"pomp and circumstance: ceremony is decoration drawn in a circle around an important event.","cn":"pomp and circumstance：仪式就是围着一件大事画出的那圈装饰。"},{"en":"under no circumstances closes every circle of possibility, so it means never.","cn":"under no circumstances 把每一种可能性的圈都关上，所以意思是“决不”。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The word is spatial before it is social: first a ring of things around a point, then a ring of conditions around an event.","cn":"这个词先有空间义，后有社会义：起初是一圈东西围着一个点，后来是一圈条件围着一个事件。"},{"en":"The ring can shrink to one detail or widen to a whole life; it can be essential or dispensable, chosen or imposed.","cn":"这个圈可以缩成一个细节，也可以扩成一条生活；可以是本质的或可弃的，可以是自选的或强加的。"},{"en":"So situation, detail, environment, means, ceremony and chance are one circle viewed at different radii.","cn":"所以“情况、细节、环境、财力、仪式、机缘”是同一个圆圈在不同半径上的样子。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"We cannot judge him without knowing the circumstances.","cn":"不了解具体情况，我们就无法评判他。"},{"en":"Under no circumstances should the door be left open.","cn":"无论如何都不应让那扇门开着。"},{"en":"The ceremony was conducted with great pomp and circumstance.","cn":"典礼办得排场十足。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“色康stance”——四周（circum）站（stance）着一圈人，就是你的处境 → circumstance 情况、环境","word":"circumstance"},"root":"源自拉丁语 circumstare“站在周围”（circum 周围 + stare 站），经古法语 circonstance 进入英语；核心是“围在事件四周的条件”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of circumstance, all from one picture: things standing around an event. The ring can be a detail, a life, a bank balance, a ceremony, or a fate.","cn":"circumstance 的九个义项都来自同一幅画：围着事件站着的东西。这个圈可以是一个细节、一条生活、一份存款、一场仪式，或一种命运。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a ring of conditions standing around an event.","cn":"核心意象：一圈条件站在事件的四周。"},"chain":["STAND AROUND","FORM A RING","SURROUNDINGS","CONDITIONS OF AN EVENT","PARTICULAR DETAIL","CHANCE OR FATE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S8","en":"THE RING JUDGES THE EVENT: conditions decide what is possible, and in law they decide how blameworthy an act is.","cn":"条件圈决定事件：条件决定什么可能，在法律上则决定一个行为该受多少责。"},{"senses":"S2 · S5","en":"THE RING SHRINKS: one fact can be picked out as a detail, or dismissed as non-essential.","cn":"圆圈缩小：一个事实可以被挑成细节，也可以被当作非本质之物丢掉。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"THE RING WIDENS TO A LIFE: surroundings become the social world, and then the financial means one lives on.","cn":"圆圈扩到一条生活：环境变成社会世界，再变成赖以生活的财力。"},{"senses":"S6 · S7","en":"THE RING AS DISPLAY AND AS CLOSURE: ceremony draws a decorative circle, while under no circumstances closes every one.","cn":"圆圈既是展示也是封闭：仪式画出装饰的一圈，under no circumstances 则把每一圈都关上。"},{"senses":"S9","en":"THE RING AS FATE: conditions you did not choose can act on you, and circumstance becomes chance.","cn":"圆圈成为命运：你未选择的条件会作用于你，circumstance 也就带上了“机缘”义。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Circumstance splits cleanly into circum- 'around' and the stare family 'stand'. The prefix also appears in circumference and circumnavigate, and the root in constant, status and stable.","cn":"circumstance 可以干净地拆成 circum-“周围”和 stare 词族“站”。前缀还出现在 circumference、circumnavigate，词根还出现在 constant、status、stable。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin circumstare 'stand around' joins circum 'around' to stare 'stand'; circumstantia 'surrounding condition' is a loan-translation of Greek peristasis, and the same stare underlies constant and status.","cn":"拉丁语 circumstare“站在周围”把 circum“周围”接到 stare“站”上；circumstantia“周围的条件”是对希腊语 peristasis 的仿译，同一个 stare 也是 constant 和 status 的基础。"},"items":[{"word":"circumstance","structure":"circum- (around) + stare (stand) + -ance (noun)","meaning":"a condition standing around an event","meaningCN":"情况；环境（circum- 周围 + stare 站 + -ance 名词）","example":"The circumstances forced us to change the plan.","exampleCN":"情况迫使我们改变计划。"},{"word":"circumstantial","structure":"circumstant- + -ial (adjective)","meaning":"based on surrounding facts; detailed","meaningCN":"基于旁证的；间接的（-ial 构成形容词）","example":"The case rested on circumstantial evidence.","exampleCN":"这案子靠间接证据支撑。"},{"word":"circumstantially","structure":"circumstantial + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"by surrounding facts; indirectly","meaningCN":"间接地；依情况地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The claim was proved only circumstantially.","exampleCN":"这一主张只是间接地被证明。"},{"word":"circumstantiate","structure":"circumstant- + -ate (verb)","meaning":"to prove by details","meaningCN":"用细节证实（-ate 构成动词）","example":"He circumstantiated his account with dates.","exampleCN":"他用日期来佐证自己的叙述。"},{"word":"circumstances","structure":"circumstance + -s (plural)","meaning":"conditions of life; financial position","meaningCN":"境况；经济状况（复数形式）","example":"They lived in modest circumstances.","exampleCN":"他们过着简朴的生活。"},{"word":"circumference","structure":"circum- (around) + ferre (carry) + -ence","meaning":"the line around a circle","meaningCN":"圆周；周长（circum- + ferre 携带）","example":"The circumference of the circle is ten metres.","exampleCN":"这个圆的周长是十米。"},{"word":"circumnavigate","structure":"circum- (around) + navigate (sail)","meaning":"to sail around","meaningCN":"环航（circum- 周围 + navigate 航行）","example":"They circumnavigated the globe by boat.","exampleCN":"他们乘船环航了地球。"},{"word":"circumspect","structure":"circum- (around) + specere (look)","meaning":"looking around; cautious","meaningCN":"谨慎的（circum- 周围 + specere 看）","example":"She was circumspect about the offer.","exampleCN":"她对那个提议持谨慎态度。"},{"word":"constant","structure":"con- (together) + stare (stand) + -ant","meaning":"standing firm; unchanging","meaningCN":"不变的；持续的（con- 一起 + stare 站）","example":"The machine needs a constant temperature.","exampleCN":"这台机器需要恒定的温度。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"circumstare","structure":"circum + stare","meaning":"to stand around, surround","meaningCN":"站在周围；环绕"},{"word":"circumstantia","structure":"circumstans + -ia","meaning":"surrounding condition","meaningCN":"周围的条件；情况"},{"word":"stare","structure":"stare (verb)","meaning":"to stand","meaningCN":"站；立"}]}},{"word":"cite","ipa_uk":"/saɪt/","ipa_us":"/saɪt/","definition_zh":"引用；引证；援引；传唤；表彰","definition_en":"to quote a passage, mention as evidence, or call someone officially to appear","core_image":"把一段话或一个人从背景里叫出来，让他站到你的论点前面","scene":"论文答辩时，导师指着段落说：You must cite the original study, not just its conclusion.","sceneCN":"这里 cite 是「引用、引证」（第 1、2 个义项：把原文或研究作为证据叫进论证）；句意：你必须引用那项原始研究，而不只是它的结论。图中可辨识物件：论文稿、荧光笔、脚注编号、答辩投影。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"引用；引证；举出（例子、证据）"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"援引（判例、法条、权威）"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"传唤；开罚单；通报表彰"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"cite a passage","zh":"引用一段文字"},{"phrase":"cite sources","zh":"标注并引用出处"},{"phrase":"cite an example","zh":"举出一个例子"},{"phrase":"cite a precedent","zh":"援引先例"},{"phrase":"be cited for bravery","zh":"因英勇受到通报表彰"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单","form":"cites"},{"label":"过去式","form":"cited"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"cited"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"citing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"citation","pos":"n.","zh":"引文；引证；传票；嘉奖令"},{"word":"citable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可引用的；值得引证的"},{"word":"recite","pos":"v.","zh":"背诵；朗诵；列举"},{"word":"incite","pos":"v.","zh":"煽动；激起"},{"word":"excite","pos":"v.","zh":"使兴奋；激起"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Quote a passage word for word","titleCN":"引用原文：把别人的句子叫进自己的文章","definition":"to quote a passage from a book or speech, usually to support what you are saying","definitionCN":"引用书文或讲话中的段落，通常用以支持自己的论述","example":"She cited a line from Orwell to open her essay.","exampleCN":"她引用奥威尔的一句话来开篇。","why":"Latin citare meant to call or summon. Quoting is summoning the exact words out of their old page and making them speak again in a new argument.","whyCN":"拉丁语 citare 本义是“叫、召”。引用就是把原话从旧书页里叫出来，让它在新的论证中重新开口。"},{"no":"02","title":"Adduce: bring evidence into the argument","titleCN":"引证：把证据调进论证现场","definition":"to mention a study, fact or example as proof for a claim","definitionCN":"提及某项研究、事实或例子，作为主张的证据","example":"The report cites three surveys that point to the same trend.","exampleCN":"这份报告引用了三项指向同一趋势的调查。","why":"The thing summoned here is not a sentence but a witness: a study is called forward to stand beside the claim and support it.","whyCN":"这里叫出来的不是一句话，而是一个证人：研究被召到主张旁边，替它作证。"},{"no":"03","title":"invoke a precedent or authority","titleCN":"援引：请出判例或权威为自己站台","definition":"to refer to a previous case, law or authority as a reason for a decision","definitionCN":"援引先前的判例、法条或权威，作为裁决依据","example":"The lawyer cited a 1998 ruling in the court's favour.","exampleCN":"律师援引了一份 1998 年的裁决，支持本院的立场。","why":"A precedent is a past voice that still has power. Citing it calls that old decision into the present case so that it can rule again.","whyCN":"先例是仍然有力量的旧声音。援引它，就是把过去的裁决叫进眼前的案件，让它再次发言。"},{"no":"04","title":"Summon to appear in court","titleCN":"传唤：让一个人到庭","definition":"to order someone to appear before a court","definitionCN":"命令某人到法庭出庭","example":"The defendant was cited to appear on the tenth of May.","exampleCN":"被告被传唤于五月十日到庭。","why":"This is the oldest English sense, straight from the Latin summons: a court calls a person forward by name until he stands in the room.","whyCN":"这是英语里最古老的义项，直接承自拉丁语的“传召”：法庭点名把人叫出来，直到他站进法庭。"},{"no":"05","title":"Issue a ticket: call someone out for an offence","titleCN":"开罚单：因违规把人“叫出来”","definition":"to officially name someone as having broken a rule, especially in traffic","definitionCN":"正式指认某人违规，尤指交通违章开罚单","example":"He was cited for driving without a licence.","exampleCN":"他因无证驾驶被开单传唤。","why":"The police citation is a written call: the state names you, records the offence, and summons you to answer for it.","whyCN":"警察开的 citation 是一声书面呼唤：国家点你的名、记下违规，再召你来说明。"},{"no":"06","title":"Mention in dispatches: name someone for honour","titleCN":"通报表彰：把名字叫到队伍前面","definition":"to mention a soldier or unit officially for brave action","definitionCN":"正式提及士兵或部队的英勇行为以示表彰","example":"Two medics were cited for rescuing the wounded under fire.","exampleCN":"两名医护因在火线抢救伤员而受到通报表彰。","why":"In a dispatch the commander reads names aloud. To be cited is to be called out of the ranks and placed before everyone as an example.","whyCN":"战报里指挥官要念出名字。be cited 就是从队列里被叫出来，摆到所有人面前作为榜样。"},{"no":"07","title":"Name a source in a footnote","titleCN":"标注出处：让来源在页脚留名","definition":"to give the exact source of information in a footnote or bibliography","definitionCN":"在脚注或参考文献中给出信息的准确来源","example":"Every chart in the article must cite its data source.","exampleCN":"文中每张图表都必须标注数据来源。","why":"A footnote is the place where the summoned source is made to stand: the reader can see who was called and where the words came from.","whyCN":"脚注就是被召来的来源站立的位置：读者能看见叫来的是谁、原话出自哪里。"},{"no":"08","title":"Call forth or evoke (archaic)","titleCN":"召唤、唤起：把看不见的力量叫出来（古义）","definition":"to call forth a spirit, feeling or power; an older literary use","definitionCN":"召唤鬼魂、情感或力量；较古老的文学用法","example":"The old rite was said to cite the spirits of the dead.","exampleCN":"据说那套古老仪式能召唤亡者的灵魂。","why":"Citare also meant to set in motion and rouse. Before it named quoting, the word could call a spirit out of silence, which is the root of excite and incite.","whyCN":"citare 还有“使动起来、激起”之意。在它表示“引用”之前，这个词能把亡灵从沉默中叫出，这也正是 excite、incite 的根源。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Cite comes from Latin citare, a frequentative of ciere 'to set in motion, call'. English first used it for a court summons, then for calling words and names forward.","cn":"cite 来自拉丁语 citare，是 ciere“使动、叫”的反复态。英语先用它指法庭传召，后来才用来把文字和名字叫到前面。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Citare meant 'to summon, urge, call; put in sudden motion, rouse'. It was a frequentative of ciere 'to move, set in motion, call, invite'.","cn":"citare 意为“传召、催促、呼叫；使突然运动、激起”，是 ciere“使动、叫、邀请”的反复态。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"The root is given as PIE *keie- 'to set in motion, move to and fro'. The starred form is a reconstruction with no written record, so this deepest layer is source uncertain.","cn":"其词根被列为原始印欧语 *keie-“使动、来回移动”。带星号的形式是重构，没有书面记录，故最深层来源不确定。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (14C)","en":"Old French citer 'to summon' carried the legal sense into English; the quotation sense was not yet part of it.","cn":"古法语的 citer“传召”把法律义带进英语，当时还没有“引用”这一义。"},{"era":"MID-15C ENGLISH","en":"English cite is recorded mid-15c. as 'to summon, call upon officially'. The court sense is therefore the word's English starting point.","cn":"英语 cite 记录于 15 世纪中期，意为“传召、正式召唤”。因此法庭义才是这个词在英语里的起点。"},{"era":"1530s ENGLISH","en":"The sense 'call forth a passage of writing, quote the words of another' is first attested in the 1530s, moving the summons from people to texts.","cn":"“叫出一段文字、引用他人原话”这一义最早记录于 16 世纪 30 年代，把“召唤”的对象从人转到了文本。"},{"era":"1540s–MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Citation 'a quoted passage' appears in the 1540s. Modern English adds the police citation and the military mention in dispatches, both written forms of calling someone forward.","cn":"citation“被引用的段落”出现于 16 世纪 40 年代。现代英语又加上警察罚单与军队通报，两者都是“把人叫出来”的书面形式。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group shares the sound /saɪt/ or the cit- stem; the second group shares the act of bringing words or evidence forward.","cn":"第一组共享读音 /saɪt/ 或 cit- 词干；第二组共享“把文字或证据提到前面”的动作。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"site","ipa":"/saɪt/","tag":"homophone","definition":"a place where something is built or happens. It sounds exactly like cite but has no calling in it.","definitionCN":"地点；场地。与 cite 完全同音，但毫无“召唤”之意。"},{"word":"sight","ipa":"/saɪt/","tag":"homophone","definition":"the ability to see, or something seen. Another /saɪt/ word, kept apart only by spelling.","definitionCN":"视力；景象。又一个读 /saɪt/ 的词，只靠拼写区分。"},{"word":"recite","ipa":"/rɪˈsaɪt/","tag":"same Latin stem","definition":"to say a text aloud from memory. Its re- means 'again': calling the words back.","definitionCN":"背诵；朗诵。前缀 re- 表示“再次”，即把文字重新叫回来。"},{"word":"incite","ipa":"/ɪnˈsaɪt/","tag":"same Latin stem","definition":"to stir people into violent or unlawful action. The in- turns the call inward, into a crowd's feelings.","definitionCN":"煽动；激起。in- 把“叫”转向人群内部的情感。"},{"word":"excite","ipa":"/ɪkˈsaɪt/","tag":"same Latin stem","definition":"to make someone eager or agitated. Ex- 'out' plus citare: call the energy out.","definitionCN":"使兴奋；激起。ex-“向外”加 citare：把能量叫出来。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"quote","ipa":"/kwəʊt/","tag":"verbatim","definition":"to repeat someone's exact words. It is the everyday word for the quotation sense of cite.","definitionCN":"引用；引述。它是 cite 表“引用原话”时最日常的说法。"},{"word":"adduce","ipa":"/əˈdjuːs/","tag":"evidence","definition":"to bring forward a fact or example as evidence. It is the formal word for citing proof.","definitionCN":"引证；举出（证据）。它是“引证证据”的正式说法。"},{"word":"mention","ipa":"/ˈmenʃn/","tag":"name","definition":"to refer to something briefly. It names without necessarily quoting or proving.","definitionCN":"提及。它只点名，不一定引用或举证。"},{"word":"summon","ipa":"/ˈsʌmən/","tag":"call a person","definition":"to order someone to come. It is the direct everyday equivalent of cite in its court sense.","definitionCN":"传唤；召唤。它直接对应 cite 的法庭义。"},{"word":"reference","ipa":"/ˈrefrəns/","tag":"point to","definition":"to point a reader to a source. It covers the footnote side of citing.","definitionCN":"参考；引用。它覆盖 citing 中“标注出处”的一面。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: the Latin stem cit- 'call', the re-/in-/ex- family, and the citation forms English actually uses.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁词干 cit-“叫”、re-/in-/ex- 词族，以及英语实际使用的 citation 系列。"},"normal":[{"en":"cite, site and sight all say /saɪt/; only cite has the c of Latin citare, 'to call'.","cn":"cite、site、sight 都读 /saɪt/；只有 cite 带着拉丁语 citare“叫”的那个 c。"},{"en":"citation = cit- 'call' + -ation: the act of calling a passage or a person forward.","cn":"citation = cit-“叫”+ -ation：把一段文字或一个人叫到前面的行为。"},{"en":"recite = re- 'again' + cite: call the text back again out of memory.","cn":"recite = re-“再次”+ cite：把课文从记忆里重新叫回来。"},{"en":"incite = in- 'into' + cite: call a feeling into someone until they act.","cn":"incite = in-“进入”+ cite：把情绪叫进某人心里，直到他行动。"},{"en":"A citation in a paper and a citation from a traffic officer are both a call: one calls a source, the other calls you to account.","cn":"论文里的 citation 和交警开的 citation 都是一声“召唤”：一个叫来源，一个叫你来担责。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Every sense is one gesture: something is called out of the background and made to stand in front.","cn":"所有义项都是同一个动作：把某物从背景里叫出来，让它站到前面。"},{"en":"Only the summoned object changes: a sentence, a study, a precedent, a defendant, a soldier's name.","cn":"变的只是被叫出来的对象：一句话、一项研究、一个判例、一名被告、一个士兵的名字。"},{"en":"Quoting summons words, a subpoena summons a body, and a commendation summons a name into the record.","cn":"引用召唤文字，传票召唤身体，嘉奖则把一个名字召进档案。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Please cite the page number when you quote the report.","cn":"引用这份报告时请注明页码。"},{"en":"The professor cited two studies to support her argument.","cn":"教授引用了两项研究来支持她的论点。"},{"en":"The driver was cited for speeding near the school gate.","cn":"那名司机因在学校门口超速被开单。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"近音记忆 · 非词源","text":"cite 读作“赛特”：把赛过特别的原文请出来作证 → cite 引用、引证","word":"cite"},"root":"源自拉丁语 citare“传召、呼叫、使动”（ciere 的反复态），词干 cit- 意为“叫”，核心是“把某物或某人叫到前面”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of cite, all one act of calling forward: a passage, a piece of evidence, a precedent, a defendant, an offence, a soldier's name, a source, or a spirit.","cn":"cite 的八个义项都是同一个“叫到前面”的动作：叫来一段文字、一项证据、一个判例、一名被告、一桩违规、一个士兵的名字、一个出处，或一个亡灵。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: calling something out of the background so it stands in front of your claim.","cn":"核心意象：把某物从背景里叫出来，让它站到你的论点前面。"},"chain":["CALL OUT","SUMMON A PERSON","SUMMON A TEXT","QUOTE AS PROOF","INVOKE AUTHORITY","NAME IN THE RECORD"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S02","en":"WORDS BECOME EVIDENCE: a sentence is quoted, and a study is brought in to prove a claim.","cn":"文字成为证据：一句话被引用，一项研究被调进来证明主张。"},{"senses":"S03","en":"THE PAST SPEAKS: an old ruling is called into the present case and given authority again.","cn":"过去开口：旧裁决被叫进眼前案件，重新获得权威。"},{"senses":"S04 · S05","en":"THE STATE CALLS A PERSON: a court summons a defendant, and a traffic citation names an offence.","cn":"国家召唤个人：法庭传唤被告，交通罚单点明违规。"},{"senses":"S06","en":"THE RANKS ARE READ: a soldier's name is called out in a dispatch and placed before everyone.","cn":"队列被点名：士兵的名字在战报里被念出，摆到所有人面前。"},{"senses":"S07 · S08","en":"THE HIDDEN IS MADE VISIBLE: a footnote lets the source stand in view, and the archaic sense calls a spirit out of silence.","cn":"隐藏者现身：脚注让来源站到明处；古义则把亡灵从沉默里叫出。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Cite is a single Latin stem cit- 'call' with a silent final -e. Its family shows the same stem under re-, in-, ex- and -ation.","cn":"cite 是单一拉丁词干 cit-“叫”加不发音的词尾 -e。它的词族显示同一词干在 re-、in-、ex- 和 -ation 下的变化。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin citare 'summon' and its base ciere 'set in motion' produced citation, recite, incite, excite and resuscitate, all still built on the call.","cn":"拉丁语 citare“传召”及其基干 ciere“使动”产生了 citation、recite、incite、excite、resuscitate，全都仍建立在“叫”上。"},"items":[{"word":"cite","structure":"cit- (call, set in motion) + -e","meaning":"to quote, adduce, or summon","meaningCN":"引用；引证；传唤（cit- 表“叫”）","example":"Cite your sources at the end of the paper.","exampleCN":"在论文末尾标注并引用你的出处。"},{"word":"citation","structure":"cit- (call) + -ation (noun of action)","meaning":"a quotation, a summons, or an official commendation","meaningCN":"引文；传票；嘉奖（-ation 构成动作或结果名词）","example":"The paper has thirty citations.","exampleCN":"这篇论文有三十条引文。"},{"word":"citable","structure":"cit- (call) + -able (worthy of)","meaning":"suitable to be quoted as evidence","meaningCN":"可引用的；值得引证的（-able 表“可……的”）","example":"Only peer-reviewed papers are citable here.","exampleCN":"这里只可引用同行评审的论文。"},{"word":"recite","structure":"re- (again) + cit- (call) + -e","meaning":"to say a text aloud from memory","meaningCN":"背诵；朗诵（re- 表“再次”，把文字重新叫回）","example":"The child recited the poem without a prompt.","exampleCN":"孩子不用提示就背出了这首诗。"},{"word":"recitation","structure":"re- (again) + cit- (call) + -ation","meaning":"the act of reciting; a recited piece","meaningCN":"背诵；朗诵（同一词干加 -ation 构成名词）","example":"The class began with a recitation of the oath.","exampleCN":"全班先背诵誓词。"},{"word":"incite","structure":"in- (into) + cit- (call) + -e","meaning":"to stir someone into action, often violent","meaningCN":"煽动；激起（in- 表“进入”，把情绪叫进人心里）","example":"His speech incited the crowd to riot.","exampleCN":"他的演讲煽动人群暴动。"},{"word":"excite","structure":"ex- (out) + cit- (call) + -e","meaning":"to arouse strong feeling or activity","meaningCN":"使兴奋；激起（ex- 表“向外”，把能量叫出来）","example":"The news excited the whole town.","exampleCN":"这个消息让全镇兴奋起来。"},{"word":"resuscitate","structure":"re- (again) + sus- (up from below) + cit- (call) + -ate","meaning":"to bring someone back to life or consciousness","meaningCN":"使复苏；救活（re- 再 + sus- 从下往上 + cit- 叫）","example":"The paramedics resuscitated the swimmer.","exampleCN":"急救人员把那名游泳者救了回来。"},{"word":"citing","structure":"cit- (call) + -ing (present participle)","meaning":"the act of quoting or summoning, used as a participle","meaningCN":"引用；传唤（-ing 构成现在分词）","example":"The footnote was missing when citing the report.","exampleCN":"引用那份报告时漏掉了脚注。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"citare","structure":"ciere (set in motion) + -tare (frequentative)","meaning":"to summon, urge, call, rouse","meaningCN":"传召；催促；呼叫；激起"},{"word":"ciere","structure":"PIE *keie- (set in motion)","meaning":"to move, set in motion, call","meaningCN":"使动；移动；呼叫"},{"word":"citatio","structure":"citare + -tio (noun of action)","meaning":"a summons; a citation","meaningCN":"传召；引证"},{"word":"incitare","structure":"in- (into) + citare (call)","meaning":"to rouse, urge on","meaningCN":"激起；煽动"}]}},{"word":"civil","ipa_uk":"/ˈsɪvl/","ipa_us":"/ˈsɪvl/","definition_zh":"公民的；民事的；国内的；民用的；世俗的；有礼貌的","definition_en":"relating to citizens or the state rather than the army or the church, and also polite","core_image":"城邦里一个公民应守的分寸：对同类讲法、讲礼，不动刀兵","scene":"婚礼登记处，工作人员解释：A civil ceremony here has the same legal force as a church wedding.","sceneCN":"这里 civil 是「世俗的、非教会的」（第 5 个义项：由民政而非教会主持）；句意：这里的民政婚礼与教堂婚礼具有同等法律效力。图中可辨识物件：登记处的国徽、结婚证、签字笔、排队的新人。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"公民的；民事的；国内的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"民用的；非军事的；世俗的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"有礼貌的；文明的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"civil rights","zh":"公民权利"},{"phrase":"civil war","zh":"内战"},{"phrase":"civil case","zh":"民事案件"},{"phrase":"civil servant","zh":"公务员"},{"phrase":"civil marriage","zh":"民政婚姻；世俗婚礼"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more civil"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most civil"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"civility","pos":"n.","zh":"礼貌；客气；公民身份"},{"word":"civilian","pos":"n.","zh":"平民；非军人"},{"word":"civilize","pos":"v.","zh":"使文明；教化"},{"word":"civilization","pos":"n.","zh":"文明；文明社会"},{"word":"uncivil","pos":"adj.","zh":"不礼貌的；粗野的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Of citizens: rights and duties of membership","titleCN":"公民的：属于城邦成员的权利与义务","definition":"relating to the rights and duties of a citizen","definitionCN":"与公民的权利和义务有关的","example":"The campaign fought for equal civil rights for all residents.","exampleCN":"这场运动为所有居民争取平等的公民权利。","why":"Latin civis meant 'townsman'. What belongs to the townsman as a member, rather than to him as a private person or soldier, is civil.","whyCN":"拉丁语 civis 意为“城邦人”。属于成员身份、而非私人身份或军人身份的东西，就是 civil。"},{"no":"02","title":"Within the state: a war among its own citizens","titleCN":"国内的：战火发生在公民之间","definition":"happening between citizens of the same country, especially a war","definitionCN":"发生在同一国家的公民之间，尤指内战","example":"The civil war split families and emptied whole towns.","exampleCN":"内战拆散了家庭，也搬空了整座整座的城镇。","why":"A war is normally between states. When the fighting stays inside the citizen body, the same word marks that the enemy is a fellow civis.","whyCN":"战争通常发生在国家之间。当战火留在公民共同体内部时，这个词就点明：敌人也是自己的公民同胞。"},{"no":"03","title":"Non-military: the civilian side of the state","titleCN":"民用的：国家生活里非军人的那一半","definition":"not relating to the armed forces","definitionCN":"与武装部队无关的；非军事的","example":"Civil aviation was grounded while the airspace was closed.","exampleCN":"领空关闭期间，民用航空全面停飞。","why":"Once civil means the citizen order, it naturally becomes the opposite of the army: the same society, but without uniforms and weapons.","whyCN":"一旦 civil 指公民秩序，它自然成为军队的反面：同一个社会，只是没有军装和武器。"},{"no":"04","title":"Civil law: disputes between private citizens","titleCN":"民事的：私人之间的纠纷，而非刑事犯罪","definition":"relating to private law and disputes between individuals, not criminal law","definitionCN":"涉及私法及个人之间的纠纷，而非刑法","example":"The dispute went to a civil court, where she sued for damages.","exampleCN":"这起纠纷进了民事法庭，她在那里起诉索赔。","why":"Roman ius civile was the law for citizens settling things among themselves. A civil case is still a citizen-to-citizen matter, not a crime against the state.","whyCN":"罗马的 ius civile 是公民之间处理事务的法律。民事案件至今仍是公民对公民的事，而不是对抗国家的犯罪。"},{"no":"05","title":"Secular: the registry office instead of the church","titleCN":"世俗的：在民政局而不是教堂","definition":"relating to the state rather than to a church or religion","definitionCN":"属于国家而非教会或宗教的","example":"They chose a civil wedding before flying abroad for the religious one.","exampleCN":"他们先办了民政婚礼，再出国办宗教仪式。","why":"The citizen order and the church are two jurisdictions. What the state registers without a blessing is civil, because it belongs to the civitas, not the ecclesia.","whyCN":"公民秩序与教会是两套管辖。国家不加祝福就登记的事属于 civil，因为它归城邦（civitas），不归教会。"},{"no":"06","title":"Polite: the minimum courtesy between citizens","titleCN":"有礼貌的：公民之间最低限度的客气","definition":"polite in a formal, restrained way, without warmth","definitionCN":"以正式、克制的方式表示礼貌，并不热情","example":"He gave a civil reply and left before the argument could start.","exampleCN":"他客气地回了一句，在争吵开始前就走了。","why":"Classical Latin already used civilis for 'affable'. Courtesy is what a citizen owes a fellow citizen; English took the sense late 16c., and it faded to 'not rude'.","whyCN":"古典拉丁语已用 civilis 表“和蔼”。礼貌是公民对同胞应尽的分寸；英语到 16 世纪后期才收进这一义，后来淡化为“不失礼”。"},{"no":"07","title":"Civilized: settled life, not barbarism","titleCN":"文明的：定居秩序，而非蛮荒","definition":"belonging to a settled, organized society rather than a barbarous one","definitionCN":"属于定居、有组织的社会，而非野蛮状态","example":"The Romans called any people without cities and laws less civil.","exampleCN":"罗马人把任何没有城市与法律的族群都称为不够文明。","why":"To Latin ears a civis was the opposite of a barbarian: one lived in a city under law, the other wandered outside it. Being civil therefore also means being on the city side of that line.","whyCN":"在拉丁语耳朵里，civis 是蛮族的反面：一个住在法律下的城里，一个在城外游荡。因此 civil 也意味着站在这条线的“城市”一侧。"},{"no":"08","title":"Civil service: the state's permanent staff","titleCN":"文职的：国家常任公务员系统","definition":"relating to the permanent administrative service of the state","definitionCN":"与国家常设行政公务系统有关的","example":"She spent thirty years in the civil service, never in uniform.","exampleCN":"她在公务员系统工作了三十年，从未穿军装。","why":"The civil service is the civilian half of government: the citizen order doing its paperwork, deliberately separated from the military chain of command.","whyCN":"civil service 是政府的平民那一半：公民秩序在办文书，并被有意与军队指挥链分开。"},{"no":"09","title":"Civil law as a legal tradition","titleCN":"民法法系：从罗马公民法传下的一整套体系","definition":"the legal system derived from Roman law, based on written codes","definitionCN":"源自罗马法、以成文法典为基础的法律体系","example":"France follows civil law, while England relies on common law.","exampleCN":"法国属民法法系，而英格兰依赖普通法。","why":"The Roman ius civile was written down as a body of rules for citizens. Modern countries that inherited that code-based tradition still call the whole system civil law.","whyCN":"罗马的 ius civile 是写给公民的成文规则体系。继承这套法典传统的现代国家，仍把整个体系称作 civil law。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Civil goes back to Latin civis 'townsman' and civilis 'of a citizen, of public life'. English took the legal sense first, then the social ones.","cn":"civil 可追到拉丁语 civis“城邦人”与 civilis“公民的、公共生活的”。英语先吸收法律义，再长出社会性的各个义项。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN (1C BC)","en":"Civilis meant 'relating to a society, to public life, to the civic order, befitting a citizen'. It was an adjective from civis 'townsman', the same base as civitas 'citizenship, community'.","cn":"civilis 意为“与社会、公共生活、公民秩序有关的，合乎公民身份的”，是 civis“城邦人”的形容词，与 civitas“公民身份、共同体”同基。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Civis is traced to PIE *kei- (1) 'to lie', also the source of words for bed and couch. The starred root is a reconstruction with no written record, so this layer is source uncertain.","cn":"civis 被追溯到原始印欧语 *kei-（1）“躺”，也是“床、卧榻”一类词的来源。带星号的词根是重构，没有书面记录，故此层来源不确定。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (13C)","en":"Old French civil 'relating to civil law' carried the Roman legal adjective into French, already narrowed to law rather than the whole citizen order.","cn":"古法语 civil“与民法有关的”把罗马的法律形容词带进法语，词义已收窄到法律，而非整个公民秩序。"},{"era":"LATE 14C ENGLISH","en":"English records civil late 14c. as 'relating to civil law or life; pertaining to the internal affairs of a state'. This is the word's English starting point.","cn":"英语在 14 世纪后期记录 civil 为“与民法或公民生活有关的；涉及国家内部事务的”。这是它进入英语的起点。"},{"era":"1550s–1610s ENGLISH","en":"The sense 'not barbarous, civilized' appears in the 1550s. By the 1610s civil also means 'secular, not ecclesiastical or military', and 'relating to a citizen in his relations with the commonwealth'; civil case is recorded from the 1610s.","cn":"“非野蛮的、文明的”一义出现于 16 世纪 50 年代。到 17 世纪 10 年代，civil 又表示“世俗的，非教会或非军事的”，以及“涉及公民与国家关系的”；civil case 记录于 17 世纪 10 年代。"},{"era":"LATE 16C–MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The polite sense existed in classical Latin but entered English only in the late 16c., later weakening to 'meeting minimum standards of courtesy'. Civil liberty is recorded from the 1640s and civil rights from 1721.","cn":"“有礼貌”义在古典拉丁语里已有，但直到 16 世纪后期才进入英语，后来弱化为“达到最低礼貌标准”。civil liberty 记录于 17 世纪 40 年代，civil rights 记录于 1721 年。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is built on the same civ- stem; the second group shares the ideas of citizenship, courtesy or the non-military state.","cn":"第一组都建立在同一个 civ- 词干上；第二组共享“公民身份、礼貌、非军事国家”这些意思。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"civic","ipa":"/ˈsɪvɪk/","tag":"same stem","definition":"relating to a city and the duties of its people. It points to the town, while civil points to the citizen.","definitionCN":"城市的；市民职责的。它指向城镇，而 civil 指向公民。"},{"word":"civilian","ipa":"/səˈvɪliən/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"a person who is not in the armed forces. It is the human noun from civil in its non-military sense.","definitionCN":"平民；非军人。它是 civil“非军事”义对应的人称名词。"},{"word":"civilize","ipa":"/ˈsɪvəlaɪz/","tag":"derived verb","definition":"to bring a society to a more organized, 'civil' condition. It turns the adjective into an action.","definitionCN":"使文明；教化。它把形容词变成动作。"},{"word":"civility","ipa":"/səˈvɪləti/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"polite behaviour. It is the noun behind the 'polite' sense of civil.","definitionCN":"礼貌；客气。它是 civil“有礼貌”义背后的名词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"polite","ipa":"/pəˈlaɪt/","tag":"courtesy","definition":"showing good manners and respect. It is warmer and more active than civil.","definitionCN":"有礼貌的；客气的。它比 civil 更热情、更主动。"},{"word":"courteous","ipa":"/ˈkɜːtiəs/","tag":"courtesy","definition":"graciously respectful, with the manner of a court. It is fuller and more dignified than civil.","definitionCN":"谦恭有礼的，带有宫廷风度。它比 civil 更周全、更庄重。"},{"word":"municipal","ipa":"/mjuːˈnɪsɪpl/","tag":"local state","definition":"relating to a town or city's own government. It is the local, place-based branch of civic life.","definitionCN":"市政的；地方自治的。它是公民生活中按地方划分的那一支。"},{"word":"domestic","ipa":"/dəˈmestɪk/","tag":"within the state","definition":"relating to affairs inside one country. It overlaps civil in civil war and civil unrest.","definitionCN":"国内的；本国的。它在 civil war、civil unrest 中与 civil 重叠。"},{"word":"secular","ipa":"/ˈsekjələ/","tag":"non-religious","definition":"not connected with religion. It is the explicit word for the civil-versus-church contrast.","definitionCN":"世俗的；非宗教的。它明确表达 civil 与教会对照的那一面。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: civis 'townsman', the civ- family, and the legal phrases English actually uses.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：civis“城邦人”、civ- 词族，以及英语实际使用的法律短语。"},"normal":[{"en":"civil, civic, civility, civilian and civilize all carry civ-, the Latin civis 'townsman'.","cn":"civil、civic、civility、civilian、civilize 都带着 civ-，即拉丁语 civis“城邦人”。"},{"en":"A civil war is a war inside the civis-body: the enemy holds the same passport.","cn":"civil war 是公民共同体内部的战争：敌人拿着同一本护照。"},{"en":"A civil servant serves the civitas, not the army; that is why the post is 'civil'.","cn":"civil servant 服务的是 civitas（公民共同体），不是军队；所以这个职位叫“文职”。"},{"en":"A civil reply is the politeness a citizen owes a fellow citizen: correct, but not warm.","cn":"civil reply 是公民对同胞应付的礼貌：得体，但不热络。"},{"en":"Civil law began as the law citizens used among themselves, which is why it is not criminal law.","cn":"civil law 起初是公民之间处理事务的法，所以它不是刑法。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"One root idea runs through every sense: the order that people keep when they live together as citizens.","cn":"所有义项背后只有一个核心：人们作为公民共同生活时所守的秩序。"},{"en":"That order has an inside and an outside: inside, law, politeness and civil service; outside, the army, the church and the barbarian.","cn":"这套秩序有内与外：对内是法律、礼貌与公务员；对外则对照军队、教会与蛮族。"},{"en":"So 'civil' never means one thing only; it always says which side of the citizen line you are on.","cn":"所以 civil 从不止一个意思；它总在说明你站在公民这条线的哪一侧。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The new law protects the civil rights of migrant workers.","cn":"新法律保护外来务工人员的公民权利。"},{"en":"The country was still recovering from a decade of civil war.","cn":"这个国家仍在从十年内战中恢复。"},{"en":"The two neighbours remained civil to each other after the quarrel.","cn":"争吵之后，两位邻居仍对彼此保持客气。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"civil = civ（公民）+ il：公民该有的样子——懂民法、守公德、讲礼貌 → civil 公民的、民事的、有礼貌的","word":"civil"},"root":"源自拉丁语 civilis“公民的、公共生活的”，来自 civis“城邦人”；核心是“公民共同体内部的秩序与分寸”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of civil, all orbiting the citizen: membership rights, war inside the state, the non-military side, private law, the secular state, minimum courtesy, settled life, the civil service, and the Roman legal tradition.","cn":"civil 的九个义项都绕着“公民”转：成员权利、国家内部的战争、非军事的一侧、私法、世俗国家、最低礼貌、定居文明、公务员系统，以及罗马法传统。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: the order a person keeps as a member of a city, not as a soldier or a churchman.","cn":"核心意象：一个人作为城邦成员——而非军人或教士——所守的秩序。"},"chain":["CITIZEN","CITIZEN ORDER","STATE AFFAIRS","CIVIL LAW","SECULAR AND CIVILIAN","COURTEOUS DISTANCE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S07","en":"MEMBERSHIP AND ITS LINE: rights belong to the citizen, and settled city life is what separates him from the barbarian.","cn":"成员身份及其边界：权利属于公民；定居的城市生活则把他与蛮族分开。"},{"senses":"S02 · S03","en":"INSIDE VERSUS OUTSIDE: a war among citizens, and a state run without soldiers.","cn":"内与外：公民之间的战争，以及不靠军人运转的国家。"},{"senses":"S04 · S09","en":"LAW AMONG CITIZENS: private disputes go to civil court, and the Roman code becomes a whole civil-law tradition.","cn":"公民之间的法：私人纠纷进民事法庭，罗马法典则演成整个民法法系。"},{"senses":"S05 · S08","en":"THE STATE WITHOUT THE CHURCH OR THE ARMY: registry-office marriage and the permanent civil service.","cn":"没有教会与军队的国家：民政局婚姻，以及常任公务员系统。"},{"senses":"S06","en":"THE SOCIAL SURFACE: courtesy is the small daily version of the citizen order, kept to a minimum.","cn":"社会表面：礼貌是公民秩序在日常里的最小版本。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Civil is the Latin stem civ- 'citizen' plus the adjective ending -il. Its family adds -ity, -ian, -ize, -ation, -ly and the negative un-.","cn":"civil 是拉丁词干 civ-“公民”加形容词词尾 -il。它的词族再加 -ity、-ian、-ize、-ation、-ly 与否定前缀 un-。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin base civis 'townsman' also gave civitas 'citizenship, community', civicus 'of a city' and civilis 'of a citizen'; English keeps all three branches.","cn":"拉丁词基 civis“城邦人”还给出 civitas“公民身份、共同体”、civicus“城市的”与 civilis“公民的”；英语三条分支都保留。"},"items":[{"word":"civil","structure":"civ- (citizen) + -il (adjective)","meaning":"of a citizen, the state, or polite behaviour","meaningCN":"公民的；国家的；有礼貌的（civ- 表公民）","example":"Civil rights are protected by the constitution.","exampleCN":"公民权利受宪法保护。"},{"word":"civility","structure":"civil + -ity (state or quality)","meaning":"politeness; the quality of being civil","meaningCN":"礼貌；客气（-ity 构成性质名词）","example":"He answered with cold civility.","exampleCN":"他冷淡而有礼地回答。"},{"word":"civilian","structure":"civil + -ian (person)","meaning":"a person who is not a soldier","meaningCN":"平民；非军人（-ian 表人）","example":"The attack killed many civilians.","exampleCN":"这次袭击造成许多平民死亡。"},{"word":"civilize","structure":"civil + -ize (make)","meaning":"to bring into a settled, organized condition","meaningCN":"使文明；教化（-ize 表“使……化”）","example":"Trade routes helped civilize the frontier.","exampleCN":"贸易路线帮助开化了边疆。"},{"word":"civilization","structure":"civilize + -ation (process or result)","meaning":"a settled society and its culture","meaningCN":"文明；文明社会（-ation 表过程或结果）","example":"Writing is a mark of early civilization.","exampleCN":"文字是早期文明的一个标志。"},{"word":"uncivil","structure":"un- (not) + civil","meaning":"rude; not showing proper courtesy","meaningCN":"不礼貌的；粗野的（un- 表否定）","example":"It was uncivil to interrupt the speaker.","exampleCN":"打断发言者是不礼貌的。"},{"word":"civilly","structure":"civil + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"politely, in a restrained way","meaningCN":"礼貌地；客气地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"She greeted the reporters civilly.","exampleCN":"她客气地向记者们打了招呼。"},{"word":"civic","structure":"civ- (city, citizen) + -ic (adjective)","meaning":"relating to a city or its citizens' duties","meaningCN":"城市的；市民的（-ic 构成形容词）","example":"Voting is a civic duty.","exampleCN":"投票是一项市民义务。"},{"word":"civics","structure":"civic + -s (subject name)","meaning":"the school subject about citizenship","meaningCN":"公民学（-s 构成学科名）","example":"Civics teaches how local government works.","exampleCN":"公民学讲授地方政府如何运作。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"civis","structure":"PIE *kei- (to lie, settle)","meaning":"townsman, citizen","meaningCN":"城邦人；公民"},{"word":"civitas","structure":"civis + -itas (state or body)","meaning":"citizenship; community of citizens; state","meaningCN":"公民身份；公民共同体；国家"},{"word":"civilis","structure":"civis + -ilis (adjective)","meaning":"of a citizen, of public life, courteous","meaningCN":"公民的；公共生活的；有礼的"},{"word":"civicus","structure":"civis + -icus (adjective)","meaning":"of a city or its citizens","meaningCN":"城市的；市民的"}]}},{"word":"clarify","ipa_uk":"/ˈklærəfaɪ/","ipa_us":"/ˈklerəfaɪ/","definition_zh":"澄清；阐明；使清楚；理清","definition_en":"to make something clear, pure, or easy to understand","core_image":"让浑水静下来，杂质沉底，光重新透过去","scene":"会议室里，项目经理举手说：Let me clarify one point before we vote.","sceneCN":"这里 clarify 是「阐明、把话说清楚」（第 2、3 个义项：让规则或事实不再含混）；句意：表决前让我把一个要点说清楚。图中可辨识物件：白板、议程表、举手的人、投影上的条款。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"澄清（液体）；提纯"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"阐明；使（陈述、问题）清楚"},{"tag":"vi.","zh":"变清澈；变得清楚"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"clarify a statement","zh":"阐明一项声明"},{"phrase":"clarify the rules","zh":"把规则说清楚"},{"phrase":"clarify one's position","zh":"表明并澄清立场"},{"phrase":"clarified butter","zh":"澄清黄油（去掉乳固体的黄油）"},{"phrase":"to clarify matters","zh":"把事情说清楚"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单","form":"clarifies"},{"label":"过去式","form":"clarified"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"clarified"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"clarifying"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"clarification","pos":"n.","zh":"澄清；说明；澄清后的状态"},{"word":"clarity","pos":"n.","zh":"清晰；清楚；透明"},{"word":"clarified","pos":"adj.","zh":"澄清的；提纯的"},{"word":"clarifying","pos":"adj.","zh":"使清楚的；有澄清作用的"},{"word":"clear","pos":"adj./v.","zh":"清楚的；清澈的；清除"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Purify a liquid until light passes through","titleCN":"澄清液体：让杂质沉下去，光透过来","definition":"to make a liquid clear by removing the substances that cloud it","definitionCN":"去除使液体浑浊的物质，使之变清","example":"Skim the foam, then clarify the broth over low heat.","exampleCN":"撇去浮沫，再用小火把高汤澄清。","why":"The Latin pieces are clarus 'clear' plus facere 'make'. The first thing English made clear was liquid: clouding matter is removed so that light can pass straight through.","whyCN":"拉丁成分是 clarus“清澈”加 facere“使”。英语最先“使清”的对象是液体：去掉浑浊物，让光直接穿过。"},{"no":"02","title":"Make a rule or idea transparent","titleCN":"阐明规则或概念：让听者一眼看透","definition":"to make a statement, rule or idea easier to understand","definitionCN":"使陈述、规则或观点更容易理解","example":"The guide clarifies how the new tax bracket works.","exampleCN":"这份指南把新税率档如何运作讲清楚了。","why":"Understanding is light passing through a medium. A rule that is unclear has matter suspended in it; clarifying removes that matter so the meaning shows through.","whyCN":"理解就像光穿过介质。含混的规则里悬浮着杂质；clarify 就是滤掉这些杂质，让意思透出来。"},{"no":"03","title":"Clear up a misunderstanding","titleCN":"澄清误会：把遮住事实的雾吹散","definition":"to explain something so that a wrong impression is removed","definitionCN":"作出解释，消除错误的印象","example":"She clarified that the delay was caused by the supplier, not the team.","exampleCN":"她澄清说，延误是供应商造成的，不是团队。","why":"A misunderstanding is mud in the water: both sides look at the same facts and see them darkly. Clarifying is the act that lets the facts become visible again.","whyCN":"误会就是水里的泥：双方看着同一批事实，却看得发暗。澄清就是让事实重新可见的动作。"},{"no":"04","title":"Settle one's own thinking","titleCN":"理清思路：让心里的水静下来","definition":"to make one's thoughts or priorities distinct and orderly","definitionCN":"使自己的想法或轻重缓急变得分明有序","example":"A night's sleep helped her clarify what she actually wanted.","exampleCN":"睡了一夜，她理清了自己真正想要什么。","why":"The murky medium can also be the mind. When confused ideas settle, the mind becomes transparent to itself, and that settling is called clarifying.","whyCN":"浑的介质也可以是头脑。混乱的念头沉淀下来，心对自己就变得透明，这个沉淀过程就叫 clarifying。"},{"no":"05","title":"Become clear by itself","titleCN":"变清：不用外力，自己澄澈起来","definition":"of a liquid or a situation, to become clear","definitionCN":"（液体或局面）自行变得清澈、明朗","example":"Left undisturbed, the wine gradually clarified in the barrel.","exampleCN":"静置不动，酒在桶里渐渐变清了。","why":"English added the intransitive use in the 1590s: the same clearing happens without an agent, as sediment falls and the liquid clears itself.","whyCN":"英语在 16 世纪 90 年代加上不及物用法：同样的“变清”不需要施动者，沉淀落下，液体自己澄清。"},{"no":"06","title":"Refine in an industrial process","titleCN":"提纯：工业流程里的“澄清”","definition":"to purify sugar, juice or another product by removing solids","definitionCN":"通过去除固体杂质来提纯糖、果汁等产品","example":"The plant clarifies cane juice before boiling it into sugar.","exampleCN":"工厂先把甘蔗汁澄清，再熬成糖。","why":"Once clarifying is a technical removal of solids, it becomes a step in production. The kitchen verb turns into an industrial process noun, clarification.","whyCN":"一旦“澄清”成为去除固体的技术动作，它就变成生产中的一道工序。厨房动词也就变成工业流程名词 clarification。"},{"no":"07","title":"Make illustrious: the medieval sense","titleCN":"使显赫、颂扬：中世纪的旧义","definition":"to make someone or something famous, glorious or known; now obsolete","definitionCN":"使某人或某物显赫、荣耀或为人所知；今已废弃","example":"Medieval chronicles were written to clarify the deeds of kings.","exampleCN":"中世纪的编年史写作，是为了使诸王的功业彰显。","why":"Late Latin clarificare meant 'to glorify', literally 'to make bright'. A king's name was made to shine before all, which is clarification as radiance rather than explanation.","whyCN":"晚期拉丁语 clarificare 意为“颂扬”，字面是“使发亮”。国王的名字被弄得在众人面前发光，这是“使显赫”而非“解释”。"},{"no":"08","title":"State one's position on the record","titleCN":"公开表明立场：把话说进记录里","definition":"to state clearly and formally what one's position is","definitionCN":"清楚而正式地表明自己的立场","example":"The minister clarified that no troops would be sent abroad.","exampleCN":"部长明确表示不会派兵出国。","why":"In public life, clarity is produced by speaking: an unclear position is made definite by saying it on the record. The metaphor of clearing now works through words, not liquids.","whyCN":"在公共生活中，清楚是靠说话造出来的：含糊的立场一经正式说出就变确定。此时“澄清”的隐喻已通过语言，而非液体运作。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Clarify joins Latin clarus 'clear, bright' to facere 'to make'. It entered English through Old French, first meaning 'glorify', then 'purify a liquid', and only later 'explain'.","cn":"clarify 把拉丁语 clarus“清澈、明亮”与 facere“使”结合。它经古法语进入英语，先表“颂扬”，再表“澄清液体”，最后才表“解释”。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Clarus meant 'clear, loud, bright, distinct', and in transferred use 'manifest, plain, evident'. With facere 'to make' it formed clarificare, literally 'to make clear'.","cn":"clarus 意为“清澈、响亮、明亮、分明”，引申为“明显、明白、显而易见”。它与 facere“使”构成 clarificare，字面即“使清楚”。"},{"era":"LATE LATIN","en":"Late Latin clarificare is glossed 'to glorify', literally 'to make clear', from clarificus 'brilliant'. The brightness was moral and social before it was optical.","cn":"晚期拉丁语 clarificare 被释为“颂扬”，字面“使清楚”，来自 clarificus“光辉的”。这种亮度先是道德与声望上的，后才是光学上的。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH (12C)","en":"Old French clarifiier meant 'clarify, make clear, explain'. It carried both the liquid and the explanatory possibilities into English.","cn":"古法语 clarifiier 意为“澄清、使清楚、解释”，把液体与解释两种可能都带进了英语。"},{"era":"EARLY 14C ENGLISH","en":"English first records clarify in the early 14c. as 'make illustrious, glorify, make known', a sense that is now obsolete.","cn":"英语最早在 14 世纪早期记录 clarify 为“使显赫、颂扬、使为人所知”，此义今已废弃。"},{"era":"EARLY 15C ENGLISH","en":"The sense 'make clear, purify', especially of liquors, appears in the early 15c. The intransitive 'become clear' follows in the 1590s.","cn":"“使清澈、提纯”一义，尤指液体，出现于 15 世纪早期。不及物的“变清”随后在 16 世纪 90 年代出现。"},{"era":"1823–MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The figurative sense 'free from obscurity, render intelligible' is dated 1823, although explanation had been part of the word since Old French. Modern English extends it to industrial purification.","cn":"“去除晦涩、使可理解”的比喻义定于 1823 年，尽管“解释”从古法语起就在词里。现代英语又把它扩展到工业提纯。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group shares the clar- / clear root; the second group shares the act of making something intelligible or pure.","cn":"第一组共享 clar- / clear 词根；第二组共享“使可理解或使纯净”的动作。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"clarity","ipa":"/ˈklærəti/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"the quality of being clear and easy to understand. It is the noun from the same clar- stem.","definitionCN":"清晰；清楚。它是同一 clar- 词干的名词。"},{"word":"clear","ipa":"/klɪə/","tag":"same root","definition":"easy to see through or understand. It is the everyday adjective behind clarify, with a different French spelling.","definitionCN":"清澈的；清楚的。它是 clarify 背后的日常形容词，只是法语拼写不同。"},{"word":"declare","ipa":"/dɪˈkleə/","tag":"same root","definition":"to announce something formally. De- plus clarare 'make clear': to make a matter clear in public.","definitionCN":"宣布；声明。de- 加 clarare“使清楚”：在公众面前把事情讲明。"},{"word":"clarification","ipa":"/ˌklærɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"an explanation that removes confusion; also the act of purifying a liquid.","definitionCN":"澄清说明；也指液体提纯。它是 clarify 的动作名词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"explain","ipa":"/ɪkˈspleɪn/","tag":"make understandable","definition":"to make something understandable by giving details. It is the everyday word for clarify in its explanatory sense.","definitionCN":"解释；说明。它是 clarify 表“解释”时最日常的说法。"},{"word":"elucidate","ipa":"/ɪˈluːsɪdeɪt/","tag":"formal explanation","definition":"to make a difficult subject clear by explanation. It is the formal, learned equivalent of clarify.","definitionCN":"阐明；解释。它是 clarify 的正式、学术化对应词。"},{"word":"illuminate","ipa":"/ˌɪljuːmɪˈneɪt/","tag":"throw light on","definition":"to make a subject easier to understand by throwing light on it. It keeps the light metaphor explicit.","definitionCN":"阐明；照亮。它把“光”的隐喻说得更明白。"},{"word":"simplify","ipa":"/ˈsɪmplɪfaɪ/","tag":"make accessible","definition":"to make something easier by removing complexity. It reaches clarity by cutting, not by filtering.","definitionCN":"简化。它靠删减而非过滤来达到清楚。"},{"word":"purify","ipa":"/ˈpjʊərɪfaɪ/","tag":"remove impurities","definition":"to remove unwanted substances. It matches clarify in its liquid and industrial senses.","definitionCN":"净化；提纯。它对应 clarify 的液体义与工业义。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: clarus 'clear', the -ify verb pattern, and the clar- family that English still uses.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：clarus“清澈”、-ify 动词模式，以及英语仍在使用的 clar- 词族。"},"normal":[{"en":"clarify = clar- 'clear' + -ify 'make': make clear. The spelling practically explains itself.","cn":"clarify = clar-“清楚”+ -ify“使”：使清楚。拼写本身几乎就把意思讲明白了。"},{"en":"clarity is the noun, clarify the verb: the state of being clear and the act of making it so.","cn":"clarity 是名词，clarify 是动词：一个是“清楚的状态”，一个是“使清楚的动作”。"},{"en":"declare = de- + clarare: to make a matter clear out loud, in public.","cn":"declare = de- + clarare：把一件事当众讲清楚。"},{"en":"clarified butter is butter with its milk solids removed, so the fat looks clear. The kitchen shows the original sense.","cn":"clarified butter 是去掉乳固体的黄油，油脂看起来清亮。厨房里就演示了这个词的本义。"},{"en":"A clarinet and a clarion both carry clarus in their history: a clear, bright sound.","cn":"clarinet 与 clarion 的历史里都带着 clarus：清亮的声音。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core is always optical: something cloudy is made transparent.","cn":"核心始终是光学式的：把浑浊的东西变透明。"},{"en":"The cloudy medium changes: broth, a rule, a misunderstanding, a mind, a public position.","cn":"浑浊的介质在变：高汤、规则、误会、头脑、公开立场。"},{"en":"In every case the same move is made: remove what blocks the light, and the thing shows itself.","cn":"每一次都是同一个动作：移走挡住光的东西，事物就自己显现。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The teacher clarified the instructions before the exam began.","cn":"考试开始前，老师把说明讲清楚了。"},{"en":"Melt the butter and simmer it until it clarifies.","cn":"把黄油融化，小火煮到它变清澈。"},{"en":"The company issued a short statement to clarify its position.","cn":"公司发布了一份简短声明来澄清立场。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"构词记忆 · 词源相关","text":"clarify = clear（清楚）+ -ify（使……）：使清楚 → 澄清、阐明；clear 与 clar- 同源","word":"clarify"},"root":"源自拉丁语 clarus“清澈、明亮、分明”+ facere“使”，经古法语 clarifiier 与晚期拉丁语 clarificare 进入英语，核心是“使浑浊变透明”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of clarify, one optical core: a cloudy medium is made transparent. The medium ranges from broth to rules, misunderstandings, the mind, wine, sugar juice and a public stance.","cn":"clarify 的八个义项只有一个光学核心：让浑浊的介质变透明。介质则从高汤延伸到规则、误会、头脑、酒、糖汁与公开立场。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: letting light pass through something that was clouded.","cn":"核心意象：让光穿过原本浑浊的东西。"},"chain":["CLOUDED LIQUID","REMOVE IMPURITIES","BECOME TRANSPARENT","CLEAR WORDS","CLEAR THE MIND","STATE IT PUBLICLY"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S06","en":"LIQUID MADE CLEAR: broth is skimmed at home, and cane juice is purified in a plant.","cn":"液体变清：家里撇清高汤，工厂提纯甘蔗汁。"},{"senses":"S02 · S04","en":"MEANING MADE CLEAR: a rule becomes transparent to the listener, and confused thoughts settle into order.","cn":"意义变清：规则对听者变得透明，混乱的念头沉淀成秩序。"},{"senses":"S03 · S08","en":"FACTS MADE VISIBLE: a misunderstanding is cleared away, and a position is put clearly on the record.","cn":"事实变可见：误会已被清除，立场也被清楚地写进记录。"},{"senses":"S05","en":"SELF-CLEARING: sediment falls on its own, and a situation clarifies without anyone acting.","cn":"自行变清：沉淀自己落下，局面不需任何人施力就明朗起来。"},{"senses":"S07","en":"BRIGHTNESS AS GLORY: the oldest sense makes a name shine before everyone.","cn":"亮度即荣耀：最古老的义项让一个名字在众人面前发光。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Clarify is the Latin stem clar- 'clear, bright' plus -ify 'to make'. The family adds -ity, -ation, -ed and -ing, and shares clar- with clear, declare and clarion.","cn":"clarify 是拉丁词干 clar-“清澈、明亮”加 -ify“使”。词族再加 -ity、-ation、-ed、-ing，并与 clear、declare、clarion 共享 clar-。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin clarus 'clear, bright' produced claritas 'brightness, clarity', clarificare 'make clear, glorify', and clarare 'make bright'; English keeps the whole family.","cn":"拉丁语 clarus“清澈、明亮”产生 claritas“明亮、清晰”、clarificare“使清楚、颂扬”与 clarare“使发亮”；英语保留整个词族。"},"items":[{"word":"clarify","structure":"clar- (clear, bright) + -ify (make)","meaning":"to make clear, pure, or understandable","meaningCN":"澄清；阐明（clar- 表清楚，-ify 表使）","example":"Could you clarify the second point?","exampleCN":"你能把第二点说清楚吗？"},{"word":"clarification","structure":"clarific- (clarify) + -ation (noun of action)","meaning":"the act of making clear; an explanation","meaningCN":"澄清；说明（-ation 构成动作名词）","example":"The memo offers no clarification on who is in charge.","exampleCN":"这份备忘录没有说明谁负责。"},{"word":"clarity","structure":"clar- (clear) + -ity (quality)","meaning":"the quality of being clear","meaningCN":"清晰；清楚（-ity 构成性质名词）","example":"The essay is admired for its clarity.","exampleCN":"这篇文章因清晰而受赞赏。"},{"word":"clarified","structure":"clarify + -ed (past participle)","meaning":"made clear or purified","meaningCN":"已澄清的；提纯的（-ed 构成过去分词）","example":"Clarified butter keeps longer than fresh butter.","exampleCN":"澄清黄油的保存时间比新鲜黄油长。"},{"word":"clarifying","structure":"clarify + -ing (present participle)","meaning":"making something clear","meaningCN":"使清楚的；澄清的（-ing 构成现在分词）","example":"She made a clarifying remark and sat down.","exampleCN":"她说了一句澄清的话就坐下了。"},{"word":"clear","structure":"clar- (clear, bright) + French spelling","meaning":"easy to see through or understand","meaningCN":"清澈的；清楚的（同根，经古法语拼写）","example":"The water was clear to the bottom.","exampleCN":"水清得能看到底。"},{"word":"declare","structure":"de- (intensive) + clar- (clear) + -e","meaning":"to announce or state formally","meaningCN":"宣布；声明（de- 加强 + clar- 使清楚）","example":"The court declared the law invalid.","exampleCN":"法院宣布该法律无效。"},{"word":"clarion","structure":"clar- (clear, loud) + -ion (noun suffix)","meaning":"a clear, high trumpet call","meaningCN":"号角声；清亮的呼唤（clar- 表清亮）","example":"A clarion sounded over the square.","exampleCN":"广场上空响起清亮的号角。"},{"word":"clarinet","structure":"clarion (clear sound) + -et (diminutive)","meaning":"a woodwind instrument with a clear tone","meaningCN":"单簧管（由“清亮声音”加指小后缀 -et）","example":"She plays the clarinet in the school band.","exampleCN":"她在校乐队吹单簧管。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"clarus","structure":"PIE *kele- (to shout) + -ro-","meaning":"clear, bright, loud, distinct","meaningCN":"清澈的；明亮的；响亮的；分明的"},{"word":"claritas","structure":"clarus + -itas (quality)","meaning":"brightness, clarity","meaningCN":"明亮；清晰"},{"word":"clarificare","structure":"clarus (clear) + facere (make)","meaning":"to make clear; to glorify","meaningCN":"使清楚；颂扬"},{"word":"clarare","structure":"clarus + -are (verb)","meaning":"to make bright or clear","meaningCN":"使明亮；使清楚"}]}},{"word":"classic","ipa_uk":"/ˈklæsɪk/","ipa_us":"/ˈklæsɪk/","definition_zh":"一流的；典型的；古典的；经典作品","definition_en":"of the highest class or a standard model, especially in art and literature","core_image":"罗马公民名册上最上面那一等：被公认为范本","scene":"旧车展上，车主拍着引擎盖说：The 1965 model is a classic — they don't build them like that anymore.","sceneCN":"这里 classic 是「经典款、受推崇的旧型号」（第 5 个义项：不再生产但被奉为范本的物件）；句意：1965 年那款是经典——现在没人这么造车了。图中可辨识物件：老爷车、引擎盖、车展铭牌、擦拭布。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"一流的；典范的；典型的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"古典的（希腊罗马）；传统典雅的"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"经典作品；经典款；古典学（the classics）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a classic example","zh":"典型例子"},{"phrase":"a classic mistake","zh":"典型的错误"},{"phrase":"classic literature","zh":"古典文学"},{"phrase":"a modern classic","zh":"现代经典"},{"phrase":"classic style","zh":"简约典雅的风格"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more classic"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most classic"},{"label":"复数","form":"classics"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"classical","pos":"adj.","zh":"古典的；经典的；传统的"},{"word":"classicism","pos":"n.","zh":"古典主义；古典风格"},{"word":"classicist","pos":"n.","zh":"古典学者；古典主义者"},{"word":"classics","pos":"n.","zh":"古典学；古典文献"},{"word":"classy","pos":"adj.","zh":"高级的；有品位的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Of the highest class: first-rate","titleCN":"一流的：属于最高那一等","definition":"judged to be of the highest quality and worth following","definitionCN":"被评判为质量最高、值得效仿的","example":"Her recording of the sonata is now considered classic.","exampleCN":"她录的那首奏鸣曲现在被视为一流演绎。","why":"Latin classicus first meant 'relating to the highest classes of the Roman people'. English kept the ranking: what is classic sits in the first class, not the second.","whyCN":"拉丁语 classicus 最初意为“与罗马人最高等级有关的”。英语保留了这种排名：classic 的东西坐在第一等，而非第二等。"},{"no":"02","title":"Textbook case: the model everyone recognizes","titleCN":"典型的：教科书里那个标准案例","definition":"very typical of its kind, often in a way that is easy to recognize","definitionCN":"非常典型，常指一眼就能认出的那种","example":"Ignoring the warning signs was a classic mistake.","exampleCN":"无视警示信号是个典型的错误。","why":"A first-class example becomes the model against which later cases are measured. From 'approved as a model' comes the modern sense 'typical': the case fits the model exactly.","whyCN":"一流的例子会成为衡量后来案例的范本。由“被认可为范本”引申出今天的“典型”：这个案例与范本严丝合缝。"},{"no":"03","title":"Of Greek and Roman antiquity","titleCN":"古典的：希腊罗马古代留下的","definition":"belonging to the standard authors and art of ancient Greece and Rome","definitionCN":"属于古希腊罗马标准作家与艺术的","example":"The library keeps its classic texts apart from modern novels.","exampleCN":"图书馆把古典文本与现代小说分开存放。","why":"From the 1620s classic named the recognized standard authors of antiquity. They were the first class of Western letters, so their period became 'classic' time.","whyCN":"从 17 世纪 20 年代起，classic 指古代公认的标准作家。他们是西方文学的第一等，因此他们所处的时代也成了“古典”时代。"},{"no":"04","title":"A classic: a work that lasts","titleCN":"经典作品：经得住时间的那一本","definition":"a book, film or piece of music of the first rank that remains admired","definitionCN":"一流且至今仍受推崇的书、电影或乐曲","example":"The novel became a classic within a decade of publication.","exampleCN":"这部小说出版十年内就成了经典。","why":"The noun appeared in 1711 for a Greek or Roman writer, then widened to any first-rank work. A classic is a model that time has not demoted from the first class.","whyCN":"名词义 1711 年指希腊或罗马作家，后扩展到任何一流作品。经典就是历经时间仍未从第一等被降下来的范本。"},{"no":"05","title":"A classic car or design: old but canonical","titleCN":"经典款：旧了，却成了公认范本","definition":"an old model or design still valued as an outstanding example of its kind","definitionCN":"虽旧却仍因是该类中的杰出范例而受重视的型号或设计","example":"He drives a classic Mini that he restored himself.","exampleCN":"他开着一辆自己修复的经典 Mini。","why":"An object no longer in production can still hold its first-class place. 'Classic' then marks not newness but canonicity: the design has become the reference for its kind.","whyCN":"不再生产的东西仍可保住第一等的位置。此时 classic 标记的不是新，而是典范性：这个设计已成该类物的参照。"},{"no":"06","title":"The Classics: the Greek and Roman curriculum","titleCN":"古典学：希腊罗马那套课程","definition":"the study of Greek and Roman literature, languages and culture","definitionCN":"对希腊罗马文学、语言与文化的研究","example":"She read Classics at Oxford before becoming a lawyer.","exampleCN":"她在牛津读古典学，之后当了律师。","why":"When the first-class texts of antiquity became a course of study, the plural the Classics named the whole body of them, and then the discipline built on that body.","whyCN":"当古代第一等文本变成一门课程，复数 the Classics 就指这批文本的整体，进而指建立其上的学科。"},{"no":"07","title":"Restrained good taste in dress or design","titleCN":"简约典雅：不过时、不过火的好品位","definition":"simple, well-proportioned and unlikely to date, in clothes or design","definitionCN":"在服装或设计上简洁、比例得当、不易过时的","example":"A classic navy blazer works for almost every occasion.","exampleCN":"一件经典的海军蓝西装外套几乎适合所有场合。","why":"If a model is first class, copying it avoids extremes. Classic style is therefore the look that stays close to the approved model: plain, balanced, and hard to make dated.","whyCN":"既然范本是第一等，照着它做就能避开极端。于是 classic style 就是贴近公认范本的样子：素净、均衡、很难过时。"},{"no":"08","title":"Classic sign: the textbook symptom","titleCN":"典型症状：医学教科书上的那一组","definition":"of a symptom or case, exactly matching the standard description","definitionCN":"（症状或病例）与标准描述完全吻合的","example":"A rash behind the ears is a classic sign of this infection.","exampleCN":"耳后出疹是这种感染的典型体征。","why":"Medicine teaches by standard cases. When a patient's symptoms match the model case exactly, doctors call the presentation classic: it belongs in the textbook.","whyCN":"医学靠标准病例教学。当病人的症状与范本病例完全吻合，医生就说表现是 classic：它够格进教科书。"},{"no":"09","title":"Colloquial 'classic!': so predictable it is funny","titleCN":"口语“真典型”： predictable 到好笑","definition":"used informally to say that behaviour is typical of a person or situation, often with amusement","definitionCN":"非正式用法，表示某行为正合某人或某情形的一贯作风，常带调侃","example":"He cancelled at the last minute — classic!","exampleCN":"他最后一刻取消了——真典型！","why":"Once a person's behaviour fits a known model, each repeat is a 'classic case' of that person. The colloquial exclamation compresses that judgment into one word.","whyCN":"一旦某人的行为符合已知范本，每次重演都是此人的“经典案例”。口语感叹把这个判断压缩成一个词。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Classic comes from Latin classicus, 'relating to the highest classes of the Roman people', from classis 'division, class'. English first used it for rank, then for the canonical authors of antiquity.","cn":"classic 来自拉丁语 classicus“与罗马人最高等级有关的”，出自 classis“分区、等级”。英语先用它表示等级，再用来指古代公认的正典作家。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Classis meant 'a class, a division; army, fleet', especially one of the six orders into which Servius Tullius divided the Roman people for taxation. Classicus meant 'relating to the highest classes', hence 'superior'.","cn":"classis 意为“等级、分区；军队、舰队”，尤指塞尔维乌斯·图利乌斯为征税把罗马人分成的六个等级之一。classicus 意为“属于最高等级的”，因而表示“优越的”。"},{"era":"LATIN NOUN USE","en":"As a noun, classicus could mean 'a marine' (miles classicus), from the military-division sense of classis. That older noun use did not survive into English.","cn":"classicus 作名词时也可指“海军士兵”（miles classicus），源自 classis 的军事分区义。这个古老名词义没有进入英语。"},{"era":"FRENCH (17C)","en":"French classique (17c.) carried the ranking adjective into modern use, still tied to the idea of an approved first class.","cn":"法语 classique（17 世纪）把这个表等级的形容词带入近代用法，仍与“被认可的第一等”这一观念相连。"},{"era":"1610s ENGLISH","en":"English records classic in the 1610s as 'of or belonging to the highest class; approved as a model', originally simply 'of the first class'.","cn":"英语在 17 世纪 10 年代记录 classic 为“属于最高等级的；被认可为范本的”，最初就是“第一等的”。"},{"era":"1620s ENGLISH","en":"By the 1620s it means 'belonging to or characteristic of the standard authors of Greek and Roman antiquity'. The literary canon takes over the ranking word.","cn":"到 17 世纪 20 年代，它表示“属于或具有希腊罗马古代标准作家特征的”。文学正典接管了这个表等级的词。"},{"era":"1711–MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The noun 'a Greek or Roman writer or work' is recorded in 1711; by the mid-18c. it covers any first-rank work. Class 'high quality' is dated 1874, and the modern 'classic car' extends the same canonical judgment to objects.","cn":"名词“希腊或罗马作家或作品”记录于 1711 年；到 18 世纪中期已涵盖任何一流作品。class 的“高质量”义定于 1874 年，现代“经典车”则把同一种正典判断扩展到物件。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group shares the class- stem; the second group shares the idea of a model that stands above the rest.","cn":"第一组共享 class- 词干；第二组共享“高于其余者的范本”这一观念。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"classical","ipa":"/ˈklæsɪkl/","tag":"derived adjective","definition":"relating to ancient Greece and Rome, or to a traditional refined style. It is the longer adjective from classic.","definitionCN":"古典的；传统典雅的。它是 classic 加 -al 的较长形容词。"},{"word":"class","ipa":"/klɑːs/","tag":"same Latin stem","definition":"a group of people or things of the same rank. It is the noun that gave classic its ranking.","definitionCN":"阶级；班级；类别。它是给 classic 提供“等级”义的名词。"},{"word":"classify","ipa":"/ˈklæsɪfaɪ/","tag":"same Latin stem","definition":"to arrange things into classes. It uses the same classis but as an action, not a judgment of rank.","definitionCN":"分类。它用同一个 classis，但表示动作，而非等级评判。"},{"word":"classicism","ipa":"/ˈklæsɪsɪzəm/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"the artistic style that takes Greek and Roman models as its standard. It is classic + -ism.","definitionCN":"古典主义。它是 classic 加 -ism 的艺术风格名。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"exemplary","ipa":"/ɪɡˈzempləri/","tag":"model","definition":"so good that it should be copied as an example. It states the 'approved model' side of classic.","definitionCN":"典范的；可作榜样的。它说出 classic“被认可为范本”的一面。"},{"word":"quintessential","ipa":"/ˌkwɪntɪˈsenʃl/","tag":"most typical","definition":"being the purest or most typical example of something. It matches the 'textbook case' sense.","definitionCN":"最典型、最纯粹的。它对应“教科书案例”一义。"},{"word":"timeless","ipa":"/ˈtaɪmləs/","tag":"enduring","definition":"not affected by changes in fashion. It explains why a classic work or design lasts.","definitionCN":"永恒的；不受时尚影响的。它解释了经典作品或设计为何耐久。"},{"word":"vintage","ipa":"/ˈvɪntɪdʒ/","tag":"old but valued","definition":"old and of good quality, especially of cars, clothes or wine. It overlaps classic in the classic-car sense.","definitionCN":"上等的旧物；复古的。它在“经典车”一义上与 classic 重叠。"},{"word":"model","ipa":"/ˈmɒdl/","tag":"standard","definition":"a person or thing held up as an example to follow. It is the underlying idea shared by all senses of classic.","definitionCN":"模范；模型。它是 classic 所有义项共享的底层观念。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Latin classis 'division, class', the class- family, and the phrases English actually uses.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 classis“分区、等级”、class- 词族，以及英语实际使用的短语。"},"normal":[{"en":"classic and class share classis: classic things belong to the first class.","cn":"classic 与 class 共享 classis：经典的东西属于第一等。"},{"en":"classical is the longer form for Greek and Roman style; classic is the shorter judgment of rank.","cn":"classical 是较长的形式，指希腊罗马风格；classic 是较短的形式，指等级评判。"},{"en":"a classic mistake is not a good mistake; it is a mistake that fits the textbook model exactly.","cn":"a classic mistake 不是“好错误”，而是与教科书范本完全吻合的错误。"},{"en":"the Classics at Oxford means the canonical Greek and Roman texts studied as a course.","cn":"牛津的 the Classics 指作为课程研读的希腊罗马正典文本。"},{"en":"a classic car is one that time has kept in first class even after the factory stopped making it.","cn":"经典车就是工厂停产之后，时间仍把它留在第一等的车。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"One judgment runs through every sense: this thing is the approved model of its kind.","cn":"所有义项背后只有一个判断：此物是同类中被认可的范本。"},{"en":"The judgment can fall on a performance, a mistake, an author, a car, a blazer or a symptom.","cn":"这个判断可以落在一次演奏、一个错误、一位作家、一辆车、一件西装外套或一个症状上。"},{"en":"So classic always ranks: it puts its object in the first class, whether by excellence or by typicality.","cn":"所以 classic 始终在排名：无论因卓越还是因典型，它都把对象放进第一等。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The film is a classic of 1970s science fiction.","cn":"这部电影是 20 世纪 70 年代科幻作品的经典。"},{"en":"Forgetting to save the file is a classic beginner's error.","cn":"忘记保存文件是典型的新手错误。"},{"en":"She wore a classic black dress that never looks out of date.","cn":"她穿了一条从不过时的经典小黑裙。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 词源相关","text":"classic = class（等级）+ -ic：属于最高那一等的 → 一流的、经典的、典型的","word":"classic"},"root":"源自拉丁语 classicus“属于最高等级的”，来自 classis“分区、等级、公民等级”；核心是“被公认为第一等的范本”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of classic, all one ranking judgment: a performance, a mistake, an ancient author, a lasting work, an old car, a curriculum, a style, a symptom or a predictable habit is placed in the first class.","cn":"classic 的九个义项都是同一个排名判断：一次演奏、一个错误、一位古代作家、一部传世作品、一辆旧车、一套课程、一种风格、一个症状或一种可预测的习惯，被放进第一等。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: the approved first-class model that later cases are measured against.","cn":"核心意象：被认可的第一等范本，后来的案例都要拿它来量。"},"chain":["ROMAN CLASS RANK","HIGHEST CLASS","APPROVED MODEL","ANCIENT CANON","LASTING WORK","TYPICAL CASE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S02","en":"RANK BECOMES JUDGMENT: first-class quality hardens into the model that a typical case must match.","cn":"等级变成判断：一流的品质凝固成范本，典型案例必须与它吻合。"},{"senses":"S03 · S04","en":"THE CANON: Greek and Roman standard authors, and the single work that time keeps in first class.","cn":"正典：希腊罗马的标准作家，以及时间始终留在第一等的那部作品。"},{"senses":"S05 · S07","en":"OBJECTS AND STYLE: an old car or a plain blazer borrows the same canonical authority.","cn":"物件与风格：一辆旧车或一件素净西装外套，借用了同一种正典权威。"},{"senses":"S06","en":"THE CANON AS A COURSE: the body of texts becomes the discipline called the Classics.","cn":"正典成为课程：那批文本整体变成名为 the Classics 的学科。"},{"senses":"S08 · S09","en":"THE MODEL IN DAILY LIFE: a textbook symptom and a predictable habit are both 'classic cases'.","cn":"日常里的范本：教科书症状与可预测的习惯，都是“经典案例”。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Classic is Latin classis 'division, class' plus -ic. Its family adds -al, -ism, -ist and -s, and the same stem yields class, classify and classification.","cn":"classic 是拉丁语 classis“分区、等级”加 -ic。词族再加 -al、-ism、-ist、-s，同一词干还给出 class、classify、classification。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin classis 'division, fleet' and classicus 'of the highest class' are the base; English class, classic, classical and classify all descend from that one ranking noun.","cn":"拉丁语 classis“分区、舰队”与 classicus“最高等级的”是词基；英语 class、classic、classical、classify 都出自这个表等级的名词。"},"items":[{"word":"classic","structure":"class- (class, division) + -ic (adjective)","meaning":"of the highest class; serving as a model","meaningCN":"一流的；典范的（-ic 构成形容词）","example":"This is a classic example of the problem.","exampleCN":"这是该问题的典型例子。"},{"word":"classical","structure":"classic + -al (adjective)","meaning":"relating to Greek and Roman antiquity or a refined tradition","meaningCN":"古典的；传统典雅的（-al 构成形容词）","example":"She studied classical architecture in Rome.","exampleCN":"她在罗马研究古典建筑。"},{"word":"classicism","structure":"classic + -ism (style or movement)","meaning":"art that follows Greek and Roman models","meaningCN":"古典主义（-ism 表风格或流派）","example":"The building is a late example of classicism.","exampleCN":"这座建筑是古典主义的晚期例子。"},{"word":"classicist","structure":"classic + -ist (person)","meaning":"a scholar of classical studies; a follower of classicism","meaningCN":"古典学者；古典主义者（-ist 表人）","example":"The classicist translated the ode into English.","exampleCN":"这位古典学者把这首颂歌译成了英语。"},{"word":"classics","structure":"classic + -s (plural noun)","meaning":"the body of Greek and Roman literature; its study","meaningCN":"古典文献；古典学（-s 构成复数名词）","example":"He read Classics before turning to law.","exampleCN":"他先读古典学，之后转学法律。"},{"word":"class","structure":"classis (division, rank) + zero suffix","meaning":"a group of the same rank or kind","meaningCN":"阶级；班级；类别（直接来自 classis）","example":"The whole class went to the museum.","exampleCN":"全班都去了博物馆。"},{"word":"classify","structure":"class + -ify (make, arrange)","meaning":"to arrange into classes","meaningCN":"分类；归类（-ify 表“使……化”）","example":"Botanists classify plants by their flowers.","exampleCN":"植物学家按花把植物分类。"},{"word":"classification","structure":"classify + -ation (process or result)","meaning":"the act or system of arranging into classes","meaningCN":"分类；分类体系（-ation 构成动作名词）","example":"The library uses a simple classification system.","exampleCN":"这家图书馆使用简单的分类系统。"},{"word":"classy","structure":"class + -y (adjective)","meaning":"stylish and high-quality, informally","meaningCN":"高级的；有品位的（-y 构成形容词，口语）","example":"They held the party in a classy hotel.","exampleCN":"他们在一家高级酒店办派对。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"classis","structure":"traditionally linked to calare (to call to arms)","meaning":"a division, class; army, fleet","meaningCN":"分区；等级；军队；舰队"},{"word":"classicus","structure":"classis + -icus (adjective)","meaning":"relating to the highest classes; superior","meaningCN":"最高等级的；优越的"},{"word":"classificare","structure":"classis + facere (make)","meaning":"to arrange into classes (medieval Latin)","meaningCN":"分类（中世纪拉丁语）"}]}},{"word":"classify","ipa_uk":"/ˈklæsɪfaɪ/","ipa_us":"/ˈklæsɪfaɪ/","definition_zh":"分类；归类；分级；列为机密","definition_en":"to arrange things into groups by shared features, or to assign something to a category","core_image":"把一堆杂乱的卡片按标签分进不同的抽屉","scene":"图书馆整理书架时，管理员说：We classify novels by genre, not by the author's nationality.","sceneCN":"这里 classify 是「分类、按共同特征归组」（第 1 个义项：按体裁把小说分进不同类别）；句意：我们按体裁而非作者国籍来分小说。图中可辨识物件：书架、分类标签、推车、扫描枪。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"把……分类；整理"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"把……归入某类；判定为"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"将（文件）列为机密；分级"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"classify something by","zh":"按……分类"},{"phrase":"classify something as","zh":"把……归为……"},{"phrase":"classify plants into families","zh":"把植物分入各科"},{"phrase":"classified documents","zh":"机密文件"},{"phrase":"classified advertisements","zh":"分类广告"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单","form":"classifies"},{"label":"过去式","form":"classified"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"classified"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"classifying"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"classification","pos":"n.","zh":"分类；类别；密级"},{"word":"classified","pos":"adj.","zh":"分类的；机密的"},{"word":"classifiable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可分类的"},{"word":"classifier","pos":"n.","zh":"分类者；分类器"},{"word":"declassify","pos":"v.","zh":"解密；撤销机密级别"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Sort into groups by shared features","titleCN":"分类整理：按共同特征分进不同抽屉","definition":"to arrange a set of things into groups that share features","definitionCN":"按共同特征把一组事物分进不同类别","example":"The librarian classified the new books by subject.","exampleCN":"图书管理员按学科把新书分类。","why":"The Latin noun classis meant a division or class; -fy means 'to make'. To classify is literally to make divisions, cutting a mixed pile into drawers that share a label.","whyCN":"拉丁名词 classis 意为“分区、等级”，-fy 意为“使”。classify 字面就是“造出分区”，把混杂的一堆切成贴着同一标签的抽屉。"},{"no":"02","title":"Assign a thing to an existing category","titleCN":"归入某类：把它放进现成的格子里","definition":"to decide that something belongs to a particular group or type","definitionCN":"判定某事物属于某一特定类别或类型","example":"Biologists classify the dolphin as a mammal, not a fish.","exampleCN":"生物学家把海豚归为哺乳动物，而不是鱼。","why":"Here the drawers already exist. The work is to look at the thing and place it in the right one, so classification becomes an act of judgment rather than of sorting.","whyCN":"这里抽屉已经存在。工作只是看清物件、把它放进正确的那一格，于是分类从“整理”变成了“判断”。"},{"no":"03","title":"Declare official information secret","titleCN":"列为机密：给它贴上“限制查阅”的标签","definition":"to mark government or military information as officially secret","definitionCN":"把政府或军方信息正式标为机密","example":"The report was classified and kept from the public for thirty years.","exampleCN":"那份报告被列为机密，三十年内不向公众开放。","why":"In 1941 classified acquired the sense 'secret': information was assigned to a restricted class of readers. The same labeling act now decides who may open the drawer.","whyCN":"1941 年 classified 获得“机密”义：信息被归入一个限定读者的等级。同一个贴标签动作，现在决定谁可以打开这个抽屉。"},{"no":"04","title":"Grade by rank or quality","titleCN":"分级：按等级高低排队","definition":"to sort goods or results into grades of quality or size","definitionCN":"按质量或大小把货物、结果分成等级","example":"The mill classifies wool into fine, medium and coarse grades.","exampleCN":"工厂把羊毛分成细、中、粗三等。","why":"Classis also carried rank. When the divisions are ordered from better to worse, classifying stops being neutral sorting and becomes grading.","whyCN":"classis 也带着“等级”义。当分区按优劣排序时，classifying 就不再是中性的整理，而成了分级。"},{"no":"05","title":"Identify and place a new species","titleCN":"科学鉴定：给新物种找到它的科属","definition":"to determine the taxonomic group of a plant, animal or specimen","definitionCN":"确定植物、动物或标本的分类群","example":"The specimen was classified as a new species of orchid.","exampleCN":"这份标本被鉴定为一种新的兰花。","why":"Natural history adopted class in 1753 for a group of related organisms. Classifying a specimen is therefore finding its family drawer in the living world's cabinet.","whyCN":"自然史在 1753 年采用 class 指一群相关生物。给标本做分类，就是在生物界的大柜子里找到它所属的那一格。"},{"no":"06","title":"Sort data or messages by type","titleCN":"数据分类：让机器按类型处理信息","definition":"to assign digital data or messages to categories, often automatically","definitionCN":"把数字数据或消息归入类别，常由程序自动完成","example":"The mail filter classifies unknown senders as spam.","exampleCN":"邮件过滤器把陌生发件人归为垃圾邮件。","why":"A spam filter repeats the old gesture at machine speed: it reads features and drops each message into the right class. The metaphor of drawers survives in software.","whyCN":"垃圾邮件过滤器以机器速度重复那个古老动作：读取特征，把每封邮件丢进正确的类别。抽屉的隐喻在软件里活了下来。"},{"no":"07","title":"Pigeonhole a person","titleCN":"给人贴标签：把一个人归入某种类型","definition":"to regard a person as belonging to a particular type or group","definitionCN":"把某人看作属于某一类型或群体","example":"Critics were quick to classify her as a regional novelist.","exampleCN":"批评家很快就把她归为地域小说家。","why":"People can be sorted too. To classify a person is to put a label on the drawer and treat everything he writes as belonging inside it, which is why the verb often sounds reductive.","whyCN":"人也能被分类。把一个人 classify，就是给抽屉贴上标签，并把他写的一切都当作属于这一格，所以这个动词常带“简化”的意味。"},{"no":"08","title":"The classifieds: ads arranged by category","titleCN":"分类广告：按类别排在一起的版面","definition":"classified advertisements, printed in columns by category","definitionCN":"按类别分栏刊登的分类广告","example":"He found the flat through the classifieds in the local paper.","exampleCN":"他通过本地报纸的分类广告找到了那套公寓。","why":"Classified advertisements were arranged in classes as early as 1913, and the shortened plural the classifieds kept the name of that layout, not of secrecy.","whyCN":"分类广告早在 1913 年就按类别排列，缩略的复数 the classifieds 保留的是这种版面编排的名字，而不是“机密”。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Classify was formed in French and entered English in 1782 from classe 'class' plus -fier 'to make'. Its root is Latin classis, a division or rank of Roman citizens.","cn":"classify 在法语中构成，1782 年进入英语，来自 classe“类别”加 -fier“使”。其词根是拉丁语 classis，即罗马公民的分区或等级。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Classis meant 'a class, a division; army, fleet', especially one of the six orders into which Servius Tullius divided the Roman people for taxation.","cn":"classis 意为“等级、分区；军队、舰队”，尤指塞尔维乌斯·图利乌斯为征税把罗马人分成的六个等级之一。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Classis is traditionally linked to calare 'to call (to arms)' and reconstructed PIE *kele- (2) 'to shout'. The starred root has no written record, so this deepest layer is source uncertain.","cn":"classis 传统上与 calare“号召（武装）”及重构的原始印欧语 *kele-（2）“喊”相联系。带星号的词根没有书面记录，故最深层来源不确定。"},{"era":"FRENCH (14C)","en":"French classe (14c.) meant a group or division, especially a group of students. English borrowed it as class around 1600.","cn":"法语 classe（14 世纪）指一群人或一个分区，尤指一群学生。英语约在 1600 年把它借为 class。"},{"era":"FRENCH (18C)","en":"French classifier joined classe to -fier 'to make', producing a verb for arranging things into classes. English took the verb in 1782.","cn":"法语 classifier 把 classe 与 -fier“使”结合，造出“把事物排成类别”的动词。英语于 1782 年借入该动词。"},{"era":"1828–1913 ENGLISH","en":"The adjective classified 'arranged in classes' is recorded in 1828. Classifieds 'newspaper advertisements arranged by classes' appears in 1913 as a shortening of classified advertisements.","cn":"形容词 classified“已分类的”记录于 1828 年。classifieds“按类别排列的报纸广告”出现于 1913 年，是 classified advertisements 的缩略。"},{"era":"1941–MODERN ENGLISH","en":"The sense 'secret' for classified government information is dated 1941 in American English. Modern computing extends classify to automatic sorting of data and mail.","cn":"classified 指政府信息“机密”的义项，在美国英语中定于 1941 年。现代计算又把 classify 扩展到数据与邮件的自动分类。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is built on the class- stem; the second group shares the act of putting things into groups.","cn":"第一组建立在 class- 词干上；第二组共享“把事物放进组里”的动作。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"class","ipa":"/klɑːs/","tag":"base noun","definition":"a group of people or things of the same kind or rank. It is the noun that classify turns into a verb.","definitionCN":"阶级；班级；类别。它是 classify 转化为动词的那个名词。"},{"word":"classic","ipa":"/ˈklæsɪk/","tag":"same stem","definition":"of the highest class; a standard model. It shares classis but judges rank instead of sorting.","definitionCN":"一流的；典范的。它共享 classis，但做的是等级评判，不是整理。"},{"word":"classification","ipa":"/ˌklæsɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"the act or system of arranging into classes; also an official secrecy level.","definitionCN":"分类；分类体系；也指官方密级。它是 classify 的动作名词。"},{"word":"classified","ipa":"/ˈklæsɪfaɪd/","tag":"derived adjective","definition":"arranged in classes, or officially secret; as a plural noun, small newspaper ads.","definitionCN":"已分类的；机密的；复数名词指报纸分类广告。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"categorize","ipa":"/ˈkætəɡəraɪz/","tag":"assign category","definition":"to put something into a category. It is the closest formal synonym of classify.","definitionCN":"把……归类。它是 classify 最接近的正式同义词。"},{"word":"sort","ipa":"/sɔːt/","tag":"arrange","definition":"to separate things into groups or order. It stresses the physical handling of a mixed pile.","definitionCN":"分类；整理。它强调对混杂一堆的动手分拣。"},{"word":"arrange","ipa":"/əˈreɪndʒ/","tag":"put in order","definition":"to put things in a particular order. It is about sequence rather than shared features.","definitionCN":"排列；布置。它讲的是顺序，而不是共同特征。"},{"word":"group","ipa":"/ɡruːp/","tag":"bring together","definition":"to put things or people together in a set. It builds the group rather than naming its class.","definitionCN":"分组；把……聚在一起。它是在造组，而不是给类别命名。"},{"word":"label","ipa":"/ˈleɪbl/","tag":"name a type","definition":"to attach a name to something, often unfairly. It matches the pigeonholing sense of classify.","definitionCN":"给……贴标签。它对应 classify“把人归入某类”的一义。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: classis 'division', the -ify verb pattern, and the class- family English still uses.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：classis“分区”、-ify 动词模式，以及英语仍在使用的 class- 词族。"},"normal":[{"en":"classify = class + -ify 'make': to make classes out of a mixed pile.","cn":"classify = class + -ify“使”：把混杂的一堆“造成”若干类别。"},{"en":"classification is the noun, classifier the person or program that does it.","cn":"classification 是名词，classifier 是做这件事的人或程序。"},{"en":"declassify is the reverse switch: un- sticking the 'secret' label off a file.","cn":"declassify 是反向开关：把“机密”标签从文件上摘下来。"},{"en":"classified ads were once literally ads arranged in classes, which is why the word has nothing to do with secrecy there.","cn":"classified ads 原本就是按类别排好的广告，所以那里的这个词与机密无关。"},{"en":"a spam filter classifies mail the way a librarian shelves books: by features, into drawers.","cn":"垃圾邮件过滤器分邮件，就像图书管理员上架：看特征，放进抽屉。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core action is always drawing a line around a set of things that share a feature.","cn":"核心动作始终是：围住一群共享某特征的事物，画一条线。"},{"en":"The line can be drawn around books, animals, wool, documents, emails or people.","cn":"这条线可以画在书、动物、羊毛、文件、邮件或人身上。"},{"en":"Sorting, grading, secrecy and pigeonholing are all one act of division followed by a judgment.","cn":"整理、分级、保密与贴标签，都是同一个“先分区、再判断”的动作。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The books are classified according to reading level.","cn":"这些书按阅读难度分类。"},{"en":"Scientists classify this lizard as a separate species.","cn":"科学家把这种蜥蜴归为独立物种。"},{"en":"The file was classified for reasons of national security.","cn":"该文件因国家安全原因被列为机密。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 词源相关","text":"classify = class（类别）+ -ify（使……）：把东西放进不同的 class → 分类、归类","word":"classify"},"root":"源自法语 classifier，来自 classe“类别”+ -fier“使”，词根为拉丁语 classis“分区、等级”；核心是“按共同特征划出类别并把事物放进去”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses of classify, all one act of drawing a class line: sorting books, placing a dolphin, sealing a file, grading wool, naming a species, filtering spam, labeling a writer or reading the classifieds.","cn":"classify 的八个义项都是同一个“划出类别线”的动作：整理书、归置海豚、给文件加密级、给羊毛分级、鉴定物种、过滤垃圾邮件、给作家贴标签，或翻阅分类广告。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a mixed pile cut into labeled drawers by shared features.","cn":"核心意象：混杂的一堆，按共同特征被切进贴好标签的抽屉。"},"chain":["DIVIDE","MAKE CLASSES","PLACE EACH THING","RANK THE CLASSES","RESTRICT ACCESS","LABEL AND PREDICT"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S02","en":"SORT AND ASSIGN: a librarian builds the drawers, and a biologist places one animal in an existing one.","cn":"整理与归置：管理员造出抽屉，生物学家把一只动物放进已有的那一格。"},{"senses":"S04 · S05","en":"RANK AND NAME: wool is graded from fine to coarse, and a new orchid receives its taxonomic place.","cn":"分级与命名：羊毛按细到粗分级，新兰花得到它的分类位置。"},{"senses":"S03 · S08","en":"THE LABEL CONTROLS: 'classified' can shut a file away or simply arrange ads by category.","cn":"标签控制出入：classified 可以把文件锁起来，也可以只是把广告按类别排好。"},{"senses":"S06","en":"THE MACHINE SORTS: software repeats the drawer gesture on mail and data at speed.","cn":"机器分拣：软件以高速在邮件与数据上重复“进抽屉”的动作。"},{"senses":"S07","en":"THE PERSON IS FILED: a writer is put in a type, and the label then shapes how she is read.","cn":"人也被归档：作家被放进某一类型，标签随后塑造别人如何读她。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Classify is class + -ify 'to make'. Its family adds -ication, -ed, -able and -er, and prefixes de-, re- and un- reverse or repeat the act.","cn":"classify 是 class 加 -ify“使”。词族再加 -ication、-ed、-able、-er，前缀 de-、re-、un- 则反转或重复这个动作。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The base is Latin classis 'division, rank'. French turned it into classe and classifier; English built class, classic, classify, classification and declassify from the same stem.","cn":"词基是拉丁语 classis“分区、等级”。法语把它变成 classe 与 classifier；英语用同一词干造出 class、classic、classify、classification、declassify。"},"items":[{"word":"classify","structure":"class- (class, division) + -ify (make)","meaning":"to arrange into classes or assign to a category","meaningCN":"分类；归入某类（-ify 表“使……化”）","example":"We classify the samples by size.","exampleCN":"我们按大小把样本分类。"},{"word":"classification","structure":"classify + -ication (noun of action)","meaning":"the act or system of classifying; a category","meaningCN":"分类；分类体系；类别（-ication 构成动作名词）","example":"The classification of these insects is still debated.","exampleCN":"这些昆虫的分类仍有争议。"},{"word":"classified","structure":"classify + -ed (past participle)","meaning":"arranged in classes; officially secret","meaningCN":"已分类的；机密的（-ed 构成过去分词或形容词）","example":"The archive holds classified material.","exampleCN":"该档案馆藏有机密材料。"},{"word":"classifiable","structure":"classify + -able (can be)","meaning":"able to be classified","meaningCN":"可分类的（-able 表“可……的”）","example":"Not every dialect is easily classifiable.","exampleCN":"并非每种方言都容易分类。"},{"word":"classifier","structure":"classify + -er (person or thing)","meaning":"one who classifies; a sorting device or program","meaningCN":"分类者；分类器（-er 表人或工具）","example":"The classifier sorts incoming mail automatically.","exampleCN":"分类器自动分拣收到的邮件。"},{"word":"class","structure":"classis (division, rank) + zero suffix","meaning":"a group of the same kind or rank","meaningCN":"类别；阶级；班级（直接来自 classis）","example":"The class meets every Monday.","exampleCN":"这个班每周一上课。"},{"word":"declassify","structure":"de- (reverse) + classify","meaning":"to remove the secret status from information","meaningCN":"解密；撤销机密级别（de- 表反转）","example":"The agency declassified the file in 2015.","exampleCN":"该机构于 2015 年解密了这份文件。"},{"word":"reclassify","structure":"re- (again) + classify","meaning":"to classify again or differently","meaningCN":"重新分类；改归别类（re- 表再次）","example":"The drug was reclassified as a controlled substance.","exampleCN":"这种药被重新归类为管制药物。"},{"word":"unclassified","structure":"un- (not) + classified","meaning":"not officially secret","meaningCN":"非机密的；未分类的（un- 表否定）","example":"The report remained unclassified.","exampleCN":"这份报告仍属非机密。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"classis","structure":"traditionally linked to calare (to call to arms)","meaning":"a division, class; army, fleet","meaningCN":"分区；等级；军队；舰队"},{"word":"classicus","structure":"classis + -icus (adjective)","meaning":"relating to the highest classes; superior","meaningCN":"最高等级的；优越的"},{"word":"classificare","structure":"classis + facere (make)","meaning":"to arrange into classes (medieval Latin)","meaningCN":"分类（中世纪拉丁语）"}]}},{"word":"climate","ipa_uk":"/ˈklaɪmət/","ipa_us":"/ˈklaɪmət/","definition_zh":"气候；风气；氛围；地带","definition_en":"the usual weather conditions of a region, and by extension the prevailing atmosphere of a group or period","core_image":"地球表面朝太阳倾斜的那一片斜坡，决定了它上面的冷暖和干湿","scene":"A farmer looks at the long-range forecast and says: The climate here has turned drier than in my father's time.","sceneCN":"这里 climate 是「气候」（第 2 个义项：一地长期的天气状况）；句意：这里的气候比我父亲那时候更干了。画面里是干裂的田地、远处的山脊和一份长期预报。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"气候；长期天气状况"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"风气；氛围；舆论环境"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（古代地理）气候带；地带"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"climate change","zh":"气候变化"},{"phrase":"a mild climate","zh":"温和的气候"},{"phrase":"the political climate","zh":"政治气候；政治氛围"},{"phrase":"a climate of opinion","zh":"舆论氛围；意见气候"},{"phrase":"a favourable business climate","zh":"有利的商业环境"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"climates"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"climatic","pos":"adj.","zh":"气候的；气候上的"},{"word":"climatically","pos":"adv.","zh":"在气候方面"},{"word":"climatology","pos":"n.","zh":"气候学"},{"word":"climatologist","pos":"n.","zh":"气候学家"},{"word":"acclimate","pos":"v.","zh":"使适应气候；使服水土"},{"word":"microclimate","pos":"n.","zh":"微气候；小气候"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Zone: a band of the earth marked by the sun","titleCN":"气候带：古人按日照划出的地球条带","definition":"in ancient geography, one of the bands of the earth's surface bounded by lines of latitude and distinguished by the length of daylight","definitionCN":"古代地理学中按纬度线划出的地球条带，以白昼长短来区分","example":"Ptolemy listed twenty-four climates between the upper Nile and the frozen north.","exampleCN":"托勒密在上尼罗河与冰封的北方之间列出了二十四个气候带。","why":"Greek klima meant a slope or inclination. The band was named for the angle at which the sun struck the earth's surface, so the earliest climate was a geometry of slant, not a kind of weather.","whyCN":"希腊语 klima 本义是“倾斜、斜坡”。条带是因太阳照射地表的倾角而得名，所以最早的 climate 是一道关于斜坡的几何题，还不是一种天气。"},{"no":"02","title":"Weather: the usual conditions of a region","titleCN":"气候：一个地方长年的天气状况","definition":"the ordinary weather conditions of a place, taken over a long period","definitionCN":"某地长期而言寻常的天气状况","example":"The island's mild climate suits citrus trees.","exampleCN":"这座岛温和的气候适合柑橘生长。","why":"Once a band was defined by its slant, that slant fixed how much sun and rain it received. By c. 1600 the word named the effect rather than the cause: the weather itself.","whyCN":"条带一旦由倾角划定，倾角就决定了它得到多少阳光和雨水。到约 1600 年，这个词从指“原因”转为指“结果”：天气本身。"},{"no":"03","title":"Region: a stretch of land seen through its weather","titleCN":"地带：按天气特征看待的一片土地","definition":"a region of the earth considered together with the weather that belongs to it","definitionCN":"连同其天气特征一起看待的一片地球区域","example":"Explorers wrote of a dry climate inland and a damp climate along the coast.","exampleCN":"探险者记载了内陆干燥的地带和沿海潮湿的地带。","why":"Metonymy of container for content: the latitude band was the unit of land, and the weather marked it, so the land and its weather came to share one name.","whyCN":"这是“容器代内容”的转喻：纬度带是土地的单位，而天气是它的标记，于是土地和它的天气共用了一个词。"},{"no":"04","title":"Atmosphere: the prevailing mood of a group","titleCN":"氛围：一个群体共同的空气般情绪","definition":"the general feeling, mood or set of attitudes shared by a group or a period","definitionCN":"一个群体或一个时期共有的总体感受、情绪或态度","example":"The climate in the office changed as soon as the new manager arrived.","exampleCN":"新经理一到，办公室的氛围就变了。","why":"The figurative sense is recorded from the 1660s. Weather surrounds everyone in a place and presses on them equally; a shared mood does the same, so mood is spoken of as the air a group breathes.","whyCN":"这一比喻义记录于 1660 年代。天气包围着某地的每个人，同等压在他们身上；共同的情绪也一样，于是情绪被说成群体呼吸的空气。"},{"no":"05","title":"Business climate: conditions that surround enterprise","titleCN":"商业环境：围绕企业经营的条件","definition":"the economic, legal and social conditions that affect how businesses operate","definitionCN":"影响企业经营的经济、法律和社会条件","example":"Low interest rates created a favourable climate for investment.","exampleCN":"低利率为投资创造了有利的环境。","why":"From air to environment: investors breathe the conditions of a market as farmers breathe weather. What surrounds and cannot be changed by one actor becomes 'climate'.","whyCN":"从“空气”到“环境”：投资者呼吸市场的条件，就像农民呼吸天气。那种包围个人、非个人所能改变的东西，就被叫作 climate。"},{"no":"06","title":"Political climate: the temper of public opinion","titleCN":"政治气候：公共舆论的 temper","definition":"the prevailing mood of public opinion at a particular time, especially as it affects politics","definitionCN":"某一时期公共舆论的主导情绪，尤指影响政治时","example":"The bill stalled in a political climate hostile to new taxes.","exampleCN":"在一股敌视新税的政治气候中，这项法案停滞不前。","why":"Public opinion behaves like weather: no single person controls it, everyone stands in it, and it can turn. Politics borrows the metaphor to describe pressure that comes from all sides.","whyCN":"舆论的举止像天气：没有一个人能控制它，每个人都站在里面，而且它会转向。政治借用这个比喻，描述从四面八方来的压力。"},{"no":"07","title":"Climate of opinion: the accepted view of an age","titleCN":"意见气候：一个时代被普遍接受的看法","definition":"the ideas and attitudes that are generally accepted during a period","definitionCN":"某一时期被普遍接受的思想与态度","example":"Darwin's theory slowly altered the climate of opinion about species.","exampleCN":"达尔文的理论慢慢改变了关于物种的意见气候。","why":"Opinion forms a medium that people think inside. A change of mind spreads through a society the way a change of weather spreads across a region, so the sum of opinions becomes a climate.","whyCN":"意见构成一种人们在其中思考的介质。看法的改变在社会里扩散，正如天气的变化在一片地区扩散，于是意见的总和成了一种气候。"},{"no":"08","title":"Climate system: the machinery behind the weather","titleCN":"气候系统：天气背后的运转机制","definition":"the interacting system of atmosphere, ocean, ice and land that produces a region's long-term weather","definitionCN":"由大气、海洋、冰和陆地相互作用、产生一地长期天气的系统","example":"Scientists now model the climate as a system of feedback loops.","exampleCN":"科学家现在把气候建模为一个由反馈回路构成的系统。","why":"Modern science turned the sum of weather into an object with parts and laws. The old word for a band of sky now names the machine that makes the band's weather.","whyCN":"现代科学把天气的总和变成了一个有部件、有规律的客体。这个原指天区的旧词，现在指制造该天区天气的那台“机器”。"},{"no":"09","title":"Microclimate: a pocket with weather of its own","titleCN":"微气候：自带天气的小口袋","definition":"the weather conditions of a small area, which differ from those of the surrounding region","definitionCN":"某一小块地方的天气状况，与周围地区不同","example":"The garden's south wall creates a warm microclimate for tomatoes.","exampleCN":"花园的南墙为番茄造出一块温暖的微气候。","why":"The prefix micro- shrinks the band down to a garden, and the original idea returns: a wall's slant changes the sun a plant receives, so a small slope makes a small climate.","whyCN":"前缀 micro- 把条带缩小到一个花园，而最初的意思回来了：墙的倾斜改变了植物得到的阳光，所以小斜坡造出小气候。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Climate begins as a Greek word for a slant. The earth's tilt, then the weather of the tilted band, then the mood of a room: each step keeps the idea of something that surrounds and leans over people.","cn":"climate 起初是希腊语里表示“倾斜”的词。先是地球的倾斜，接着是倾斜地带上的天气，再后来是一个房间里的气氛：每一步都保留了“某种东西斜压在人上方、包围着人”的意念。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK (c. 3C BC)","en":"Greek klima meant 'slope, inclination', from klinein 'to lean'. Geographers used it for a band of the earth's surface defined by the angle of the sun and the length of daylight.","cn":"希腊语 klima 意为“斜坡、倾斜”，来自 klinein“倾斜”。地理学家用它指按太阳角度和白昼长度划定的地表条带。"},{"era":"LATE 14c ENGLISH","en":"English borrowed it through Old French climat and Latin clima as 'a horizontal zone of the earth measured by lines parallel to the equator'. Ancient writers counted 7, 12, 24 or 30 such zones.","cn":"英语经古法语 climat 和拉丁语 clima 借入，意为“用平行于赤道的线量出的地球水平地带”。古代作者数出 7 个、12 个、24 个或 30 个这样的地带。"},{"era":"c. 1600","en":"As temperature came to matter more than daylight, the word shifted to 'the combined weather of a region' — heat, cold, rain and wind taken together.","cn":"当气温比白昼长短更受重视时，词义转向“一个地区天气的总和”——冷、热、雨、风合在一起。"},{"era":"1660s","en":"The figurative sense 'mental or moral atmosphere' is recorded from the 1660s, applied to the air of a society or a period.","cn":"“精神或道德氛围”的比喻义记录于 1660 年代，用于一个社会或一个时代的气氛。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Climate change in the modern sense of human-caused global warming is recorded from 1983, while climatic change was used from 1975. Microclimate and climate system extend the word to small pockets and to the planet as a whole.","cn":"climate change 指人为全球变暖的现代用法记录于 1983 年，而 climatic change 从 1975 年就在使用。microclimate 与 climate system 把该词扩展到小口袋和整个星球。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Klinein is traced to PIE *klei- 'to lean', also behind incline, decline, recline and ladder. The reconstructed root has no written attestation, so the deepest step is source uncertain.","cn":"klinein 被追溯到原始印欧语 *klei-“倾斜”，incline、decline、recline、ladder 也出自这里。该重构词根没有书面记录，故最深层来源不确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"clime","ipa":"/klaɪm/","tag":"shortened form","definition":"a region or its climate, used mainly in literary English. It is a shortened doublet of climate.","definitionCN":"地带；气候，主要用于文学语言。它是 climate 的缩短双式词。"},{"word":"climax","ipa":"/ˈklaɪmæks/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"the most intense or highest point of a story or process. It comes from Greek klimax 'ladder', not from klima.","definitionCN":"高潮；顶点。它来自希腊语 klimax“梯子”，与 klima 无关。"},{"word":"climb","ipa":"/klaɪm/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"to go up something using hands and feet. It shares the cli- opening but comes from Old English climban.","definitionCN":"攀爬。它同样以 cli- 开头，但来自古英语 climban。"},{"word":"climatic","ipa":"/klaɪˈmætɪk/","tag":"derived adjective","definition":"relating to climate. It is climate plus -ic, and is the adjective you need for climatic change.","definitionCN":"气候的。它是 climate 加 -ic，表示气候变化时要用 climatic change。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"weather","ipa":"/ˈweðə(r)/","tag":"short-term","definition":"the state of the atmosphere at a particular place and time. It is what climate averages over years.","definitionCN":"天气；某时某地的气象状况。它正是气候长年累积的对象。"},{"word":"atmosphere","ipa":"/ˈætməsfɪə(r)/","tag":"mood","definition":"the air around the earth, or the feeling a place or group gives off. It matches the figurative climate closely.","definitionCN":"大气；也指某地或某群体散发的气氛。它与比喻义的 climate 最贴近。"},{"word":"environment","ipa":"/ɪnˈvaɪrənmənt/","tag":"conditions","definition":"the surrounding conditions in which people work or live. It is broader than climate and not weather-based.","definitionCN":"环境；周围条件。它比 climate 更宽，也不以天气为本。"},{"word":"mood","ipa":"/muːd/","tag":"feeling","definition":"the way a person or group feels at a particular time. It is the inner state that a climate of opinion describes.","definitionCN":"情绪；心境。它是意见气候所描述的那种内在状态。"},{"word":"trend","ipa":"/trend/","tag":"direction","definition":"the general direction in which something is changing. A climate of opinion has a trend, but a trend is a movement, not a surrounding medium.","definitionCN":"趋势；走向。意见气候有趋势，但趋势是运动方向，不是包围人的介质。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Greek klima 'slope', the klinein family, and the derived forms English actually uses.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：希腊语 klima“斜坡”、klinein 词族，以及英语实际使用的派生形式。"},"normal":[{"en":"climate = Greek klima 'slope': the earth leans toward the sun, and the slope decides how warm the band is.","cn":"climate = 希腊语 klima“斜坡”：地球朝太阳倾斜，斜坡决定这一带有多暖。"},{"en":"The same klinein 'to lean' gives incline, decline, recline and climax's cousin klimax 'ladder'.","cn":"同一个 klinein“倾斜”还给出 incline、decline、recline，以及 climax 的亲戚 klimax“梯子”。"},{"en":"acclimate is ad- 'to' + climate: to bring a plant or person into a new climate.","cn":"acclimate 是 ad-“朝向”+ climate：把植物或人带进一个新气候。"},{"en":"microclimate shrinks the band to a garden wall; the slant of the wall is a tiny klima.","cn":"microclimate 把条带缩到一堵花园墙；墙的倾斜就是一个微小的 klima。"},{"en":"When people say the political climate, they mean the weather of opinion that everyone stands in.","cn":"人们说政治气候时，指的是每个人都站在其中的意见天气。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core operation is a slant that decides what reaches the surface: sun, rain, then mood, then opportunity.","cn":"核心动作是一个决定“什么能到达表面”的倾斜：先是阳光、雨水，再是情绪，再是机会。"},{"en":"The word always names something that surrounds people and cannot be changed by one person alone.","cn":"这个词始终指某种包围着人、非一人之力可以改变的东西。"},{"en":"So zone, weather, atmosphere, business conditions and opinion are one metaphor scaled from a planet down to a room.","cn":"所以地带、天气、氛围、商业条件与舆论，是同一个比喻从星球缩放到一个房间。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The south of the country has a warm, dry climate.","cn":"该国南部气候温暖干燥。"},{"en":"The new policy changed the climate for small businesses.","cn":"新政策改变了小企业的经营环境。"},{"en":"In the current political climate, few MPs dare to raise the issue.","cn":"在当前的政治气候下，很少有议员敢提出这个问题。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音拆分 · 非词源","text":"cli 像 climb（爬坡）+ mate（伙伴）——和伙伴一起爬坡，坡上阳光不同，天气也不同 → climate 气候","word":"climate"},"root":"源自希腊语 klima“倾斜、斜坡”（klinein 倾斜），古人按太阳照射地表的倾角划分地带，核心是“斜坡决定天气”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of climate, all traced to one image: a slanted band of the earth. The slant first names a zone, then the weather of that zone, then the mood that surrounds a group, and finally the conditions that surround a market or a debate.","cn":"climate 的九个义项都追溯到同一个意象：地球上一条倾斜的地带。倾斜先命名一个地带，再命名该地带的天气，再命名包围群体的情绪，最后命名包围市场或争论的条件。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a slope of the earth that decides what sun and weather reach it.","cn":"核心意象：地球的一段斜坡，决定阳光与天气如何到达它上面。"},"chain":["SLOPE OF THE EARTH","BAND OF LATITUDE","WEATHER OF A REGION","SURROUNDING AIR","MOOD OF A GROUP","CONDITIONS OF ACTION"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S03","en":"LAND IS MEASURED BY SLANT: the ancient zone and the region seen through its weather are the same band of ground.","cn":"土地按倾斜来量：古代气候带与按天气看待的地区，是同一条地面带。"},{"senses":"S02 · S08","en":"WEATHER BECOMES A SYSTEM: the usual conditions of a place, and the machinery of ocean and air that produces them.","cn":"天气成为系统：一地的寻常天气，以及制造它的海洋与大气机制。"},{"senses":"S04 · S07","en":"AIR BECOMES MOOD: a room's feeling and an age's accepted opinion are weather that people breathe inside.","cn":"空气变成情绪：房间的气氛与时代公认的看法，都是人们身处其中呼吸的天气。"},{"senses":"S05 · S06","en":"CONDITIONS BECOME CLIMATE: business and politics are described as surroundings no single actor controls.","cn":"条件成为气候：商业与政治被描述为任何单一行动者都无法控制的周遭环境。"},{"senses":"S09","en":"THE BAND SHRINKS: micro- reduces the climate to a garden pocket whose wall changes the sun.","cn":"条带缩小：micro- 把气候缩到花园一角，那里一堵墙就改变了阳光。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Climate is a Greek loan with a Latin-shaped ending. Its family shows the root klima 'slope' and the productive suffixes -ic, -al, -ology and -ate.","cn":"climate 是带拉丁式词尾的希腊借词。它的词族展示了词根 klima“斜坡”以及能产的 -ic、-al、-ology、-ate 后缀。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin form was clima (genitive climatis), borrowed from Greek klima. From this stem English built climatic, climatology and the verb acclimate, while Greek klinein 'to lean' also gave incline and decline.","cn":"拉丁形式是 clima（属格 climatis），借自希腊语 klima。英语从这个词干造出 climatic、climatology 和动词 acclimate，而希腊语 klinein“倾斜”还给出 incline 与 decline。"},"items":[{"word":"climate","structure":"Greek klima (slope) + Latin -atis stem","meaning":"the long-term weather of a region; a prevailing atmosphere","meaningCN":"气候；氛围（klima 斜坡 + 拉丁词干）","example":"The climate of the coast is mild all year.","exampleCN":"沿海地区全年气候温和。"},{"word":"climatic","structure":"climat- (climate stem) + -ic (adjective)","meaning":"relating to climate","meaningCN":"气候的（-ic 构成形容词）","example":"Climatic change is affecting the harvest.","exampleCN":"气候变化正在影响收成。"},{"word":"climatically","structure":"climatic + -ally (adverb)","meaning":"in terms of climate","meaningCN":"在气候方面（-ally 构成副词）","example":"The two cities are climatically very different.","exampleCN":"这两座城市在气候上差别很大。"},{"word":"climatology","structure":"climat- + -ology (study of)","meaning":"the scientific study of climate","meaningCN":"气候学（-ology 表学科）","example":"She took a degree in climatology.","exampleCN":"她取得了气候学学位。"},{"word":"climatologist","structure":"climatology + -ist (person)","meaning":"a scientist who studies climate","meaningCN":"气候学家（-ist 表人）","example":"Climatologists expect the region to get drier.","exampleCN":"气候学家预计该地区会变得更干。"},{"word":"acclimate","structure":"ad- (to) + climate","meaning":"to accustom a plant or person to a new climate","meaningCN":"使适应气候；使服水土（ad- 表朝向）","example":"The plants were acclimated to the greenhouse first.","exampleCN":"这些植物先被适应了温室的环境。"},{"word":"acclimatize","structure":"acclimate + -ize (verb)","meaning":"to become or make used to a new climate","meaningCN":"使适应气候（-ize 构成动词）","example":"It took them a week to acclimatize to the altitude.","exampleCN":"他们花了一周才适应那里的海拔。"},{"word":"microclimate","structure":"micro- (small) + climate","meaning":"the climate of a small, distinct area","meaningCN":"微气候（micro- 表微小）","example":"The valley has its own microclimate.","exampleCN":"这个山谷有它自己的微气候。"},{"word":"clime","structure":"climate shortened","meaning":"a region or its climate, chiefly literary","meaningCN":"地带；气候（climate 的缩短形式，多用于文学）","example":"He travelled to warmer climes for his health.","exampleCN":"为了健康，他去了气候更暖的地方。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"clima","structure":"Greek klima > Latin clima, climat-","meaning":"a zone or slope of the earth","meaningCN":"地带；地球的斜坡"},{"word":"klima","structure":"Greek, from klinein 'to lean'","meaning":"an inclination, a slope","meaningCN":"倾斜；斜坡"}]}},{"word":"clinical","ipa_uk":"/ˈklɪnɪkl/","ipa_us":"/ˈklɪnɪkl/","definition_zh":"临床的；诊所的；冷静客观的；简朴无装饰的","definition_en":"relating to the treatment of patients at the bedside, and by extension detached, analytical and plain","core_image":"医生俯身病床，只看症状和数字，不掺入自己的情绪","scene":"A doctor reads a chart at the bedside and says: Let's keep this clinical — just the test results.","sceneCN":"这里 clinical 是「冷静客观的、只谈事实的」（第 5 个义项：像病历报告一样不带感情）；句意：我们临床一点，只看检验结果。画面里是病床、病历夹和监护仪。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"临床的；病床旁的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"冷静客观的；不带感情的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"简朴实用的；无装饰的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"clinical trial","zh":"临床试验"},{"phrase":"clinical practice","zh":"临床实践"},{"phrase":"clinical symptoms","zh":"临床症状"},{"phrase":"a clinical approach","zh":"冷静客观的处理方式"},{"phrase":"clinical depression","zh":"临床抑郁症"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more clinical"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most clinical"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"clinically","pos":"adv.","zh":"临床上；冷静客观地"},{"word":"clinic","pos":"n.","zh":"诊所；门诊部"},{"word":"clinician","pos":"n.","zh":"临床医生"},{"word":"preclinical","pos":"adj.","zh":"临床前的；试验前的"},{"word":"subclinical","pos":"adj.","zh":"亚临床的；无明显症状的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Bedside medicine: care given at the patient's bed","titleCN":"临床的：在病人床边进行的医疗","definition":"relating to the observation and treatment of patients, especially at the bedside rather than in theory","definitionCN":"与观察和治疗病人有关的，尤指在病床边而非在理论层面","example":"Clinical medicine begins with listening carefully to the patient.","exampleCN":"临床医学从仔细倾听病人开始。","why":"Greek kline meant 'bed', and klinike techne was 'the practice at the sickbed'. Clinical marks whatever happens at that bed rather than in a lecture hall.","whyCN":"希腊语 kline 意为“床”，klinike techne 是“病床边的实践”。clinical 标记的是发生在那张床边、而不是讲堂里的事。"},{"no":"02","title":"Clinic-based: belonging to an outpatient setting","titleCN":"诊所的：属于门诊场所的","definition":"relating to a clinic or to outpatient care rather than a long hospital stay","definitionCN":"与诊所或门诊护理有关，而非长期住院","example":"The hospital opened a clinical wing for outpatients last month.","exampleCN":"这家医院上月启用了一个门诊临床区。","why":"Clinic shifted from 'bedridden person' to 'private hospital' in the 1880s. Clinical followed the building where beds are laid out, so the place gave its name to the service.","whyCN":"clinic 在 1880 年代从“卧床的人”转为“私立医院”。clinical 跟着那栋摆着病床的楼走，于是场所把名字给了服务。"},{"no":"03","title":"Observed signs: evidence the body shows","titleCN":"临床体征：身体直接呈现的证据","definition":"of symptoms or signs, observed directly in the patient rather than produced in a laboratory","definitionCN":"（症状或体征）直接观察病人所得，而非实验室制造出的","example":"The diagnosis rests on clinical signs rather than on lab tests.","exampleCN":"诊断依据的是临床体征，而不是实验室检查。","why":"What is clinical is what the bedside reveals. A clinical sign is evidence the body presents to the observer, before any machine turns it into numbers.","whyCN":"“临床的”就是病床边能看出来的。临床体征是身体直接呈现给观察者的证据，还没被机器变成数字。"},{"no":"04","title":"Trial stage: testing a treatment in patients","titleCN":"临床阶段的：在病人身上试验疗法","definition":"of research, carried out with patients rather than with cells or animals","definitionCN":"（研究）在病人身上进行，而不是在细胞或动物身上","example":"The drug entered clinical trials last spring.","exampleCN":"这种药去年春天进入了临床试验。","why":"Research becomes clinical when it moves from the lab bench to beds occupied by patients. The setting names the stage: the bed is the test site.","whyCN":"研究从实验台移到有病人的床，就叫临床。场所命名了阶段：病床就是试验场。"},{"no":"05","title":"Coldly dispassionate: a report without feeling","titleCN":"冷静客观的：不带感情的报告","definition":"expressing facts in a detached way, as if describing a medical case","definitionCN":"以超然的方式陈述事实，仿佛在描述一个病例","example":"She gave a clinical account of the accident, without a trace of anger.","exampleCN":"她冷静客观地叙述了那场事故，没有一丝怒意。","why":"This sense is recorded from 1928: a doctor describes a body as a case, not as a person. Detachment is the tone of the bedside carried into ordinary speech.","whyCN":"这一义记录于 1928 年：医生把身体描述为一个病例，而不是一个人。超然就是病床边的语调被带进了日常语言。"},{"no":"06","title":"Analytical: cutting straight to the measurable","titleCN":"精准分析的：直接切到可量之处","definition":"precise and analytical, focusing on measurable detail and excluding emotion","definitionCN":"精准而分析性的，聚焦可衡量的细节，排除情绪","example":"The coach took a clinical look at every mistake in the video.","exampleCN":"教练冷静精准地看了录像里的每一个失误。","why":"From a medical report to any report: a clinical judgment strips away feeling and keeps only what can be counted or seen, as if the subject lay on an examination table.","whyCN":"从病历报告扩展到任何报告：临床判断剥去情绪，只留下能数、能看见的东西，仿佛对象正躺在检查台上。"},{"no":"07","title":"Plain and functional: bare as an examination room","titleCN":"简朴实用的：像检查室一样素净","definition":"plain, bare and functional in appearance, without decoration","definitionCN":"外观素净、实用、没有装饰的","example":"The room was clinical: white walls, a metal bed and nothing else.","exampleCN":"那房间很素净：白墙、一张铁床，别的什么都没有。","why":"A clinic is built for cleaning and examination, not for decoration. Bare white surfaces are what hygiene looks like, so anything similarly unadorned is called clinical.","whyCN":"诊所是为清洁和检查而建，不为装饰。光裸的白色表面就是卫生的样子，于是任何同样无装饰的东西都被叫作 clinical。"},{"no":"08","title":"Bedside teaching: learning with real patients","titleCN":"临床教学的：在真实病人身上学习","definition":"relating to the part of medical education carried out with real patients","definitionCN":"与医学教育中面对真实病人的那部分有关","example":"Medical students spend their third year in clinical training.","exampleCN":"医学生在第三年接受临床训练。","why":"The original Greek practice was instruction at the sickbed, with students watching the teacher examine a patient. Clinical names the half of learning that no textbook can supply.","whyCN":"希腊语原初的做法就是在病床边教学，学生看着老师检查病人。clinical 命名了教科书给不了的那一半学习。"},{"no":"09","title":"Diagnosable: a condition that earns the label","titleCN":"临床诊断的：够得上这个标签的病症","definition":"of a condition, formally recognized and treated as an illness rather than a mood or habit","definitionCN":"（状况）被正式认定为疾病并加以治疗，而非仅是一时情绪或习惯","example":"The doctor treated it as clinical depression, not mere sadness.","exampleCN":"医生把它当作临床抑郁症来治疗，而不只是悲伤。","why":"To call a condition clinical is to move it into the world of beds, charts and diagnostic criteria. It becomes an illness to be treated, not a mood to be endured.","whyCN":"把一个状况叫作 clinical，就是把它移进病床、病历和诊断标准的世界。它成了要治疗的病，而不是要忍受的情绪。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Clinical is the adjective of the sickbed. Greek kline 'bed' gave the word for a physician who visits patients in their beds, and English kept the bed in every later sense.","cn":"clinical 是病床的形容词。希腊语 kline“床”给出了“到床边看病人的医生”一词，英语在后来每个义项里都保留着那张床。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK","en":"Kline meant 'bed, couch, that on which one lies'. From it came klinikos 'of the bed' and klinike techne 'the practice at the sickbed'.","cn":"kline 意为“床、卧榻、人躺卧其上之物”。由它产生 klinikos“床的”和 klinike techne“病床边的实践”。"},{"era":"LATIN","en":"Latin clinicus meant 'a physician who visits patients in their beds', a direct borrowing of the Greek idea of medicine done at the bed.","cn":"拉丁语 clinicus 意为“到病人床边看病的医生”，直接借用了希腊语“在床边行医”的观念。"},{"era":"1620s ENGLISH","en":"The noun clinic first meant 'a bedridden person, one confined to bed by sickness'. A related sense was 'one who defer baptism until the death-bed' (1660s).","cn":"名词 clinic 最初指“卧床的人、因病困在床上的人”。相关义项还有“拖延到临终才受洗的人”（1660 年代）。"},{"era":"1780 ENGLISH","en":"Clinical is recorded in 1780 as 'pertaining to hospital patients or hospital care', formed from clinic + -al. The earlier adjective was clinic 'of the sick-bed' from the 1620s.","cn":"clinical 记录于 1780 年，意为“与医院病人或医院护理有关的”，由 clinic + -al 构成。更早的形容词是 1620 年代的 clinic“病床的”。"},{"era":"1884–1928","en":"Clinic 'private hospital' comes from German Klinik in 1884, through the notion of bedside teaching. Clinical 'coldly dispassionate' is recorded from 1928, like a medical report.","cn":"clinic 的“私立医院”义来自 1884 年的德语 Klinik，经由“床边教学”的观念。clinical“冷静不带感情”记录于 1928 年，如一份病历报告。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Kline is traced to PIE *klei- 'to lean', also behind incline, decline and recline. The reconstructed root has no written attestation, so the deepest step is source uncertain.","cn":"kline 被追溯到原始印欧语 *klei-“倾斜”，incline、decline、recline 也出自这里。该重构词根没有书面记录，故最深层来源不确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"clinic","ipa":"/ˈklɪnɪk/","tag":"base noun","definition":"a place where people receive medical advice or treatment. It is the noun that clinical was built on.","definitionCN":"诊所；门诊部。它是 clinical 所依附的名词。"},{"word":"clinician","ipa":"/klɪˈnɪʃn/","tag":"person noun","definition":"a doctor who treats patients directly rather than doing only research. It is clinic + -ian.","definitionCN":"临床医生。它是 clinic 加 -ian，指直接看病人而非只做研究的医生。"},{"word":"clinch","ipa":"/klɪntʃ/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"to settle a matter or secure a win. It shares the clin- opening but is unrelated to beds.","definitionCN":"敲定；确保获胜。它同样以 clin- 开头，但与病床无关。"},{"word":"incline","ipa":"/ɪnˈklaɪn/","tag":"same PIE root","definition":"to lean or slope, or to tend toward something. It comes from the same *klei- 'to lean' root as kline.","definitionCN":"倾斜；倾向于。它与 kline 同出 *klei-“倾斜”词根。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"medical","ipa":"/ˈmedɪkl/","tag":"medicine","definition":"relating to medicine in general. It is broader than clinical and can describe theory as well as practice.","definitionCN":"医学的。它比 clinical 更宽，既可指实践也可指理论。"},{"word":"detached","ipa":"/dɪˈtætʃt/","tag":"emotion","definition":"not showing personal feelings. It matches the 'coldly dispassionate' sense but says nothing about beds.","definitionCN":"超然的；不带个人感情的。它对应“冷静客观”义，但不涉及病床。"},{"word":"objective","ipa":"/əbˈdʒektɪv/","tag":"judgment","definition":"based on facts rather than feelings. It is close to the analytical sense of clinical.","definitionCN":"客观的；基于事实而非感情的。它接近 clinical 的分析义。"},{"word":"dispassionate","ipa":"/dɪsˈpæʃənət/","tag":"tone","definition":"calm and not influenced by emotion. It is the direct synonym of clinical in its 1928 sense.","definitionCN":"冷静公正的；不受情绪影响的。它就是 clinical 1928 年那一义的直接同义词。"},{"word":"sterile","ipa":"/ˈsteraɪl/","tag":"appearance","definition":"free from bacteria, or lacking warmth and life. It overlaps with the plain, bare sense of clinical.","definitionCN":"无菌的；也指缺乏生气。它与 clinical 的素净、无装饰义重叠。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Greek kline 'bed', the clinic family, and the derived forms English actually uses.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：希腊语 kline“床”、clinic 词族，以及英语实际使用的派生形式。"},"normal":[{"en":"clinical = kline 'bed' + -al: whatever belongs to the sickbed.","cn":"clinical = kline“床”+ -al：属于病床的一切。"},{"en":"clinic first meant a bedridden person, then the building where such people were treated.","cn":"clinic 先指卧床的人，再指治疗这些人的那栋楼。"},{"en":"A clinical report sounds like a doctor reading a chart: facts only, no anger, no tears.","cn":"clinical 的报告听起来像医生读病历：只有事实，没有怒气，没有眼泪。"},{"en":"A clinical trial is named for its setting: the trial happens at patients' beds, not at a lab bench.","cn":"临床试验因场所得名：试验发生在病人床边，不在实验台。"},{"en":"A clinical room is white, bare and easy to clean, because a clinic is built for hygiene rather than beauty.","cn":"clinical 的房间洁白、空旷、好打扫，因为诊所是为卫生而非美观而建。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core operation is looking at a person the way a doctor looks at a case: closely, but from outside.","cn":"核心动作是像医生看病例那样看一个人：看得很近，但站在外面。"},{"en":"The bed supplies both the authority and the chill: nearness to suffering produces detachment as its professional tone.","cn":"病床同时提供权威与寒意：离痛苦太近，超然就成了它的职业语调。"},{"en":"So medical care, detached tone, precise analysis and bare surfaces are one stance: examine, measure, do not merge.","cn":"所以医疗服务、冷静语气、精准分析与素净表面是同一种姿态：检查、测量，但不与之融为一体。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The new drug is still in clinical trials.","cn":"这种新药仍在临床试验中。"},{"en":"He described the scene in a clinical, almost cold voice.","cn":"他用一种冷静、近乎冷淡的声音描述了那个场景。"},{"en":"The ward was clean and clinical, with no flowers allowed.","cn":"病房干净而素净，不允许摆放鲜花。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音拆分 · 非词源","text":"cli 像 clean（干净）+ ni 像 nurse（护士）——干净得像护士站的病房 → clinical 临床的、冷静的","word":"clinical"},"root":"源自希腊语 kline“床、卧榻”，经 klinikos“床的”、拉丁语 clinicus“床边行医的医生”进入英语，核心是“病床边”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of clinical, all traced to one place: the sickbed. What happens at the bed is medical; the tone used at the bed is detached; the room built for the bed is bare; and a condition serious enough for the bed is diagnosable.","cn":"clinical 的九个义项都追溯到一个地方：病床。床边发生的事是医疗；床边用的语气是冷静；为病床而建的房间是素净；严重到需要上床的状况是可诊断的。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a doctor at the sickbed, observing closely and recording without feeling.","cn":"核心意象：医生守在病床边，看得仔细，记录时不掺感情。"},"chain":["BED","BEDSIDE PRACTICE","PATIENT CARE","DETACHED TONE","BARE SETTING","DIAGNOSED CONDITION"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S02","en":"THE BED DEFINES THE MEDICINE: care at the patient's bed, and the clinic building where that bed stands.","cn":"病床定义了医学：病人床边的照护，以及摆放那张床的诊所大楼。"},{"senses":"S03 · S04","en":"THE BED DEFINES THE EVIDENCE: signs the body shows, and trials run on patients rather than cells.","cn":"病床定义了证据：身体呈现的体征，以及在病人而非细胞身上做的试验。"},{"senses":"S05 · S06","en":"THE BED DEFINES THE TONE: a case described without feeling, and any judgment stripped to measurable detail.","cn":"病床定义了语调：不带感情地描述病例，以及任何被剥到可量细节的判断。"},{"senses":"S07","en":"THE BED DEFINES THE ROOM: white, bare and easy to clean, because hygiene outranks decoration.","cn":"病床定义了房间：洁白、空旷、易打扫，因为卫生优先于装饰。"},{"senses":"S08 · S09","en":"THE BED DEFINES LEARNING AND ILLNESS: students learn at real beds, and a condition serious enough for the bed becomes a diagnosis.","cn":"病床定义了学习与疾病：学生在真实的床边学习，严重到需要卧床的状况成为诊断。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Clinical is clinic + -al. Its family shows the Greek bed-root kline, the person suffix -ian, the negation prefix non-, and the size prefixes pre- and sub-.","cn":"clinical 是 clinic + -al。它的词族展示了希腊语“床”词根 kline、表人后缀 -ian、否定前缀 non-，以及表程度前缀 pre- 与 sub-。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin source is clinicus 'bedside physician', from Greek klinikos 'of the bed' and kline 'bed'. English added -al, -ian, -ly and the medical prefixes pre-, sub- and non-.","cn":"拉丁来源是 clinicus“床边医生”，出自希腊语 klinikos“床的”和 kline“床”。英语加上 -al、-ian、-ly 以及医学前缀 pre-、sub-、non-。"},"items":[{"word":"clinical","structure":"clinic + -al (adjective)","meaning":"relating to patients, or detached and plain","meaningCN":"临床的；冷静客观的（-al 构成形容词）","example":"The clinical staff meet every morning at eight.","exampleCN":"临床人员每天早上八点开会。"},{"word":"clinic","structure":"Greek klinike (techne), practice at the sickbed","meaning":"a place for medical advice or treatment","meaningCN":"诊所；门诊部（原指病床边的医术）","example":"She works at a clinic in the suburbs.","exampleCN":"她在郊区的一家诊所工作。"},{"word":"clinician","structure":"clinic + -ian (person)","meaning":"a doctor who treats patients directly","meaningCN":"临床医生（-ian 表人）","example":"The clinician ordered another blood test.","exampleCN":"临床医生又开了一项血液检查。"},{"word":"clinically","structure":"clinical + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a clinical manner; in medical terms","meaningCN":"临床上；冷静客观地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The patient was clinically dead for two minutes.","exampleCN":"这名病人在临床上死亡了两分钟。"},{"word":"preclinical","structure":"pre- (before) + clinical","meaning":"before a treatment is tested in patients","meaningCN":"临床前的；试验前的（pre- 表之前）","example":"The drug passed preclinical tests on mice.","exampleCN":"这种药通过了在小鼠身上的临床前试验。"},{"word":"subclinical","structure":"sub- (below) + clinical","meaning":"present but not strong enough to show clear symptoms","meaningCN":"亚临床的；症状不明显的（sub- 表低于）","example":"The infection remained subclinical for weeks.","exampleCN":"感染在数周内一直处于亚临床状态。"},{"word":"nonclinical","structure":"non- (not) + clinical","meaning":"not related to direct patient care","meaningCN":"非临床的（non- 表否定）","example":"She moved from research into a nonclinical role.","exampleCN":"她从研究转到了非临床岗位。"},{"word":"polyclinic","structure":"poly- (many) + clinic","meaning":"a clinic treating many kinds of disease","meaningCN":"综合诊所；多科诊所（poly- 表多）","example":"The polyclinic has cardiology and dermatology units.","exampleCN":"这家综合诊所有心脏科和皮肤科。"},{"word":"clinicopathological","structure":"clinic + -o- + pathological","meaning":"combining bedside findings with the study of disease tissue","meaningCN":"临床病理的（临床 + 连接元音 + 病理的）","example":"The case was settled by clinicopathological review.","exampleCN":"这个病例通过临床病理复核得以定论。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"clinicus","structure":"Latin, from Greek klinikos","meaning":"a physician who visits patients in their beds","meaningCN":"到病人床边看病的医生"},{"word":"kline","structure":"Greek","meaning":"bed, couch","meaningCN":"床；卧榻"},{"word":"klinike","structure":"Greek klinike (techne)","meaning":"the practice at the sickbed","meaningCN":"病床边的医术"}]}},{"word":"coherent","ipa_uk":"/kəʊˈhɪərənt/","ipa_us":"/koʊˈhɪrənt/","definition_zh":"连贯的；前后一致的；黏合在一起的；相干的","definition_en":"sticking together so that the parts form a connected, consistent whole","core_image":"许多散块被黏成一体，抽掉哪一块，整体就散架","scene":"An editor taps a paragraph and says: This paragraph is clear, but the essay as a whole is not coherent yet.","sceneCN":"这里 coherent 是「（文章整体）连贯的、前后一致的」（第 1 个义项）；句意：这一段本身清楚，但整篇文章还不够连贯。画面里是红笔、稿件和贴满便签的墙。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"连贯的；有条理的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"一致的；协调的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"（物理）相干的；黏合的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a coherent argument","zh":"连贯的论证"},{"phrase":"coherent policy","zh":"协调一致的政策"},{"phrase":"coherent whole","zh":"连贯的整体"},{"phrase":"coherent light","zh":"相干光"},{"phrase":"remain coherent","zh":"保持连贯"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级","form":"more coherent"},{"label":"最高级","form":"most coherent"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"coherence","pos":"n.","zh":"连贯性；一致性；相干性"},{"word":"coherently","pos":"adv.","zh":"连贯地；有条理地"},{"word":"incoherent","pos":"adj.","zh":"不连贯的；语无伦次的"},{"word":"cohere","pos":"v.","zh":"黏合；连贯一致"},{"word":"cohesion","pos":"n.","zh":"黏合；凝聚力"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Text: parts joined so the meaning flows","titleCN":"连贯的：各部分接上，意思能流动","definition":"of speech or writing, logically connected and easy to follow","definitionCN":"（口语或文章）逻辑连接、容易跟上的","example":"Her essay is coherent from the first paragraph to the last.","exampleCN":"她的文章从第一段到最后一段都很连贯。","why":"The Latin verb meant 'to stick together'. Sentences cohere when each one sticks to the next, so the reader can walk across the paragraph without a gap.","whyCN":"那个拉丁动词本义是“黏在一起”。句子彼此黏住，读者就能走过整段而没有断口，这就是连贯。"},{"no":"02","title":"Argument: claims that hold each other up","titleCN":"一致的：论点彼此支撑","definition":"of ideas or an argument, consistent with one another and forming a single case","definitionCN":"（观点或论证）彼此一致，构成一个整体主张","example":"The theory is coherent: every claim supports the next.","exampleCN":"这个理论前后一致：每个主张都支撑下一个。","why":"Sticking together is not mere sequence but mutual support. In an argument each claim must adhere to the others, or the structure pulls apart when one is pressed.","whyCN":"黏在一起不只是排成顺序，而是互相支撑。在论证里，每个主张都得附着在别的主张上，否则一压就散。"},{"no":"03","title":"Person: a mind whose words still connect","titleCN":"表达清楚的：话还连得起来的人","definition":"of a person, able to think and speak in a clear, connected way","definitionCN":"（人）能够清楚、有条理地思考和表达的","example":"The patient was drowsy but coherent after the operation.","exampleCN":"手术之后病人昏昏欲睡，但说话还有条理。","why":"When the mind holds together, its output holds together. A coherent patient is one whose thoughts still stick to one another, which is why doctors test coherence after sedation.","whyCN":"思维黏得住，说出的话就黏得住。coherent 的病人是思想仍彼此相连的人，所以医生在麻醉后要测试“连贯性”。"},{"no":"04","title":"Waves: crests that keep the same step","titleCN":"相干的：波峰始终踩着同一步点","definition":"of waves, having the same frequency and a constant phase difference, so they can interfere stably","definitionCN":"（波）频率相同、相位差恒定，因而能稳定干涉的","example":"Two coherent beams produce a stable interference pattern.","exampleCN":"两束相干光产生稳定的干涉图样。","why":"Physics took the 'sticking together' image literally: wave crests that stay locked in step remain glued to one another over distance, so their pattern does not blur.","whyCN":"物理学把这个“黏在一起”的意象照字面用了：波峰始终同步，就在长距离上彼此黏住，图样因此不会糊掉。"},{"no":"05","title":"Group: many wills acting as one body","titleCN":"协调一致的：众多意志像一个身体那样行动","definition":"of a group or policy, united and consistent so that the parts do not work against each other","definitionCN":"（群体或政策）统一而一致，各部分不相互抵触","example":"The party needs a coherent policy on housing.","exampleCN":"这个党需要一套协调一致的住房政策。","why":"A group is coherent when its members stick to one line. The physical image of parts adhering becomes social: no faction pulls away from the whole.","whyCN":"一个群体在成员都黏在一条线上时才是连贯的。部分附着的物理意象变成社会意象：没有哪一派从整体上扯开。"},{"no":"06","title":"Substance: a mass that holds its shape","titleCN":"黏合的：能保持形状的一团物质","definition":"of a material, sticking together firmly as a single mass","definitionCN":"（材料）牢固地黏成一团","example":"The wet clay stayed coherent enough to be shaped by hand.","exampleCN":"湿黏土黏得足够结实，可以用手塑形。","why":"This is the oldest physical sense: particles that adhere to one another form a coherent mass. Everything abstract later borrows this picture of a body that does not crumble.","whyCN":"这是最古老的物理义：相互附着的颗粒形成一团黏合的物质。后来一切抽象用法都借用了这个“不散架的身体”的图景。"},{"no":"07","title":"Laser light: one wavelength in lockstep","titleCN":"相干光：步调一致的一束光","definition":"of light, having a single wavelength and a fixed phase relationship, as in a laser","definitionCN":"（光）波长单一、相位关系固定，如激光","example":"A coherent beam can carry a signal across a room without spreading.","exampleCN":"相干光束能把信号送过房间而不发散。","why":"Ordinary light is a crowd of waves out of step; laser light is a column marching in step. Coherent here means the waves are so glued in rhythm that the beam stays narrow.","whyCN":"普通光是步调杂乱的一群波；激光是齐步走的一列。这里的 coherent 指波在节奏上黏得如此紧，光束因此保持狭窄。"},{"no":"08","title":"Account: a story with no missing joints","titleCN":"条理清楚的：关节齐全的叙述","definition":"of an account or explanation, orderly and intelligible, with no gaps in the sequence","definitionCN":"（叙述或解释）有条理、可理解，顺序上没有缺环","example":"He gave a coherent account of what happened that night.","exampleCN":"他对那晚发生的事做了条理清楚的叙述。","why":"A story coheres when cause sticks to effect and each scene sticks to the next. Where a joint is missing, the listener feels the seam, and we say the account is incoherent.","whyCN":"当因黏住果、每一幕黏住下一幕时，故事就连贯。缺一个关节，听者就摸到接缝，我们便说叙述不连贯。"},{"no":"09","title":"Strategy: a plan whose pieces agree","titleCN":"成体系的：各块彼此呼应的计划","definition":"of a plan or set of actions, internally consistent and aimed at one goal","definitionCN":"（计划或行动组合）内部一致、指向同一目标","example":"The company lacks a coherent strategy for its overseas branches.","exampleCN":"这家公司对其海外分支机构缺乏一套连贯的战略。","why":"A strategy is coherent when its decisions stick to one aim; if each department pulls in its own direction, the plan has no single body to hold it together.","whyCN":"当各项决策都黏在同一个目标上，战略才连贯；若每个部门各自拉扯，计划就没有一个整体来维持它。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Coherent comes from Latin cohaerere, 'to stick together'. The physical sense of parts adhering is the source of every later sense: text, argument, group, mind and light all 'hold together'.","cn":"coherent 来自拉丁语 cohaerere“黏在一起”。部分附着的物理义是后来一切义项的源头：文章、论证、群体、心智、光，全都“黏得住”。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Cohaerere meant 'to stick together, be connected'. It was com- 'together' plus haerere 'to adhere, stick, cling'.","cn":"cohaerere 意为“黏在一起、相连”，由 com-“一起”加 haerere“附着、黏住、紧贴”构成。"},{"era":"1550s ENGLISH","en":"The adjective enters English as 'harmonious', a sense close to the Latin participle: things that fit and hold together without conflict.","cn":"该形容词以“和谐的”义进入英语，接近拉丁分词的意思：彼此贴合、黏在一起而不冲突。"},{"era":"1570s ENGLISH","en":"By the 1570s it also meant 'sticking together' physically, and 'connected, consistent' of speech and thought.","cn":"到 1570 年代，它也表示物理上的“黏在一起”，以及言语和思想上的“连贯、一致”。"},{"era":"17c–19c SCIENCE","en":"Optics and later physics adopted coherence for waves that keep a fixed phase relationship; a coherent beam is literally a set of waves marching in step.","cn":"光学及后来的物理学采用 coherence 指保持固定相位关系的波；相干光束字面上就是齐步走的一组波。"},{"era":"MODERN ENGLISH","en":"Modern usage extends the word to persons ('coherent after the accident'), to organizations and to policy, always asking whether the parts still hold together.","cn":"现代用法把该词扩展到人（“事故后神志清楚”）、组织与政策，问的始终是：各部分是否还黏得住。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Haerere itself is of uncertain origin. Watkins proposed PIE *ghais- 'to adhere', but some linguists reject the link and de Vaan offers no etymology, so the deepest step is source uncertain.","cn":"haerere 本身来源不确定。Watkins 提出原始印欧语 *ghais-“附着”，但一些语言学家否定这一联系，de Vaan 也未给出词源，故最深层来源不确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"cohere","ipa":"/kəʊˈhɪə(r)/","tag":"base verb","definition":"to stick together or be logically connected. It is the verb behind coherent.","definitionCN":"黏合；连贯一致。它是 coherent 背后的动词。"},{"word":"coherence","ipa":"/kəʊˈhɪərəns/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"the quality of being connected and consistent. It is the noun of coherent.","definitionCN":"连贯性；一致性。它是 coherent 的名词。"},{"word":"incoherent","ipa":"/ˌɪnkəʊˈhɪərənt/","tag":"negated form","definition":"not connected or not able to speak clearly. It is in- 'not' plus coherent.","definitionCN":"不连贯的；语无伦次的。它是 in-“不”加 coherent。"},{"word":"adherent","ipa":"/ədˈhɪərənt/","tag":"same root","definition":"sticking to a surface, or a supporter of a cause. It shares the Latin root haerere 'to stick'.","definitionCN":"附着的；拥护者。它与 coherent 同出拉丁词根 haerere“黏住”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"consistent","ipa":"/kənˈsɪstənt/","tag":"agreement","definition":"always behaving or being stated in the same way. It stresses agreement over time rather than physical joining.","definitionCN":"一致的；始终如一的。它强调时间上的相符，而非物理连接。"},{"word":"logical","ipa":"/ˈlɒdʒɪkl/","tag":"reasoning","definition":"following clear rules of reasoning. It focuses on inference, while coherent focuses on the whole holding together.","definitionCN":"合乎逻辑的。它聚焦推理规则，而 coherent 聚焦整体是否黏得住。"},{"word":"cohesive","ipa":"/kəʊˈhiːsɪv/","tag":"sticking","definition":"forming a united whole; tending to stick together. It is close to the physical and social senses of coherent.","definitionCN":"有凝聚力的；黏合的。它接近 coherent 的物理义与社会义。"},{"word":"unified","ipa":"/ˈjuːnɪfaɪd/","tag":"one body","definition":"made into a single whole. It describes the result, where coherent describes the holding-together.","definitionCN":"统一的；一体化的。它描述结果，而 coherent 描述黏合的状态。"},{"word":"lucid","ipa":"/ˈluːsɪd/","tag":"clarity","definition":"expressed clearly and easy to understand. It matches the clarity of a coherent explanation but not its structure.","definitionCN":"清晰易懂的。它对应连贯解释的清晰，但不涉及结构。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Latin com- and haerere, the cohere family, and the derived forms English actually uses.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 com- 与 haerere、cohere 词族，以及英语实际使用的派生形式。"},"normal":[{"en":"coherent = co- 'together' + haerere 'to stick': the parts are glued, so the whole holds.","cn":"coherent = co-“一起”+ haerere“黏”：各部分被黏住，整体才立得住。"},{"en":"The same haerere gives adhere, adherent and adhesion: all about one thing clinging to another.","cn":"同一个 haerere 还给出 adhere、adherent、adhesion：都是关于一物紧贴另一物。"},{"en":"coherence is what an essay, a policy and a laser beam can all have: the pieces keep the same step.","cn":"coherence 是文章、政策和激光束都能有的东西：各块保持同一步点。"},{"en":"incoherent is in- 'not' + coherent: words that will not stick, so a drunk or a feverish person becomes incoherent.","cn":"incoherent 是 in-“不”+ coherent：话黏不起来，所以醉酒或发烧的人会语无伦次。"},{"en":"Doctors ask a patient to count backwards to test whether the mind is still coherent.","cn":"医生让病人倒着数数，就是测试他的思维是否还连贯。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core operation is adhesion: separate pieces must grip one another before anything larger can exist.","cn":"核心动作是黏附：分开的块必须先互相咬住，更大的东西才可能存在。"},{"en":"The same grip is scaled to sentences, arguments, groups, minds and waves; in each case the test is whether a piece can be pulled away.","cn":"同一种咬合被缩放到句子、论证、群体、心智和波；每一次的检验都是：能否把某一块抽走。"},{"en":"So 'logical', 'consistent', 'unified' and 'in step' are not separate meanings but one question: does the whole still hold when pressed?","cn":"所以“合乎逻辑、前后一致、统一、同步”并非彼此无关，而是同一个问题：受压时整体还立得住吗？"}]},"examples":[{"en":"She gave a clear and coherent explanation of the new rules.","cn":"她对新规则做了清楚而连贯的解释。"},{"en":"The government has failed to produce a coherent energy policy.","cn":"政府未能拿出一套协调一致的能源政策。"},{"en":"The witness was too shaken to give a coherent account.","cn":"那名证人受惊过度，无法做出条理清楚的叙述。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音拆分 · 非词源","text":"co（一起）+ here（这里）+ ent——把所有材料都“一起放在这里”黏住 → coherent 连贯的","word":"coherent"},"root":"源自拉丁语 cohaerere“黏在一起”，由 com-“一起”+ haerere“附着、黏住”构成，核心是“各部分黏成一体”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of coherent, all traced to one act: parts sticking together. Sentences, claims, minds, waves, groups, clay, laser light, stories and strategies are all tested by whether their pieces still hold.","cn":"coherent 的九个义项都追溯到一个动作：各部分黏在一起。句子、主张、心智、波、群体、黏土、激光、故事与战略，检验的都是各块是否还黏得住。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: separate pieces adhering into one body that does not fall apart.","cn":"核心意象：分开的块黏附成一个不散架的整体。"},"chain":["STICK TOGETHER","HOLD AS A MASS","CONNECT IN SPEECH","AGREE IN THOUGHT","ACT AS ONE GROUP","KEEP IN STEP"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S08","en":"WORDS STICK: sentences joined into a flowing text, and events joined into an intelligible account.","cn":"词句黏合：句子接成流动的文章，事件接成可理解的叙述。"},{"senses":"S02 · S09","en":"CLAIMS STICK: an argument whose claims support one another, and a strategy whose decisions serve one aim.","cn":"主张黏合：论点彼此支撑的论证，以及决策服务同一目标的战略。"},{"senses":"S03","en":"THE MIND STICKS: a person whose thoughts still connect, the medical test of coherence.","cn":"心智黏合：思想仍能相连的人，也就是医学上的连贯性测试。"},{"senses":"S04 · S07","en":"WAVES STICK: crests locked in phase, from interference patterns to a laser beam that does not spread.","cn":"波黏合：波峰锁在同一相位，从干涉图样到不发散的激光束。"},{"senses":"S05 · S06","en":"BODIES STICK: clay that holds its shape, and a group whose members hold one line.","cn":"形体黏合：保持形状的黏土，以及成员守同一条线的群体。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Coherent is co- + haerere + -ent. Its family shows the prefix com-/co-, the root haer- 'stick', and the suffixes -ent, -ence, -sion and -ive.","cn":"coherent 是 co- + haerere + -ent。它的词族展示了前缀 com-/co-、词根 haer-“黏”，以及后缀 -ent、-ence、-sion、-ive。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin verb cohaerere 'to stick together' yields coherent, coherence and cohere. Its participle haesus gives cohesion, while adhaerere gives adhere and adherent.","cn":"拉丁动词 cohaerere“黏在一起”给出 coherent、coherence、cohere。它的分词 haesus 给出 cohesion，而 adhaerere 给出 adhere 与 adherent。"},"items":[{"word":"coherent","structure":"co- (together) + haerere (stick) + -ent (adjective)","meaning":"connected and consistent; sticking together","meaningCN":"连贯的；一致的；黏合的（-ent 构成形容词）","example":"The report is coherent and well argued.","exampleCN":"这份报告连贯且论证充分。"},{"word":"coherently","structure":"coherent + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a connected, consistent way","meaningCN":"连贯地；有条理地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"He could not speak coherently after the fall.","exampleCN":"摔倒后他说话语无伦次。"},{"word":"coherence","structure":"coherent + -ence (noun)","meaning":"the state of sticking together or being consistent","meaningCN":"连贯性；一致性；相干性（-ence 构成名词）","example":"The essay lacks coherence between paragraphs.","exampleCN":"这篇文章段与段之间缺乏连贯。"},{"word":"incoherent","structure":"in- (not) + coherent","meaning":"not connected; unable to speak clearly","meaningCN":"不连贯的；语无伦次的（in- 表否定）","example":"He was incoherent with pain.","exampleCN":"他痛得语无伦次。"},{"word":"incoherence","structure":"in- (not) + coherence","meaning":"lack of connection or clarity","meaningCN":"不连贯；语无伦次（in- 表否定）","example":"The incoherence of the plan worried investors.","exampleCN":"计划的不连贯让投资者担忧。"},{"word":"cohere","structure":"co- + haerere (verb)","meaning":"to stick together or be logically consistent","meaningCN":"黏合；连贯一致（动词原形）","example":"The chapters cohere into a single story.","exampleCN":"这些章节黏合成一个完整的故事。"},{"word":"cohesion","structure":"co- + haesus (pp of haerere) + -ion","meaning":"the act or state of sticking together; unity","meaningCN":"黏合；凝聚力（-ion 构成名词）","example":"Sport builds cohesion within a team.","exampleCN":"运动能建立团队内部的凝聚力。"},{"word":"adhere","structure":"ad- (to) + haerere (stick)","meaning":"to stick fast to a surface or follow a rule closely","meaningCN":"附着；坚持（ad- 表朝向）","example":"The tape adheres to damp surfaces.","exampleCN":"这种胶带能粘在潮湿表面。"},{"word":"adherent","structure":"adhere + -ent (person or adjective)","meaning":"sticking to something; a supporter of a cause","meaningCN":"附着的；拥护者（-ent 表人或形容词）","example":"He is a loyal adherent of the old theory.","exampleCN":"他是旧理论的忠实拥护者。"},{"word":"inhere","structure":"in- (in) + haerere (stick)","meaning":"to exist as a natural quality in something","meaningCN":"固有；内在（in- 表在内）","example":"Risk inheres in every investment.","exampleCN":"每一项投资都固有风险。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"cohaerere","structure":"com- + haerere","meaning":"to stick together, be connected","meaningCN":"黏在一起；相连"},{"word":"haerere","structure":"Latin","meaning":"to adhere, stick, cling","meaningCN":"附着；黏住；紧贴"},{"word":"cohaerens","structure":"present participle of cohaerere","meaning":"sticking together; consistent","meaningCN":"黏在一起的；连贯的"}]}},{"word":"coincide","ipa_uk":"/ˌkəʊɪnˈsaɪd/","ipa_us":"/ˌkoʊɪnˈsaɪd/","definition_zh":"同时发生；位置重合；完全一致；巧合","definition_en":"to fall on the same point in time or space, or to agree exactly","core_image":"两条本来分开的轨迹，最后落到同一个点上","scene":"Two friends meet on the platform and one says: What a coincidence — our trains coincided by the minute.","sceneCN":"这里 coincide 是「（时间上）同时发生、恰好重合」（第 1 个义项）；句意：真巧，我们两趟车分秒不差地同时到站。画面里是站台、两只对上的手表和同一块站牌。","pos":[{"tag":"vi.","zh":"同时发生；恰好重合"},{"tag":"vi.","zh":"一致；相符"},{"tag":"vi.","zh":"（几何）重合"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"coincide with","zh":"与……同时发生；与……相符"},{"phrase":"coincide in time","zh":"在时间上重合"},{"phrase":"views coincide","zh":"观点一致"},{"phrase":"interests coincide","zh":"利益相符"},{"phrase":"coincide exactly","zh":"完全重合；分毫不差"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单","form":"coincides"},{"label":"过去式","form":"coincided"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"coincided"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"coinciding"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"coincidence","pos":"n.","zh":"巧合；同时发生；重合"},{"word":"coincident","pos":"adj.","zh":"同时发生的；重合的"},{"word":"coincidental","pos":"adj.","zh":"巧合的；偶然的"},{"word":"coincidentally","pos":"adv.","zh":"碰巧；巧合地"},{"word":"coinciding","pos":"adj.","zh":"同时发生的；重合的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Time: two events land on one moment","titleCN":"同时发生：两件事落在同一个时刻","definition":"to happen at the same time as something else","definitionCN":"与另一事同时发生","example":"The conference coincides with the start of the harvest.","exampleCN":"会议恰好与收割的开始同时。","why":"The Latin verb was com- 'together' + incidere 'to fall upon'. Two events coincide when they fall on the same instant, as two arrows hitting one mark.","whyCN":"那个拉丁动词是 com-“一起”+ incidere“落到……上”。两件事同时发生，就是它们落到同一个瞬间，像两支箭射中同一个点。"},{"no":"02","title":"Space: two things occupy one place","titleCN":"位置重合：两物占着同一处空间","definition":"to occupy the same space or position","definitionCN":"占据同一空间或位置","example":"The two beams coincide at the centre of the lens.","exampleCN":"两束光在透镜中心重合。","why":"Falling together in space is the literal image: two bodies descend onto one point and can no longer be told apart by position.","whyCN":"在空间里“一起落下”是最字面的意象：两个物体落到同一个点上，位置再也分不出彼此。"},{"no":"03","title":"Identity: two things turn out to be one","titleCN":"同一：两样东西其实是同一个","definition":"to be identical in substance or nature with something else","definitionCN":"在实质或性质上与另一事物完全相同","example":"His account of the night coincides exactly with hers.","exampleCN":"他对那晚的叙述与她的完全一致。","why":"If two descriptions fall on the same point, the gap between them disappears. Coinciding here means the two versions cannot be separated by any detail.","whyCN":"如果两份叙述落到同一点上，它们之间的缝隙就消失了。这里的重合指两个版本在任何细节上都分不开。"},{"no":"04","title":"Opinion: two minds meet on a point","titleCN":"意见一致：两个头脑在一点上相遇","definition":"of views or interests, to agree or be in harmony","definitionCN":"（观点或利益）一致或和谐","example":"Our views on the merger coincide almost completely.","exampleCN":"我们对合并的看法几乎完全一致。","why":"Opinions are paths that can arrive at the same conclusion. When they coincide, two people stand on one point, even if they started from different places.","whyCN":"意见是可能抵达同一结论的路径。当它们重合，两个人就站在同一个点上，哪怕出发处不同。"},{"no":"05","title":"Geometry: lines laid on lines","titleCN":"几何重合：线与线叠在一起","definition":"of geometric points, lines or figures, to occupy exactly the same position","definitionCN":"（几何的点、线或图形）占据完全相同的位置","example":"If the two circles coincide, every point on one lies on the other.","exampleCN":"如果两个圆重合，一个圆上的每一点都在另一个圆上。","why":"Geometry strips away everything but position. Coinciding figures are two names for one set of points, the purest case of 'falling on the same spot'.","whyCN":"几何剥掉了一切，只剩位置。重合的图形是同一组点的两个名字，这是“落到同一处”最纯粹的情形。"},{"no":"06","title":"Calendar: a date falls on another date","titleCN":"日期相撞：一个日子落在另一个日子上","definition":"of dates or occasions, to fall on the same day","definitionCN":"（日期或场合）落在同一天","example":"Her birthday coincides with the first day of the spring festival.","exampleCN":"她的生日恰好是春节的第一天。","why":"Calendars are grids of slots; two occasions coincide when they drop into one slot. The metaphor is spatial, but the space is made of dates.","whyCN":"日历是一格一格的槽；两个日子同时落进同一格，就是重合。比喻是空间的，只是这个空间由日期构成。"},{"no":"07","title":"Chance: a meeting that was not arranged","titleCN":"巧合：并非安排却撞在一起","definition":"of events, to happen together by chance, without a planned connection","definitionCN":"（事件）偶然同时发生，并无计划中的联系","example":"Their arrivals coincided, though neither knew the other was coming.","exampleCN":"他们同时到达，尽管谁也不知道对方会来。","why":"The word describes the landing, not the cause. When two paths meet without a planner, the meeting looks like chance, and coincidence becomes the name for that surprise.","whyCN":"这个词描述的是“落点”，不是原因。两条路径在没有安排者的情况下相遇，这次相遇就显得偶然，coincidence 便成了这种意外的名字。"},{"no":"08","title":"Fit: a result lands on what was wanted","titleCN":"相符：结果正好落在所愿之处","definition":"to correspond exactly to a need, wish or expectation","definitionCN":"与需求、愿望或预期完全相符","example":"The new branch's opening coincided with a surge in demand.","exampleCN":"新分店的开业恰逢需求激增。","why":"When an outcome falls on the exact point a plan aimed at, we say the two coincide. Here chance and fit merge: the event lands where it was needed.","whyCN":"当结果正好落在计划瞄准的那一点，我们说二者重合。此处偶然与契合合并：事件落在正需要它的地方。"},{"no":"09","title":"Astrology: planets falling into one house","titleCN":"星象同宫：行星落进同一个位置","definition":"in medieval astrology, of two planets, to occupy the same degree of the zodiac","definitionCN":"在中世纪占星术中，（两颗行星）占据黄道同一度数","example":"Medieval tables noted when Saturn and Jupiter coincided.","exampleCN":"中世纪的星表会记下土星与木星何时同宫。","why":"Medieval Latin coincidere was an astrological term for planets 'falling upon together' in one degree. The modern word kept the geometry and dropped the stars.","whyCN":"中世纪拉丁语 coincidere 是占星术语，指行星“一起落到”同一度数。现代词保留了这层几何，丢掉了星辰。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Coincide is built from 'together' and 'to fall'. Its whole history is one picture: two things falling onto the same point, whether that point is a moment, a place, a date or a conclusion.","cn":"coincide 由“一起”和“落下”构成。它的整部历史就是一个画面：两样东西落到同一个点上，无论这个点是时刻、地点、日期还是结论。"},"items":[{"era":"MEDIEVAL LATIN","en":"Coincidere meant literally 'to fall upon together'. It was used in astrology for planets occupying the same degree of the zodiac.","cn":"coincidere 字面意为“一起落到……上”。它在中世纪占星术中指行星占据黄道同一度数。"},{"era":"1640s ENGLISH","en":"The Latin verb coincidere was used in English writing from the 1640s, still close to its 'fall together' image.","cn":"拉丁动词 coincidere 从 1640 年代起在英语写作中使用，仍贴近“一起落下”的意象。"},{"era":"1705 ENGLISH","en":"The English verb is recorded in 1705 as 'be identical in substance or nature', the sense in which two accounts or natures cannot be told apart.","cn":"英语动词记录于 1705 年，意为“在实质或性质上完全相同”，即两份叙述或两种性质无法分辨。"},{"era":"1715 ENGLISH","en":"By 1715 it meant 'occupy the same space, agree in position', restoring the literal geometry of two bodies at one point.","cn":"到 1715 年，它表示“占据同一空间、位置相符”，恢复了两物在同一地点的字面几何。"},{"era":"1809 ENGLISH","en":"The everyday modern sense 'occur at the same time' is recorded from 1809, extending the same point from space to the clock.","cn":"日常现代义“同时发生”记录于 1809 年，把同一个“点”从空间延伸到时钟。"},{"era":"PROTO-INDO-EUROPEAN","en":"Cadere 'to fall' is traced to PIE *kad- 'to fall', also behind accident, incident, occasion and cadence. The reconstructed root has no written record, so the deepest step is source uncertain.","cn":"cadere“落下”被追溯到原始印欧语 *kad-“落下”，accident、incident、occasion、cadence 也出自这里。该重构词根没有书面记录，故最深层来源不确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"coincidence","ipa":"/kəʊˈɪnsɪdəns/","tag":"derived noun","definition":"a surprising happening of two events at once, or the state of occupying the same position. It is the noun of coincide.","definitionCN":"巧合；同时发生；重合。它是 coincide 的名词。"},{"word":"incident","ipa":"/ˈɪnsɪdənt/","tag":"same root","definition":"an event, often an unpleasant one. It comes from the same cadere 'to fall', literally 'a thing that falls upon one'.","definitionCN":"事件，常指不愉快的事。它同出 cadere“落下”，字面是“落到某人身上的事”。"},{"word":"incidence","ipa":"/ˈɪnsɪdəns/","tag":"same root","definition":"the rate at which something occurs. It shares the -cid- root but means frequency, not overlap.","definitionCN":"发生率。它同样有 -cid- 词根，但指频率，不是重合。"},{"word":"decide","ipa":"/dɪˈsaɪd/","tag":"near spelling","definition":"to settle a question or choice. It looks close but comes from de- + caedere 'to cut', not cadere 'to fall'.","definitionCN":"决定。它形近，但来自 de- + caedere“切”，不是 cadere“落”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"concur","ipa":"/kənˈkɜː(r)/","tag":"agreement","definition":"to agree in opinion, or to happen at the same time. It matches both the opinion and time senses.","definitionCN":"同意；同时发生。它同时对应观点义与时间义。"},{"word":"correspond","ipa":"/ˌkɒrɪˈspɒnd/","tag":"match","definition":"to match or be equivalent to something. It stresses a correspondence between two sets, not a landing on one point.","definitionCN":"相符；对应。它强调两个集合之间的对应，而非落到同一点。"},{"word":"overlap","ipa":"/ˌəʊvəˈlæp/","tag":"shared area","definition":"to cover part of the same area or time. It is a partial coincidence, not a complete one.","definitionCN":"部分重叠。它是部分重合，而非完全重合。"},{"word":"match","ipa":"/mætʃ/","tag":"fit","definition":"to be equal or similar to something. It is the everyday word for the 'agree exactly' sense.","definitionCN":"相配；相符。它是“完全一致”一义最日常的说法。"},{"word":"synchronize","ipa":"/ˈsɪŋkrənaɪz/","tag":"timing","definition":"to make two things happen at the same time. It is intentional, whereas coincide is usually not.","definitionCN":"使同步。它是刻意安排的，而 coincide 通常不是。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Latin com- and cadere, the -cid- family, and the derived forms English actually uses.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 com- 与 cadere、-cid- 词族，以及英语实际使用的派生形式。"},"normal":[{"en":"coincide = co- 'together' + in- 'upon' + cadere 'to fall': two things fall onto one spot.","cn":"coincide = co-“一起”+ in-“落在……上”+ cadere“落”：两样东西落到同一个点上。"},{"en":"The same cadere gives accident, incident, occasion and cadence, all built on something falling or happening.","cn":"同一个 cadere 还给出 accident、incident、occasion、cadence，都建立在“落下、发生”上。"},{"en":"In astrology, coincidere meant two planets falling into the same degree; the modern word keeps the geometry and drops the stars.","cn":"在占星术里，coincidere 指两颗行星落到同一度数；现代词保留了这层几何，丢掉了星辰。"},{"en":"A coincidence is simply two paths landing on one point when nobody planned it.","cn":"巧合就是没人安排时，两条路径落到同一个点上。"},{"en":"When two watches agree to the second, their readings coincide; when two people agree on a plan, their minds do.","cn":"两只手表对到同一秒，读数重合；两个人同意一个计划，头脑也重合。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core operation is two independent paths arriving at one point, whether in space, time or thought.","cn":"核心动作是两条独立的路径抵达同一个点，无论在空间、时间还是思想上。"},{"en":"What changes is only the kind of point: a degree of the zodiac, a coordinate, a date, a minute, a conclusion.","cn":"变化的只是“点”的种类：黄道度数、坐标、日期、分钟、结论。"},{"en":"So 'happen together', 'overlap', 'be identical' and 'agree' are one event seen at different scales of precision.","cn":"所以“同时发生、重合、完全相同、意见一致”是同一个事件在不同精度上被看到。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The festival coincides with the end of the school term.","cn":"这个节日恰逢学期结束。"},{"en":"Her interests coincide with those of the research group.","cn":"她的兴趣与研究小组的一致。"},{"en":"The two triangles coincide exactly when folded.","cn":"折叠时这两个三角形完全重合。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音拆分 · 非词源","text":"co（一起）+ in（进来）+ cide（像 side 边）——两条边一起进到同一处 → coincide 重合、同时发生","word":"coincide"},"root":"源自中世纪拉丁语 coincidere“一起落到……上”，由 com-“一起”+ incidere“落到”（in- 上 + cadere 落）构成，核心是“落到同一个点”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of coincide, all traced to one act: falling onto the same point. The point may be a moment, a place, a date, a degree of the sky or a conclusion; in every case two paths meet at one mark.","cn":"coincide 的九个义项都追溯到一个动作：落到同一个点上。这个点可以是时刻、地点、日期、天上的度数或结论；每一次都是两条路径在同一点相遇。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two separate paths landing on one exact point.","cn":"核心意象：两条分开的路径落在同一个精确的点上。"},"chain":["FALL TOGETHER","LAND ON ONE POINT","SHARE ONE SPACE","MEET IN TIME","AGREE IN MIND","KEEP THE SAME POSITION"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S06","en":"TIME MEETS: events fall on one moment, and dates fall into one slot of the calendar.","cn":"时间相遇：事件落到同一个时刻，日期落进日历的同一格。"},{"senses":"S02 · S05","en":"SPACE MEETS: bodies share one location, and geometric figures lie exactly on one another.","cn":"空间相遇：物体共享同一位置，几何图形正好叠在彼此上面。"},{"senses":"S03 · S04","en":"MINDS MEET: two accounts cannot be told apart, and two opinions stand on one point.","cn":"头脑相遇：两份叙述无法分辨，两个意见站在同一个点上。"},{"senses":"S07 · S08","en":"CHANCE AND FIT: paths cross without a planner, or land exactly where a plan needed them.","cn":"偶然与契合：路径在没有安排者时交叉，或正好落在计划需要的地方。"},{"senses":"S09","en":"THE OLD SKY: astrology had two planets falling into one degree, the original technical use.","cn":"古老的天空：占星术中两颗行星落入同一度数，这是最早的技术用法。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Coincide is co- + in- + cadere. Its family shows the prefixes com-/co- and in-, the fall-root cad-, and the noun suffixes -ence and -al.","cn":"coincide 是 co- + in- + cadere。它的词族展示了前缀 com-/co- 与 in-、表“落”的词根 cad-，以及名词后缀 -ence、-al。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin cadere 'to fall' is the root of a large family: incident, accident, occasion, cadence and coincidence. Medieval Latin coincidere joined com- with incidere, literally 'to fall upon together'.","cn":"拉丁语 cadere“落下”是一个大词族的根：incident、accident、occasion、cadence、coincidence。中世纪拉丁语 coincidere 把 com- 与 incidere 结合，字面即“一起落到……上”。"},"items":[{"word":"coincide","structure":"co- (together) + in- (upon) + cadere (fall)","meaning":"to fall on the same point; to agree exactly","meaningCN":"同时发生；重合；一致（co- 一起，in- 在上，cadere 落）","example":"My holiday coincides with hers.","exampleCN":"我的假期和她的重合。"},{"word":"coincidence","structure":"coincide + -ence (noun)","meaning":"a chance happening of two events at once; the state of overlapping","meaningCN":"巧合；同时发生；重合（-ence 构成名词）","example":"By coincidence, we sat next to each other.","exampleCN":"碰巧，我们坐在了一起。"},{"word":"coincident","structure":"coincide + -ent (adjective)","meaning":"happening at the same time or occupying the same position","meaningCN":"同时发生的；重合的（-ent 构成形容词）","example":"The two events were coincident by chance.","exampleCN":"这两个事件偶然同时发生。"},{"word":"coincidental","structure":"coincident + -al (adjective)","meaning":"resulting from chance rather than planning","meaningCN":"巧合的；偶然的（-al 构成形容词）","example":"The similarity is purely coincidental.","exampleCN":"这种相似纯属巧合。"},{"word":"coincidentally","structure":"coincidental + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"by chance; at the same time","meaningCN":"碰巧；巧合地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"Coincidentally, they had both applied for the same job.","exampleCN":"碰巧，他们俩都申请了同一份工作。"},{"word":"incidence","structure":"in- (upon) + cadere (fall) + -ence","meaning":"the rate at which something happens","meaningCN":"发生率；发病率（同根 cadere，-ence 构成名词）","example":"The incidence of the disease has fallen.","exampleCN":"这种病的发病率已经下降。"},{"word":"incident","structure":"in- (upon) + cadere (fall) + -ent","meaning":"an event that falls upon someone; a minor disturbance","meaningCN":"事件；小事故（同根 cadere，-ent 构成名词）","example":"The incident was reported to the police.","exampleCN":"这起事件已向警方报告。"},{"word":"occasion","structure":"ob- (toward) + casus (a falling) + -ion","meaning":"a particular time or event when something happens","meaningCN":"场合；时机（同根 cadere 的分词 casus）","example":"We met on several occasions.","exampleCN":"我们见过好几次面。"},{"word":"accident","structure":"ad- (to) + cadere (fall) + -ent","meaning":"an unintended event, literally something that befalls","meaningCN":"事故；意外（字面为“落到身上的事”）","example":"The accident happened at the crossroads.","exampleCN":"事故发生在十字路口。"},{"word":"cadence","structure":"cadere (to fall) + -ence","meaning":"a rhythm of falling beats, especially in speech or music","meaningCN":"节奏；抑扬顿挫（由“落下的节拍”引申）","example":"She spoke with a gentle cadence.","exampleCN":"她说话带着柔和的节奏。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"coincidere","structure":"com- + incidere","meaning":"to fall upon together; used of planets in astrology","meaningCN":"一起落到……上；占星术中指行星同宫"},{"word":"incidere","structure":"in- + cadere","meaning":"to fall upon, happen","meaningCN":"落到……上；发生"},{"word":"cadere","structure":"Latin","meaning":"to fall, sink, settle down","meaningCN":"落下；下沉"}]}},{"word":"collapse","ipa_uk":"/kəˈlæps/","ipa_us":"/kəˈlæps/","definition_zh":"倒塌；昏倒；崩溃；瓦解；折叠","definition_en":"to fall in or down suddenly through loss of support, and by extension to fail or break down completely","core_image":"抽掉一根支柱，整座结构瞬间向内塌下去","scene":"A firefighter signals from the rubble and shouts: Get back — the wall is about to collapse!","sceneCN":"这里 collapse 是「倒塌」（第 1 个义项：建筑失去支撑而塌下）；句意：退后，墙要塌了！画面里是裂缝的砖墙、扬起的尘土和消防员的手势。","pos":[{"tag":"vi.","zh":"倒塌；昏倒；崩溃"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"使倒塌；使折叠"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"倒塌；崩溃；垮台"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"collapse under the weight","zh":"在重压下塌下"},{"phrase":"collapse from exhaustion","zh":"因精疲力竭而昏倒"},{"phrase":"financial collapse","zh":"金融崩溃"},{"phrase":"talks collapse","zh":"谈判破裂"},{"phrase":"a collapsible chair","zh":"一把折叠椅"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单","form":"collapses"},{"label":"过去式","form":"collapsed"},{"label":"过去分词","form":"collapsed"},{"label":"现在分词","form":"collapsing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"collapsible","pos":"adj.","zh":"可折叠的"},{"word":"collapsibility","pos":"n.","zh":"可折叠性"},{"word":"collapsed","pos":"adj.","zh":"倒塌的；垮掉的"},{"word":"lapse","pos":"n./v.","zh":"失误；流逝；（权利）失效"},{"word":"relapse","pos":"n./v.","zh":"复发；旧病复发"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Structure: a building gives way","titleCN":"倒塌：建筑失去支撑而垮下","definition":"of a building or structure, to fall down suddenly because it has lost support","definitionCN":"（建筑或结构）因失去支撑而突然塌下","example":"The roof collapsed under the weight of the snow.","exampleCN":"屋顶在积雪的重压下塌了。","why":"Latin collabi is com- 'together' + labi 'to slip, fall'. A structure collapses when its parts slip toward one another and fall as one mass.","whyCN":"拉丁语 collabi 是 com-“一起”+ labi“滑、落”。结构倒塌，就是各部件朝彼此滑落，作为一整团落下。"},{"no":"02","title":"Body: a person goes down","titleCN":"昏倒：人撑不住而倒下","definition":"of a person, to fall down suddenly because of illness, injury or exhaustion","definitionCN":"（人）因疾病、受伤或精疲力竭而突然倒下","example":"He collapsed from exhaustion after the marathon.","exampleCN":"马拉松之后他因精疲力竭而昏倒。","why":"The body is a structure held up by its own support. When strength slips away, the frame falls in on itself, exactly as a wall does.","whyCN":"身体是一座靠自身支撑立起的结构。力气一滑走，这副架子就像墙一样向内塌下。"},{"no":"03","title":"Institution: a system loses its footing","titleCN":"崩溃：一套制度失去立足点","definition":"of a company, bank or system, to fail suddenly and completely","definitionCN":"（公司、银行或体系）突然而彻底地失败","example":"The bank collapsed within a week of the bad loans.","exampleCN":"坏账出现后，这家银行一周内就倒闭了。","why":"A business rests on credit, trust and cash flow as a building rests on pillars. Remove one support and the whole arrangement falls together, which is why failure is described as structural.","whyCN":"企业靠信用、信任和现金流支撑，正如建筑靠柱子。抽掉一根支撑，整个安排就一起塌下，所以失败被说成是结构性的。"},{"no":"04","title":"Talks: an agreement comes apart","titleCN":"破裂：谈判谈不下去而散架","definition":"of negotiations or discussions, to break down completely without agreement","definitionCN":"（谈判或讨论）彻底破裂，未达成一致","example":"The peace talks collapsed after two days.","exampleCN":"和平谈判两天后就破裂了。","why":"Negotiation is a temporary structure built from concessions. When one side withdraws a prop, the whole conversation falls in and nothing is left standing.","whyCN":"谈判是用让步搭起的临时结构。一方抽走一根支柱，整场对话就塌下，什么也立不住。"},{"no":"05","title":"Fold: a frame that packs itself down","titleCN":"折叠：把架子收拢压小","definition":"to fold up or be folded into a smaller, compact form","definitionCN":"折叠起来，或能被折成更小的紧凑形态","example":"The table collapses into a flat case you can carry.","exampleCN":"这张桌子能折成一个可手提的扁箱子。","why":"A folding chair does not fall in ruin but falls in by design: its joints let it descend into itself. The same inward movement is put to useful purpose.","whyCN":"折叠椅不是毁坏地塌下，而是按设计塌下：它的关节让它向自身内部收拢。同一个向内动作被派上了用场。"},{"no":"06","title":"Lung: an air sac falls in","titleCN":"肺萎陷：气囊瘪下去","definition":"of a lung, to shrink and fail to inflate, as when air escapes into the chest cavity","definitionCN":"（肺）缩小、无法充气，如空气漏入胸腔时","example":"His left lung collapsed after the accident.","exampleCN":"事故之后他的左肺萎陷了。","why":"The lung is a balloon held open by internal pressure. When pressure fails, the walls fall inward, a medical version of a roof caving in.","whyCN":"肺是靠内部压力撑开的气球。压力一失，壁就向内塌，这是屋顶塌陷的医学版本。"},{"no":"07","title":"Prices: a market drops through the floor","titleCN":"暴跌：市场跌穿地板","definition":"of prices or a market, to fall suddenly and sharply","definitionCN":"（价格或市场）突然大幅下跌","example":"Oil prices collapsed when demand dried up.","exampleCN":"需求枯竭后油价暴跌。","why":"A price is held up by confidence in future demand. When that support gives way, quotes drop vertically, as if the floor had been removed from under them.","whyCN":"价格由对未来需求的信心托着。支撑一失，报价就垂直下落，仿佛脚下的地板被抽走。"},{"no":"08","title":"Regime: a government loses its pillars","titleCN":"垮台：政权失去支柱","definition":"of a government or regime, to fall from power suddenly","definitionCN":"（政府或政权）突然失去权力、垮台","example":"The regime collapsed after weeks of protests.","exampleCN":"数周抗议之后，该政权垮台了。","why":"A regime stands on army, police and legitimacy. When those pillars slip away at once, the state falls together — the political form of the same physical event.","whyCN":"政权靠军队、警察与合法性立着。这些柱子一旦同时滑走，国家就一起塌下——同一个物理事件的政治形态。"},{"no":"09","title":"The event: a collapse in the abstract","titleCN":"崩溃事件：作为名词的那一塌","definition":"a sudden fall or failure of a structure, system, market or person","definitionCN":"结构、体系、市场或人的突然倒塌或失败","example":"The collapse of the bridge cut the town in two.","exampleCN":"大桥垮塌把小镇一分为二。","why":"English turned the verb into a noun in 1792, first for the lungs. The noun names the event itself: not the slipping but the moment when everything has already come down.","whyCN":"英语在 1792 年把动词变成名词，最初指肺。名词命名事件本身：不是“正在滑落”，而是万物已经塌下的那一刻。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Collapse is Latin 'to slip together'. Every sense, from a falling roof to a failing bank to a folding chair, keeps that single movement: parts that lose their support slide inward and come down as one.","cn":"collapse 是拉丁语“一起滑落”。从塌下的屋顶到倒闭的银行再到折叠椅，每个义项都保留同一个动作：失去支撑的部件向内滑动，作为一体落下。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN","en":"Collabi meant 'to fall together', from com- 'together' plus labi 'to slip, glide, fall'. Its past participle was collapsus.","cn":"collabi 意为“一起落下”，由 com-“一起”加 labi“滑、溜、落”构成，过去分词是 collapsus。"},{"era":"1732 ENGLISH","en":"The English verb is recorded in 1732 as 'fall together, fall into an irregular mass through loss of support or rigidity'.","cn":"英语动词记录于 1732 年，意为“一起落下，因失去支撑或刚性而塌成一团不规则的东西”。"},{"era":"1792 ENGLISH","en":"The noun appears in 1792 as 'a falling in or together', first used of the lungs. The mental sense follows in 1801.","cn":"名词出现于 1792 年，意为“向内塌下、一起塌下”，最初用于肺。精神层面的用法紧随其后，见于 1801 年。"},{"era":"1801 ENGLISH","en":"The figurative sense 'come to nothing, fail' is recorded from 1801, and 'physical prostration' from 1808.","cn":"比喻义“归于失败、垮掉”记录于 1801 年，“身体虚脱”记录于 1808 年。"},{"era":"1856–1883","en":"By 1856 the noun was used of institutions in 'sudden or complete failure'. The transitive 'cause to collapse' is recorded from 1883.","cn":"到 1856 年，名词已用于机构“突然或彻底的失败”。及物义“使倒塌”记录于 1883 年。"},{"era":"ORIGIN UNCERTAIN","en":"Labi 'to slip, fall' is itself of unknown etymology; no reliable earlier root has been established. The deepest step is therefore source uncertain.","cn":"labi“滑、落”本身词源不明，没有可靠的更早词根被确立。因此最深层来源不确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The first group is chosen for spelling, the second for meaning, so that form and sense stay separate.","cn":"第一组按拼写挑选，第二组按词义挑选，这样词形和词义不会混在一起。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"collapsible","ipa":"/kəˈlæpsəbl/","tag":"derived adjective","definition":"able to be folded into a smaller shape. It is collapse + -ible, and belongs to the folding sense.","definitionCN":"可折叠的。它是 collapse 加 -ible，属于折叠义。"},{"word":"lapse","ipa":"/læps/","tag":"same root","definition":"a small mistake, or a gradual passing of time. It comes from the same labi 'to slip'.","definitionCN":"小失误；时间的流逝。它同出 labi“滑”。"},{"word":"relapse","ipa":"/rɪˈlæps/","tag":"same root","definition":"to fall back into illness or a bad state. It is re- 'back' plus labi 'to slip'.","definitionCN":"旧病复发；故态复萌。它是 re-“回”加 labi“滑”。"},{"word":"elapse","ipa":"/ɪˈlæps/","tag":"same root","definition":"of time, to pass by. It shares labi but has no sense of falling down.","definitionCN":"（时间）流逝。它同出 labi，但没有“塌下”的意思。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"fall","ipa":"/fɔːl/","tag":"general","definition":"to move downward, often by gravity. It is the plain word behind every physical sense of collapse.","definitionCN":"落下；跌倒。它是 collapse 一切物理义背后最普通的词。"},{"word":"crash","ipa":"/kræʃ/","tag":"impact","definition":"to hit something violently and noisily, or to fail suddenly. It adds sound and impact to the fall.","definitionCN":"猛烈撞击；突然失败。它给“落下”加上了声音与冲击。"},{"word":"fail","ipa":"/feɪl/","tag":"breakdown","definition":"to stop working or not succeed. It is the general word for the institutional and abstract senses.","definitionCN":"失败；失灵。它是制度义与抽象义的通用词。"},{"word":"cave in","ipa":"/ˌkeɪv ˈɪn/","tag":"structure","definition":"of a roof or ground, to fall inward. It is the closest phrase to the literal structural sense.","definitionCN":"（屋顶或地面）塌陷。它最贴近字面的结构义。"},{"word":"give way","ipa":"/ˌɡɪv ˈweɪ/","tag":"support fails","definition":"to break or yield under pressure. It names the moment support stops holding.","definitionCN":"支撑不住；让步。它命名支撑停止承托的那一刻。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"These links are real: Latin com- and labi, the lapse family, and the derived forms English actually uses.","cn":"这些联想都是真实的：拉丁语 com- 与 labi、lapse 词族，以及英语实际使用的派生形式。"},"normal":[{"en":"collapse = co- 'together' + labi 'to slip': the parts slip toward one another and come down as one.","cn":"collapse = co-“一起”+ labi“滑”：各部件朝彼此滑去，一起落下。"},{"en":"The same labi gives lapse, relapse, elapse and prolapse: everything that slips or falls out of place.","cn":"同一个 labi 还给出 lapse、relapse、elapse、prolapse：都是滑走或掉落原位的东西。"},{"en":"A collapsible chair is designed to fall in on itself, so the ruin-image becomes a convenience.","cn":"折叠椅被设计成向自身内部塌下，于是“废墟”的意象变成了便利。"},{"en":"A lung collapses like a balloon whose air has escaped; a bank collapses like a building whose credit has gone.","cn":"肺萎陷像漏了气的气球；银行倒闭像失了信用的建筑。"},{"en":"The noun a collapse names the finished event, first recorded for the lungs in 1792.","cn":"名词 a collapse 命名完成的事件，1792 年最先用于肺。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"The core operation is loss of support: remove one prop and the parts slide inward instead of standing apart.","cn":"核心动作是失去支撑：抽走一根支柱，各部件便向内滑落，不再分开立着。"},{"en":"The structure changes material all the way up: stone, body, credit, concession, lung, price, legitimacy.","cn":"结构一路更换材质：石头、身体、信用、让步、肺、价格、合法性。"},{"en":"So 'cave in', 'faint', 'go bankrupt', 'break down', 'fold up' and 'plummet' are one physical story told in different materials.","cn":"所以“塌陷、昏倒、破产、破裂、折起、暴跌”是同一个物理故事用不同材质讲述。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Several buildings collapsed during the earthquake.","cn":"地震中有几栋建筑倒塌了。"},{"en":"She collapsed at work and was taken to hospital.","cn":"她在工作时昏倒，被送进了医院。"},{"en":"The deal collapsed when the two sides failed to agree on a price.","cn":"由于双方未能就价格达成一致，交易告吹了。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音拆分 · 非词源","text":"co（一起）+ lapse（滑落）——所有东西一起滑落，整栋楼就塌了 → collapse 倒塌、崩溃","word":"collapse"},"root":"源自拉丁语 collabi“一起滑落”，由 com-“一起”+ labi“滑、落”构成，过去分词 collapsus，核心是“失去支撑，部件向内塌下”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of collapse, all traced to one movement: parts that lose their support slip inward and come down together. Stone, bodies, banks, talks, chairs, lungs, prices and governments all fall by the same geometry.","cn":"collapse 的九个义项都追溯到一个动作：失去支撑的部件向内滑落、一起塌下。石头、身体、银行、谈判、椅子、肺、价格与政府，都按同一套几何倒下。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a structure whose support is gone falls inward into one mass.","cn":"核心意象：失去支撑的结构向内塌成一团。"},"chain":["SLIP TOGETHER","LOSE SUPPORT","FALL INWARD","BREAK DOWN","FAIL COMPLETELY","PACK DOWN"],"branches":[{"senses":"S01 · S06","en":"PHYSICAL FRAMES FAIL: a roof falls under weight, and a lung falls in when its air pressure is lost.","cn":"物理框架失效：屋顶在重压下塌落，肺在气压丧失时瘪下。"},{"senses":"S02 · S07","en":"THE BODY AND THE MARKET DROP: strength leaves a person, and confidence leaves a price.","cn":"身体与市场下坠：力气离开人，信心离开价格。"},{"senses":"S03 · S08","en":"STRUCTURES OF POWER FAIL: a bank loses its credit pillars, and a regime loses its legitimacy.","cn":"权力结构失效：银行失去信用支柱，政权失去合法性。"},{"senses":"S04","en":"A BUILT CONVERSATION FALLS: negotiation is a frame of concessions, and it comes apart when a side withdraws.","cn":"搭起的对话塌下：谈判是由让步构成的框架，一方抽走就散架。"},{"senses":"S05 · S09","en":"THE SAME MOTION, KEPT AND NAMED: a chair folds by design, and the noun names the finished fall.","cn":"同一个动作的利用与命名：椅子按设计折起，名词命名完成的那一塌。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Collapse is co- + labi. Its family shows the prefixes com-/co-, re- and pro-, the slip-root lab-, and the adjective suffix -ible.","cn":"collapse 是 co- + labi。它的词族展示了前缀 com-/co-、re-、pro-，表“滑”的词根 lab-，以及形容词后缀 -ible。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Latin labi 'to slip, fall' yields collapse, lapse, relapse, elapse and prolapse. Its participle lapsus is the source of the noun lapse, literally 'a slipping'.","cn":"拉丁语 labi“滑、落”给出 collapse、lapse、relapse、elapse、prolapse。它的分词 lapsus 是名词 lapse 的来源，字面即“一次滑落”。"},"items":[{"word":"collapse","structure":"co- (together) + labi (slip, fall)","meaning":"to fall in suddenly; to fail completely; to fold up","meaningCN":"倒塌；崩溃；折叠（co- 一起，labi 滑落）","example":"The old bridge collapsed in the flood.","exampleCN":"那座旧桥在洪水中垮塌了。"},{"word":"collapsible","structure":"collapse + -ible (able to be)","meaning":"able to be folded into a smaller form","meaningCN":"可折叠的（-ible 表能够被……）","example":"We packed the collapsible table in the car.","exampleCN":"我们把折叠桌塞进了车里。"},{"word":"collapsibility","structure":"collapsible + -ity (quality)","meaning":"the quality of being foldable or liable to fall in","meaningCN":"可折叠性；易塌性（-ity 构成名词）","example":"The test measures the collapsibility of the soil.","exampleCN":"这项测试测量土壤的塌陷性。"},{"word":"collapsed","structure":"collapse + -ed (past participle or adjective)","meaning":"fallen down; in a state of ruin","meaningCN":"倒塌的；垮掉的（-ed 构成分词或形容词）","example":"Rescuers searched the collapsed building.","exampleCN":"救援人员在倒塌的建筑中搜寻。"},{"word":"collapsing","structure":"collapse + -ing (present participle)","meaning":"in the act of falling in or failing","meaningCN":"正在倒塌的；正在崩溃的（-ing 构成现在分词）","example":"They ran from the collapsing wall.","exampleCN":"他们从正在倒塌的墙边跑开。"},{"word":"lapse","structure":"labi (slip) + -se, or Latin lapsus","meaning":"a slip in memory or conduct; a passing of time","meaningCN":"失误；（时间）流逝；失效（来自 lapsus 一次滑落）","example":"It was a lapse of judgment, not a crime.","exampleCN":"那是判断失误，不是犯罪。"},{"word":"relapse","structure":"re- (back) + labi (slip)","meaning":"to slip back into illness or a former bad state","meaningCN":"旧病复发；故态复萌（re- 表回）","example":"She relapsed two months after treatment.","exampleCN":"治疗两个月后她旧病复发了。"},{"word":"elapse","structure":"e- (out) + labi (slip)","meaning":"of time, to slip away or pass","meaningCN":"（时间）流逝（e- 表出去）","example":"Ten years elapsed before they met again.","exampleCN":"十年过去他们才再次相见。"},{"word":"prolapse","structure":"pro- (forward) + labi (slip)","meaning":"of an organ, to slip forward out of place","meaningCN":"（器官）脱垂；脱出（pro- 表向前）","example":"The condition can cause a prolapse of the uterus.","exampleCN":"这种状况可能导致子宫脱垂。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"collabi","structure":"com- + labi","meaning":"to fall together, collapse","meaningCN":"一起落下；倒塌"},{"word":"labi","structure":"Latin","meaning":"to slip, glide, fall; of unknown etymology","meaningCN":"滑；溜；落（词源不明）"},{"word":"collapsus","structure":"past participle of collabi","meaning":"fallen together","meaningCN":"一起塌下的"}]}}]);
